python/pull/389\">aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python#389</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/compare/v1.6.0...v1.6.1\">https://github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/compare/v1.6.0...v1.6.1</a></p>\n<h2>Bedrock AgentCore SDK v1.6.0</h2>\n<h2>Installation</h2>\n<pre lang=\"bash\"><code>pip install bedrock-agentcore==1.6.0\n</code></pre>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<p>See <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/blob/v1.6.0/CHANGELOG.md\">CHANGELOG.md</a>\nfor details.</p>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>feat: add custom code-based evaluator decorator and typed models by\n<a href=\"https://github.com/jariy17\"><code>@​jariy17</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/pull/383\">aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python#383</a></li>\n<li>Release v1.6.0 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/github-actions\"><code>@​github-actions</code></a>[bot]\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/pull/385\">aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python#385</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/compare/v1.5.1...v1.6.0\">https://github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/compare/v1.5.1...v1.6.0</a></p>\n<h2>Bedrock AgentCore SDK v1.5.1</h2>\n<h2>Installation</h2>\n<pre lang=\"bash\"><code>pip install bedrock-agentcore==1.5.1\n</code></pre>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<p>See <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/blob/v1.5.1/CHANGELOG.md\">CHANGELOG.md</a>\nfor details.</p>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">bedrock-agentcore's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>[1.6.1] - 2026-04-10</h2>\n<h3>Added</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>feat: add read_only flag to AgentCoreMemorySessionManager to disable\nACM persistence (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/issues/389\">#389</a>)\n(215b5bd)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Fixed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>fix: replace blocklist with allowlist for install_packages() package\nvalidation (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/issues/403\">#403</a>)\n(ed953b5)</li>\n<li>fix: skip integration tests for Dependabot and remove missing label\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/issues/382\">#382</a>)\n(4ebfdcb)</li>\n<li>fix: pin griffe version and fix ExplanationStyle attribute error (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/issues/381\">#381</a>)\n(2bdb9f1)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Other Changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>chore(deps): bump boto3 and botocore minimum to 1.42.86 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/issues/399\">#399</a>)\n(df9a21d)</li>\n<li>fix(ci): add pytest-rerunfailures to integration test dependencies\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/issues/400\">#400</a>)\n(5ccb283)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>[1.6.0] - 2026-03-31</h2>\n<h3>Added</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>feat: add custom code-based evaluator decorator and typed models (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/issues/383\">#383</a>)\n(09f45f3)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>[1.5.1] - 2026-03-31</h2>\n<h3>Other Changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Revert &quot;feat: Emit OTEL attributes for AgentCore Evaluation\nsupport (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/issues/368\">#368</a>)&quot;\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/issues/380\">#380</a>)\n(a516260)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>[1.5.0] - 2026-03-30</h2>\n<h3>Added</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>feat: add ground truth support to EvaluationClient and\nOnDemandEvaluationDatasetRunner (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/issues/376\">#376</a>)\n(29b0115)</li>\n<li>feat: Add certificates to create_code_interpreter() (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/issues/373\">#373</a>)\n(bc95735)</li>\n<li>feat: add support for policies and certificates (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/issues/371\">#371</a>)\n(88c5101)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Other Changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>chore: Modify arn parsing in runtime client to allow for different\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/issues/362\">#362</a>)\n(a10c0fd)</li>\n<li>ci: add breaking change detection workflow for pull requests (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/issues/358\">#358</a>)\n(9341468)</li>\n<li>ci: add backward compatibility integration test workflow (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/issues/357\">#357</a>)\n(50654c1)</li>\n<li>ci: add Dependabot auto-merge workflow (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/issues/361\">#361</a>)\n(38425ec)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>[1.4.8] - 2026-03-26</h2>\n<h3>Added</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>feat: Emit OTEL attributes for AgentCore Evaluation support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/issues/368\">#368</a>)\n(8bae410)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Fixed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>fix: lazy import strands-agents-evals to avoid ImportError when not\ninstalled (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/issues/367\">#367</a>)\n(2c4911d)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Other Changes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>ci: migrate PyPI publishing to OIDC Trusted Publishing (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/issues/363\">#363</a>)\n(5bdf009)</li>\n<li>ci(deps): bump trufflesecurity/trufflehog from 3.93.8 to 3.94.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/issues/360\">#360</a>)\n(cd86ebd)</li>\n<li>ci(deps): bump actions/github-script from 7 to 8 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/issues/359\">#359</a>)\n(64db2f0)</li>\n<li>Skip LTM retrieval when content has no text (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/issues/299\">#299</a>)\n(a49db7d)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/commit/5759f54a4f4babc06bbfee923c75615f0e5f3aea\"><code>5759f54</code></a>\nchore: bump version to 1.6.1 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/issues/404\">#404</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/commit/ed953b58a96bd6d5ed1ca67792f6888cf04edf26\"><code>ed953b5</code></a>\nfix: replace blocklist with allowlist for install_packages() package\nvalidati...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/commit/df9a21d1cab0e232bf27ebe8f4a859bbeddd032a\"><code>df9a21d</code></a>\nchore(deps): bump boto3 and botocore minimum to 1.42.86 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/issues/399\">#399</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/commit/5ccb2830e6f3ad000938849977f0ed3dd98e29e1\"><code>5ccb283</code></a>\nfix(ci): add pytest-rerunfailures to integration test dependencies (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/issues/400\">#400</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/commit/215b5bdea345bbcd875b28a8e59d8e17fe4337d0\"><code>215b5bd</code></a>\nfeat: add read_only flag to AgentCoreMemorySessionManager to disable ACM\npers...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/commit/4ebfdcb93442b93f1c3bbb51a4f02dd2b963fe2a\"><code>4ebfdcb</code></a>\nfix: skip integration tests for Dependabot and remove missing label (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/issues/382\">#382</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/commit/2bdb9f1983611c0b8bee83e8c6c1978d98251980\"><code>2bdb9f1</code></a>\nfix: pin griffe version and fix ExplanationStyle attribute error (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/issues/381\">#381</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/commit/7033752952d5c339d2f14ad0c5c66ad8bdf1ae42\"><code>7033752</code></a>\nRelease v1.6.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/issues/385\">#385</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/commit/09f45f3f51a1427f0c72b77b19274b6cff6b49bd\"><code>09f45f3</code></a>\nfeat: add custom code-based evaluator decorator and typed models (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/issues/383\">#383</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/commit/daaa8072ce5b6a4c8a425906c1cd9d2a60506f7a\"><code>daaa807</code></a>\nRelease v1.5.1 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/issues/384\">#384</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/aws/bedrock-agentcore-sdk-python/compare/v1.4.7...v1.6.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=bedrock-agentcore&package-manager=uv&previous-version=1.4.7&new-version=1.6.1)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-22T16:54:00Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f933fbf4a3fb37a88fd05a9ce9821e15a1272842","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f933fbf4a3fb37a88fd05a9ce9821e15a1272842","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f933fbf4a3fb37a88fd05a9ce9821e15a1272842/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0017000834f8f82bdd6ece5f69fdee5b785efe88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0017000834f8f82bdd6ece5f69fdee5b785efe88","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0017000834f8f82bdd6ece5f69fdee5b785efe88"}]},{"sha":"0017000834f8f82bdd6ece5f69fdee5b785efe88","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDAwMTcwMDA4MzRmOGY4MmJkZDZlY2U1ZjY5ZmRlZTViNzg1ZWZlODg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-22T15:28:54Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-22T15:28:54Z"},"message":"docs(code): add dev quickstart and reorder (#4106)\n\nThe `libs/code` development guide jumped straight into specialized\ntopics (Textual CSS devtools, debugging) with no on-ramp for a\ncontributor who just wants to get the package running locally.\n\nThis adds a quickstart section up top, then keeps the existing CSS\ndevtools and debugging guides below. Ordering now flows from what most\ncontributors need first to the more specialized workflows.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4da98c6a-a5d3-6209-003b-f4f3fb734389)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"25911d7223513ff7ec5c73c44cbccf0444e74e48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/25911d7223513ff7ec5c73c44cbccf0444e74e48"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/0017000834f8f82bdd6ece5f69fdee5b785efe88","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOVS2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIhMQABkpqK0XXum0q9VWmT00RwNb\nqqU/ExkETBWf1ClRAikm8OYSAi1KCfE3jZWmVlKKjyMtyZYNDdFVE47kBKFvTEN6\nvZfu6e2zMnJA5z1qsNl3p9zT+0qvarQXrnKzDMZodWHO4Tj8BUFX/CEMIUi52sPe\nZozzv2xrAvmHWpBqLtx5V8Xug/VRGMQqh6+OzR172K2IEYsTdNrrvSc/y/kaXBIu\na6Q7byhILBjZUqo9iQBymJD7HdJFMwcxfi8ALCqLsaGRb84oraWS2gTuAUFtbAbd\n0DSg1+61xS7Vsb9ohTjZ//8c9pxIgq2elcQUCUpiO4iWWjbi9fzB11lcjzZCV8pS\nP+FeYbutWbYfd3ysIHOtwWuCq8acxawChGm+am6j25aETYL/ezn/1Obl+I84Q9H2\nVEpi3/Bc/4MX5jmqJzYJBXxCd+rMjYdE6QsHBYyjsUHrPykDN16v8m+D4VsUKxY2\nIdc81OBMa0zAjEvqhhzObDPxH6ANve3KtyeG20skKYHkHwyTk0R97YGYJfU8Dqp4\n0oPq5paVfp0hM2SmUos9GY+LIKpE4umZEmt6yyl3Ra1q3ymoxnCVXwcAx2sJBBBe\nfaVMACCE1fVVOrLvh+0HdrgHqsSoQLfx0AVZ4QFrIeEUIlLVAKIn9dEQcG0K+LT8\nalfAWPlP4+09JhTTtgVR\n=YruU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 25911d7223513ff7ec5c73c44cbccf0444e74e48\nparent df8db8af6a7cbfc2ab535020b951d73759da73dd\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1782142134 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782142134 -0400\n\ndocs(code): add dev quickstart and reorder (#4106)\n\nThe `libs/code` development guide jumped straight into specialized\ntopics (Textual CSS devtools, debugging) with no on-ramp for a\ncontributor who just wants to get the package running locally.\n\nThis adds a quickstart section up top, then keeps the existing CSS\ndevtools and debugging guides below. Ordering now flows from what most\ncontributors need first to the more specialized workflows.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4da98c6a-a5d3-6209-003b-f4f3fb734389)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-22T15:28:55Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0017000834f8f82bdd6ece5f69fdee5b785efe88","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0017000834f8f82bdd6ece5f69fdee5b785efe88","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0017000834f8f82bdd6ece5f69fdee5b785efe88/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"df8db8af6a7cbfc2ab535020b951d73759da73dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/df8db8af6a7cbfc2ab535020b951d73759da73dd","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/df8db8af6a7cbfc2ab535020b951d73759da73dd"}]},{"sha":"df8db8af6a7cbfc2ab535020b951d73759da73dd","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGRmOGRiOGFmNmE3Y2JmYzJhYjUzNTAyMGI5NTFkNzM3NTlkYTczZGQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-20T23:56:29Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-20T23:56:29Z"},"message":"feat(code): confirm \"Launched\" after auto-update restart (#4098)\n\nThe startup auto-update now updates its `Launching...` line to\n`Launched.` once the upgraded version is running.\n\n---\n\nDuring a startup auto-update, `Updated to v{latest}. Launching...` is\nprinted immediately before `os.execv` replaces the process, so the\nprinting generation can never resolve its own status line. The re-exec'd\nprocess already detects the post-update restart by consuming the\n`RESTARTED_AFTER_UPDATE` sentinel; once `is_installed_version_at_least`\nconfirms the upgrade actually took effect, it now rewrites that line in\nplace to `Updated to v{latest}. Launched.`.\n\nThe new `_confirm_launch_after_restart` helper performs the rewrite with\na Rich `Control` cursor-up + erase-line sequence, and is gated on\n`console.is_terminal` so redirected (non-terminal) output is never\npolluted with escape codes. A failed re-exec that did not change the\nrunning version is correctly left as `Launching...`.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/27a04727-aae3-d6e0-61ef-358ae09e8d92)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"ffc08404e01040fcb044d2921a57d2534cfe58e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/ffc08404e01040fcb044d2921a57d2534cfe58e8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/df8db8af6a7cbfc2ab535020b951d73759da73dd","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNyitCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMWQQAF8OrR9ShKRqr2VuyVJfHTyW\nSTCpv157vjZBrfXQTRFZXIWAGpUbNMEVr36ECumBwqDsevx/EuDNvcas6i7lDJpR\nZfA8hLHyOkZjc9m1THO0sgxRn03qjGef825sFNPGY5R0yqDwUSHz/8EQTNKO5Oub\ndKtFIqDOtg7Bx6ODs+GHPcbBI8ehM17YLqoE/P8Dx6f+5bJZ/ximCTRPpQBuQW2q\nHWvVQzyxYkNCAw3zF3UJB6enWDzvcapTVwHYXUKbe6OIDwBfMc4bfkVIkkrdAjQr\n0RGvTf2dwbrpa0OX/OhdwdF8m07OonBMQlsYF1cxM8uu01svB6OmZv6jsTRe14ww\nPXiG0EEZlUOHJ6tKqP71a59EF/Cbmsf1UlCY65rPJ0++tLifPe4MBELqDjHENhbP\n5qR+Cxql8hmd9EvImiwK38QybX+JQrpvtq3fwLOuF0eQ4XA9D5GYQZ8V5xmfdMdx\ns0+RsAf1CtEJk4g3yrKLtvS7ZLtUqi6kgEzsrzm7o7e0mfOmky/nR7IF1stnyRv/\nbJrRp8vmXgt7mCtNr0aP1a6z1Wn2qXbSjrCGUqYpsUJ7CT9prWxsOxb7OKNuIDZZ\nKUwLntthi8GMhcsY4FrMeloLjfZqQMQjH7837swNDTyIIOxfKvDKrri61nEeQORg\nc9+6S3iDlm/owWwvaj7u\n=RH71\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ffc08404e01040fcb044d2921a57d2534cfe58e8\nparent ae1de8b0766c69f6eac0c3cb919c6aac7d9e136c\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781999789 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781999789 -0400\n\nfeat(code): confirm \"Launched\" after auto-update restart (#4098)\n\nThe startup auto-update now updates its `Launching...` line to\n`Launched.` once the upgraded version is running.\n\n---\n\nDuring a startup auto-update, `Updated to v{latest}. Launching...` is\nprinted immediately before `os.execv` replaces the process, so the\nprinting generation can never resolve its own status line. The re-exec'd\nprocess already detects the post-update restart by consuming the\n`RESTARTED_AFTER_UPDATE` sentinel; once `is_installed_version_at_least`\nconfirms the upgrade actually took effect, it now rewrites that line in\nplace to `Updated to v{latest}. Launched.`.\n\nThe new `_confirm_launch_after_restart` helper performs the rewrite with\na Rich `Control` cursor-up + erase-line sequence, and is gated on\n`console.is_terminal` so redirected (non-terminal) output is never\npolluted with escape codes. A failed re-exec that did not change the\nrunning version is correctly left as `Launching...`.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/27a04727-aae3-d6e0-61ef-358ae09e8d92)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-20T23:56:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/df8db8af6a7cbfc2ab535020b951d73759da73dd","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/df8db8af6a7cbfc2ab535020b951d73759da73dd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/df8db8af6a7cbfc2ab535020b951d73759da73dd/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url