gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2d6fb53cd8c94680a42fa9d7041509ff78050616","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2d6fb53cd8c94680a42fa9d7041509ff78050616","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2d6fb53cd8c94680a42fa9d7041509ff78050616"}]},{"sha":"2d6fb53cd8c94680a42fa9d7041509ff78050616","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDJkNmZiNTNjZDhjOTQ2ODBhNDJmYTlkNzA0MTUwOWZmNzgwNTA2MTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nishitha M","email":"32355027+imnishitha@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-18T22:24:09Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-18T22:24:09Z"},"message":"fix(sdk): preserve media references in summarization archives (#3990)\n\nFixes #[2873](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/2873)\n\n---\n\n## User story\n\nAs a user whose conversation history includes messages with media, I\nexpect that content to remain recoverable when `SummarizationMiddleware`\noffloads older messages during compaction.\n\n---\n\nWhen a thread grows past the summarization threshold,\n`SummarizationMiddleware` keeps the conversation small by moving older\nmessages out of the active context. It first saves those older messages\nto `/conversation_history/{thread_id}.md`, then replaces them in the\nactive conversation with a concise summary and a pointer to the saved\nfile. See the [summarization\ndocs](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/deepagents/context-engineering#summarization)\nfor background on this flow. Crucially, when messages are offloaded to\ndisk, they should preserve all content originally present.\n\nPreviously, the offload step relied on LangChain's default message\nrendering (via `get_buffer_string()`), which only preserved text\ncontent. Non-text content blocks were silently dropped from the saved\nhistory file. The issue surfaced with images, but the underlying problem\nwas broader: URL-based media references could be omitted, and base64\nmedia had no durable reference once the original messages were compacted\naway.\n\n---\n\n`SummarizationMiddleware` now preserves media references during offload.\nFor media that already has a URL, the offload step now writes the\nmessage in `get_buffer_string()`'s XML format, which keeps the media\nreference in the saved history file.\n\nFor base64 image content, `SummarizationMiddleware` first writes the\nimage bytes to the backend alongside the saved conversation history,\nunder `/conversation_history/media/{content_hash}.{ext}`. It then\nrewrites the original base64 content block into a normal image reference\npointing at that stored file. For example, a block containing inline\nbase64 image data becomes a reference like:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"image\",\n  \"url\": \"/conversation_history/media/{content_hash}.png\"\n}\n```\n\nWhen the message is written to the saved history file, that reference is\npreserved in the XML-rendered output rather than embedding the raw\nbase64 payload.\n\nThe helper handles all three base64 shapes recognized by langchain_core:\n\n- Explicit base64 field: {\"type\": \"image\", \"base64\": \"...\", \"mime_type\":\n\"...\"}\n    - Top-level data: URL: {\"image/png;base64,...\"}\n- OpenAI-style image_url: {\"type\": \"image_url\", \"image_url\": {\"url\":\n\"data:...\"}}\n\nIf storing one of those files fails, the saved history file includes an\nexplicit failed-offload marker for that block instead of making it look\nlike the media was never there:\n\n```xml\n<image error=\"failed_to_offload\" />\n```\n\nThe difference is that this file now keeps durable references for media\ncontent instead of preserving only the surrounding text.\n\n---\n\n## Dependency note\n\nThis PR should land with a Deep Agents LangChain dependency bump to a\nversion that includes\n[langchain-ai/langchain#38171](https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchain/pull/38171).\nThat upstream change switches `SummarizationMiddleware` summary-input\nserialization to XML so URL-backed media survives the summarization\nprompt, matching the archive-preservation behavior here.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Nishitha M <32355027+imnishitha@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","tree":{"sha":"db5b8d301e2df5d9f452d0f38d22595e1b85a049","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/db5b8d301e2df5d9f452d0f38d22595e1b85a049"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/2d6fb53cd8c94680a42fa9d7041509ff78050616","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNHAJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2KUQAE9DykcbstGQwK2Zuwe17Si9\nUxek5fdoZuiSBqHTQQxsEzINqulVk9rOXm0uyRCNbGit5UP/Lc8omMtPdr3gsG3b\nDFojdKUEbc9yZrhGVssTbmC85rB5mykRlGpPVv5OXdiX8UDiw6rg65MoUZCOKLTz\ncfexwqnb6UJd6t+nLzdLGESGlcZZEwR6saOrfzjhhepDKFybX6SNtNXP06F/SlHk\nJGDgeAQeu3B0RWQczjn1AV3/nPXiTgCCdnS6wV8d1EFKmKgPpyu+ftkQu+pLPQTz\nM7Y9GwI3A3QMStBkjUwdY/q/r8ZWrpGV6ADjACByuo67u2T23BBCHbrcg/3TQ3ED\nD9Yco2zn4JCLPXAG0jqS60c3eQTMBOhQKeDDDlgv7hjX6jCtmX5gFrJr5ymH+SwT\n6tph59wfRaTOHdC+/FQYtftCxhGn7/rw6hPlGb7GXVkIpy7qa4PVgfMZVlBnBnX9\nSv7LC3HqGwcBIoL8ys6XIzvEG0rnUznd4yTwttTLlWvdLf3ujUtAKU3gW28wvkJd\nNULcVfaGvjr2lBPayaDC9ljpTE5ALrb0SYhnZ5myTKdNLmn4l5xhI64cVelxAYZw\nub/a1HaykO/N25RcsL2pkZxQpyIC39hhnl2u8NJajqHqkOeCEtejfEl3+c/AOYxe\nPYPhRPSL6KM/dB3wyOvG\n=lBgg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree db5b8d301e2df5d9f452d0f38d22595e1b85a049\nparent 20507f9370bbc1bc91f04a9ffe60c25af61e1aa4\nauthor Nishitha M <32355027+imnishitha@users.noreply.github.com> 1781821449 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781821449 -0400\n\nfix(sdk): preserve media references in summarization archives (#3990)\n\nFixes #[2873](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/2873)\n\n---\n\n## User story\n\nAs a user whose conversation history includes messages with media, I\nexpect that content to remain recoverable when `SummarizationMiddleware`\noffloads older messages during compaction.\n\n---\n\nWhen a thread grows past the summarization threshold,\n`SummarizationMiddleware` keeps the conversation small by moving older\nmessages out of the active context. It first saves those older messages\nto `/conversation_history/{thread_id}.md`, then replaces them in the\nactive conversation with a concise summary and a pointer to the saved\nfile. See the [summarization\ndocs](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/deepagents/context-engineering#summarization)\nfor background on this flow. Crucially, when messages are offloaded to\ndisk, they should preserve all content originally present.\n\nPreviously, the offload step relied on LangChain's default message\nrendering (via `get_buffer_string()`), which only preserved text\ncontent. Non-text content blocks were silently dropped from the saved\nhistory file. The issue surfaced with images, but the underlying problem\nwas broader: URL-based media references could be omitted, and base64\nmedia had no durable reference once the original messages were compacted\naway.\n\n---\n\n`SummarizationMiddleware` now preserves media references during offload.\nFor media that already has a URL, the offload step now writes the\nmessage in `get_buffer_string()`'s XML format, which keeps the media\nreference in the saved history file.\n\nFor base64 image content, `SummarizationMiddleware` first writes the\nimage bytes to the backend alongside the saved conversation history,\nunder `/conversation_history/media/{content_hash}.{ext}`. It then\nrewrites the original base64 content block into a normal image reference\npointing at that stored file. For example, a block containing inline\nbase64 image data becomes a reference like:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"image\",\n  \"url\": \"/conversation_history/media/{content_hash}.png\"\n}\n```\n\nWhen the message is written to the saved history file, that reference is\npreserved in the XML-rendered output rather than embedding the raw\nbase64 payload.\n\nThe helper handles all three base64 shapes recognized by langchain_core:\n\n- Explicit base64 field: {\"type\": \"image\", \"base64\": \"...\", \"mime_type\":\n\"...\"}\n    - Top-level data: URL: {\"image/png;base64,...\"}\n- OpenAI-style image_url: {\"type\": \"image_url\", \"image_url\": {\"url\":\n\"data:...\"}}\n\nIf storing one of those files fails, the saved history file includes an\nexplicit failed-offload marker for that block instead of making it look\nlike the media was never there:\n\n```xml\n<image error=\"failed_to_offload\" />\n```\n\nThe difference is that this file now keeps durable references for media\ncontent instead of preserving only the surrounding text.\n\n---\n\n## Dependency note\n\nThis PR should land with a Deep Agents LangChain dependency bump to a\nversion that includes\n[langchain-ai/langchain#38171](https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchain/pull/38171).\nThat upstream change switches `SummarizationMiddleware` summary-input\nserialization to XML so URL-backed media survives the summarization\nprompt, matching the archive-preservation behavior here.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Nishitha M <32355027+imnishitha@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","verified_at":"2026-06-18T22:24:10Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2d6fb53cd8c94680a42fa9d7041509ff78050616","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2d6fb53cd8c94680a42fa9d7041509ff78050616","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2d6fb53cd8c94680a42fa9d7041509ff78050616/comments","author":{"login":"imnishitha","id":32355027,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzU1MDI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32355027?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha","html_url":"https://github.com/imnishitha","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/imnishitha/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"20507f9370bbc1bc91f04a9ffe60c25af61e1aa4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/20507f9370bbc1bc91f04a9ffe60c25af61e1aa4","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/20507f9370bbc1bc91f04a9ffe60c25af61e1aa4"}]},{"sha":"20507f9370bbc1bc91f04a9ffe60c25af61e1aa4","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDIwNTA3ZjkzNzBiYmMxYmM5MWYwNGE5ZmZlNjBjMjVhZjYxZTFhYTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-18T21:51:08Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-18T21:51:08Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump jupyter-server from 2.18.0 to 2.20.0 in /examples/deep_research (#4082)\n\nBumps [jupyter-server](https://github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server)\nfrom 2.18.0 to 2.20.0.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/releases\">jupyter-server's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v2.20.0</h2>\n<h2>2.20.0</h2>\n<p>(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/compare/v2.19.0...333e700119ee0bcc0b5fcd4c158213d7c275c778\">Full\nChangelog</a>)</p>\n<h3>Security fixes</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>CVE-2026-44727 <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/security/advisories/GHSA-fcw5-x6j4-ccmp\">GHSA-fcw5-x6j4-ccmp</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Enhancements made</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix confusing terminal output when using ServerApp.ip=0.0.0.0 <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/pull/1643\">#1643</a>\n(<a href=\"https://github.com/Yann-P\"><code>@​Yann-P</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/minrk\"><code>@​minrk</code></a>)</li>\n<li>Add a toggle to enable curve encryption for all kernels that support\nit <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/pull/1638\">#1638</a>\n(<a href=\"https://github.com/krassowski\"><code>@​krassowski</code></a>,\n<a href=\"https://github.com/Carreau\"><code>@​Carreau</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/ianthomas23\"><code>@​ianthomas23</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/minrk\"><code>@​minrk</code></a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bugs fixed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Grab the port from <code>bind_sockets</code> in case its different\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/pull/1651\">#1651</a>\n(<a href=\"https://github.com/choldgraf\"><code>@​choldgraf</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/krassowski\"><code>@​krassowski</code></a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Maintenance and upkeep improvements</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix <code>test_authorizer</code> having a spurious comma in params\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/pull/1664\">#1664</a>\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/krassowski\"><code>@​krassowski</code></a>)</li>\n<li>Add a reminder to merge GHSA before release <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/pull/1659\">#1659</a>\n(<a href=\"https://github.com/Yann-P\"><code>@​Yann-P</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Carreau\"><code>@​Carreau</code></a>)</li>\n<li>Exclude problematic <code>pywinpty</code> 3.0.4 version <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/pull/1658\">#1658</a>\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/krassowski\"><code>@​krassowski</code></a>)</li>\n<li>ci: explicitly pass base-setup inputs to fix strict validation\nfailures <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/pull/1626\">#1626</a>\n(<a href=\"https://github.com/Carreau\"><code>@​Carreau</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Copilot\"><code>@​Copilot</code></a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation improvements</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Align docs for curve encryption with latest JEP version <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/pull/1660\">#1660</a>\n(<a href=\"https://github.com/krassowski\"><code>@​krassowski</code></a>,\n<a href=\"https://github.com/Carreau\"><code>@​Carreau</code></a>)</li>\n<li>Remove PGP key from docs <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/pull/1653\">#1653</a>\n(<a href=\"https://github.com/Yann-P\"><code>@​Yann-P</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/krassowski\"><code>@​krassowski</code></a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Contributors to this release</h3>\n<p>The following people contributed discussions, new ideas, code and\ndocumentation contributions, and review.\nSee <a\nhref=\"https://github-activity.readthedocs.io/en/latest/use/#how-does-this-tool-define-contributions-in-the-reports\">our\ndefinition of contributors</a>.</p>\n<p>(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/graphs/contributors?from=2026-05-29&amp;to=2026-06-17&amp;type=c\">GitHub\ncontributors page for this release</a>)</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/Carreau\"><code>@​Carreau</code></a> (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Ajupyter-server%2Fjupyter_server+involves%3ACarreau+updated%3A2026-05-29..2026-06-17&amp;type=Issues\">activity</a>)\n| <a href=\"https://github.com/choldgraf\"><code>@​choldgraf</code></a>\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Ajupyter-server%2Fjupyter_server+involves%3Acholdgraf+updated%3A2026-05-29..2026-06-17&amp;type=Issues\">activity</a>)\n| <a href=\"https://github.com/Copilot\"><code>@​Copilot</code></a> (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Ajupyter-server%2Fjupyter_server+involves%3ACopilot+updated%3A2026-05-29..2026-06-17&amp;type=Issues\">activity</a>)\n| <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/ianthomas23\"><code>@​ianthomas23</code></a> (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Ajupyter-server%2Fjupyter_server+involves%3Aianthomas23+updated%3A2026-05-29..2026-06-17&amp;type=Issues\">activity</a>)\n| <a href=\"https://github.com/krassowski\"><code>@​krassowski</code></a>\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Ajupyter-server%2Fjupyter_server+involves%3Akrassowski+updated%3A2026-05-29..2026-06-17&amp;type=Issues\">activity</a>)\n| <a href=\"https://github.com/minrk\"><code>@​minrk</code></a> (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Ajupyter-server%2Fjupyter_server+involves%3Aminrk+updated%3A2026-05-29..2026-06-17&amp;type=Issues\">activity</a>)\n| <a href=\"https://github.com/Yann-P\"><code>@​Yann-P</code></a> (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Ajupyter-server%2Fjupyter_server+involves%3AYann-P+updated%3A2026-05-29..2026-06-17&amp;type=Issues\">activity</a>)</p>\n<h2>v2.19.0</h2>\n<h2>2.19.0</h2>\n<p>(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/compare/v2.18.2...664e2255c71efe963f397b9f803dbcf503b5a920\">Full\nChangelog</a>)</p>\n<h3>Enhancements made</h3>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">jupyter-server's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>2.20.0</h2>\n<p>(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/compare/v2.19.0...333e700119ee0bcc0b5fcd4c158213d7c275c778\">Full\nChangelog</a>)</p>\n<h3>Enhancements made</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix confusing terminal output when using ServerApp.ip=0.0.0.0 <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/pull/1643\">#1643</a>\n(<a href=\"https://github.com/Yann-P\"><code>@​Yann-P</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/minrk\"><code>@​minrk</code></a>)</li>\n<li>Add a toggle to enable curve encryption for all kernels that support\nit <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/pull/1638\">#1638</a>\n(<a href=\"https://github.com/krassowski\"><code>@​krassowski</code></a>,\n<a href=\"https://github.com/Carreau\"><code>@​Carreau</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/ianthomas23\"><code>@​ianthomas23</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/minrk\"><code>@​minrk</code></a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bugs fixed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Grab the port from <code>bind_sockets</code> in case its different\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/pull/1651\">#1651</a>\n(<a href=\"https://github.com/choldgraf\"><code>@​choldgraf</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/krassowski\"><code>@​krassowski</code></a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Maintenance and upkeep improvements</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Fix <code>test_authorizer</code> having a spurious comma in params\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/pull/1664\">#1664</a>\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/krassowski\"><code>@​krassowski</code></a>)</li>\n<li>Add a reminder to merge GHSA before release <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/pull/1659\">#1659</a>\n(<a href=\"https://github.com/Yann-P\"><code>@​Yann-P</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Carreau\"><code>@​Carreau</code></a>)</li>\n<li>Exclude problematic <code>pywinpty</code> 3.0.4 version <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/pull/1658\">#1658</a>\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/krassowski\"><code>@​krassowski</code></a>)</li>\n<li>ci: explicitly pass base-setup inputs to fix strict validation\nfailures <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/pull/1626\">#1626</a>\n(<a href=\"https://github.com/Carreau\"><code>@​Carreau</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Copilot\"><code>@​Copilot</code></a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Documentation improvements</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Align docs for curve encryption with latest JEP version <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/pull/1660\">#1660</a>\n(<a href=\"https://github.com/krassowski\"><code>@​krassowski</code></a>,\n<a href=\"https://github.com/Carreau\"><code>@​Carreau</code></a>)</li>\n<li>Remove PGP key from docs <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/pull/1653\">#1653</a>\n(<a href=\"https://github.com/Yann-P\"><code>@​Yann-P</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/krassowski\"><code>@​krassowski</code></a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Contributors to this release</h3>\n<p>The following people contributed discussions, new ideas, code and\ndocumentation contributions, and review.\nSee <a\nhref=\"https://github-activity.readthedocs.io/en/latest/use/#how-does-this-tool-define-contributions-in-the-reports\">our\ndefinition of contributors</a>.</p>\n<p>(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/graphs/contributors?from=2026-05-29&amp;to=2026-06-17&amp;type=c\">GitHub\ncontributors page for this release</a>)</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/Carreau\"><code>@​Carreau</code></a> (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Ajupyter-server%2Fjupyter_server+involves%3ACarreau+updated%3A2026-05-29..2026-06-17&amp;type=Issues\">activity</a>)\n| <a href=\"https://github.com/choldgraf\"><code>@​choldgraf</code></a>\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Ajupyter-server%2Fjupyter_server+involves%3Acholdgraf+updated%3A2026-05-29..2026-06-17&amp;type=Issues\">activity</a>)\n| <a href=\"https://github.com/Copilot\"><code>@​Copilot</code></a> (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Ajupyter-server%2Fjupyter_server+involves%3ACopilot+updated%3A2026-05-29..2026-06-17&amp;type=Issues\">activity</a>)\n| <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/ianthomas23\"><code>@​ianthomas23</code></a> (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Ajupyter-server%2Fjupyter_server+involves%3Aianthomas23+updated%3A2026-05-29..2026-06-17&amp;type=Issues\">activity</a>)\n| <a href=\"https://github.com/krassowski\"><code>@​krassowski</code></a>\n(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Ajupyter-server%2Fjupyter_server+involves%3Akrassowski+updated%3A2026-05-29..2026-06-17&amp;type=Issues\">activity</a>)\n| <a href=\"https://github.com/minrk\"><code>@​minrk</code></a> (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Ajupyter-server%2Fjupyter_server+involves%3Aminrk+updated%3A2026-05-29..2026-06-17&amp;type=Issues\">activity</a>)\n| <a href=\"https://github.com/Yann-P\"><code>@​Yann-P</code></a> (<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Ajupyter-server%2Fjupyter_server+involves%3AYann-P+updated%3A2026-05-29..2026-06-17&amp;type=Issues\">activity</a>)</p>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n<h2>2.19.0</h2>\n<p>(<a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/compare/v2.18.2...664e2255c71efe963f397b9f803dbcf503b5a920\">Full\nChangelog</a>)</p>\n<h3>Enhancements made</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Return <code>unresolved</code> stanza when kernel scope is\nunavailable for <code>resolvePath</code> (instead of failing with 404)\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/pull/1641\">#1641</a>\n(<a href=\"https://github.com/MUFFANUJ\"><code>@​MUFFANUJ</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Carreau\"><code>@​Carreau</code></a>, <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/krassowski\"><code>@​krassowski</code></a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Bugs fixed</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Recreate notary store on failure to prevent save deadlock and data\nloss <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/pull/1640\">#1640</a>\n(<a href=\"https://github.com/krassowski\"><code>@​krassowski</code></a>,\n<a href=\"https://github.com/Carreau\"><code>@​Carreau</code></a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Maintenance and upkeep improvements</h3>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/commit/05a78ad879e69ef87e91b2714a8ebeb5ff9628a7\"><code>05a78ad</code></a>\nPublish 2.20.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/commit/6cbee8d65e71abac851c4492fea987ad080580bd\"><code>6cbee8d</code></a>\nMerge commit from fork</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/commit/333e700119ee0bcc0b5fcd4c158213d7c275c778\"><code>333e700</code></a>\nFix <code>test_authorizer</code> having a spurious comma in params (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/issues/1664\">#1664</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/commit/cccd543352d9be0365de56627b671cc8aa9cab0c\"><code>cccd543</code></a>\nFix CI: explicitly pass base-setup inputs to avoid strict validation\nfailures</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/commit/cd16d715dfb1f84b2e5056317927fc930b811842\"><code>cd16d71</code></a>\nAlign docs for curve encryption with latest JEP version (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/issues/1660\">#1660</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/commit/e458061e6ee50368bbdb74153092fc8400704ee0\"><code>e458061</code></a>\nAdd a toggle to enable curve encryption for all kernels that support it\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/issues/1638\">#1638</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jupyter-server/jupyter_server/commit/0ceeb4fb61be1deaaa7c1ff01325f7dd47db1c46\"><code>0ceeb4f<