 access in the Triton convolution2d_bwd_weight\nkernel on B100/B200 (sm100) GPUs (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/187081\">#187081</a>),\nfixed by updating Triton to 3.7.1 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/186814\">#186814</a>)</li>\n<li>Fix fill_ on byte-dtype views with misaligned storage offset (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/186821\">#186821</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Releng / Build</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Drop CPython 3.13t from the binary build matrix (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/182951\">#182951</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/commit/7269437d655783a26cba32aa88195b741ff496aa\"><code>7269437</code></a>\nUpdate triton to 3.7.1 release (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/186814\">#186814</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/commit/88f16c2e68c0bcd24fcc974014c044a4995b26f4\"><code>88f16c2</code></a>\n[MPS] Fix fill_ on byte-dtype views with misaligned storage offset (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/186821\">#186821</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/commit/ccf6e670f128f7f64492468581f89a14fc127eb1\"><code>ccf6e67</code></a>\n[release-only] Update version to 2.12.1 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/186813\">#186813</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/commit/88a6dc788f17f2bf1cc53672b8c40f13cda0673e\"><code>88a6dc7</code></a>\nRevive CUDA 12.9 nightly binary builds (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/186015\">#186015</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/commit/ded55054597e87d73d21266c3099d71943d0515f\"><code>ded5505</code></a>\n[CD] Drop CPython 3.13t from binary build matrix (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/182951\">#182951</a>)\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/186654\">#186654</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/compare/v2.12.0...v2.12.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=torch&package-manager=uv&previous-version=2.12.0&new-version=2.12.1)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> major version` will close this\ngroup update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific\ndependency's major version (unless you unignore this specific\ndependency's major version or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> minor version` will close this\ngroup update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific\ndependency's minor version (unless you unignore this specific\ndependency's minor version or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name>` will close this group update PR\nand stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific dependency\n(unless you unignore this specific dependency or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name>` will remove all of the ignore\nconditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name> <ignore condition>` will\nremove the ignore condition of the specified dependency and ignore\nconditions\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-18T21:50:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8f88817a02cf77f570a75f937ef72a517cb34238","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8f88817a02cf77f570a75f937ef72a517cb34238","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8f88817a02cf77f570a75f937ef72a517cb34238/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"014a9033af70b5b8b08ad2eb36f98590f5f1cca8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/014a9033af70b5b8b08ad2eb36f98590f5f1cca8","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/014a9033af70b5b8b08ad2eb36f98590f5f1cca8"}]},{"sha":"014a9033af70b5b8b08ad2eb36f98590f5f1cca8","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDAxNGE5MDMzYWY3MGI1YjhiMDhhZDJlYjM2Zjk4NTkwZjVmMWNjYTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Colin Francis","email":"131073567+colifran@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-18T21:26:25Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-18T21:26:25Z"},"message":"fix(quickjs): ptc tools in tools namespace are rendered without prepended `tools.` in system prompt and task as ptc duplicated task global (#4075)\n\n### Summary\n\nOur system prompt for the code interpreter has a tools namespace section\nthat shows call signatures for PTC tools. The existing logic rendered\nthose tools without tools. prepended. This caused the agent to confuse\nthe task global with the tools-namespaced (PTC) task variant, which uses\n`subagent_type` instead of `subagentType`. Additionally, since we\nalready expose task as a global we should disallow it from being\nprovided as a ptc tool.\n\nThis PR prepends tools. to rendered PTC tool signatures to differentiate\nPTC tools from globals and throws a value error if task is passed in\nptc.\n\n### Tests\n\n- Unit tests to validate expected behavior\n- Ran an e2e test in LangSmith to validate behavior","tree":{"sha":"e9299bded07441535f69358773f88fa5e3d57bef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/e9299bded07441535f69358773f88fa5e3d57bef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/014a9033af70b5b8b08ad2eb36f98590f5f1cca8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNGKBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYgcQAJaLBWEOYJoY8iugeI+W6wJS\n8XrLle3MZmMdr/mJciabZwqbH3iH1ROa00v8YLh0At0PHWiDdtUYBmjvl+dBrI7j\ng4Ry3h/QH32GcCaQ23uxKR5Thd90yRvWk8JeHICXCFrt3se4d9GX8v+F/w9bhDe4\nM9gsm4n7VEMj8Z80Wv1wS0vDmmfHOJ3GeHk9SKssDCxdJNmGgMrIFJtahOoPNt22\n9m144GimjDYn7xbOPP4XohuV370/5sFKxxjMiL1tPRNRF70XJWHsI/JYCkx57Gre\nWsNgI1RRn5a61HMtAqKD5cxSnpOgyMPw+6QibLSwxPmnXfctBANbp6mcdSlPuTpb\nE+WWrkHYbvIQPAPoUjRb7Zgr7qzEOoB3FXcY3Tf9N/epKgKvm2IO5ywVJuvvpz/I\nxoEfiPuKB4HjKvVyvIy7gC6UhAU3UXbQKIxmMoUnFd5mH46R3NnRXR6MiBuaLk8f\nZ0+y7gdFiCKdjfgfOGNZKSQGUgOee2KuDnBmYOk6Zay0RRP2cd7cy72Ov3U5ldAC\nrd0lhIXXvAxQFsdzEMzMfbj05pmH7tX87cAuwzJ+78I0vRL8eNnPhpXQKIa+9x0e\ntVd/HpeMHfhnUwELNXM50UTfux3ICyNnOmdK1xEJFV8pot/pcP4bxQLVsdi/qu4m\nc5W9NbRvLzGIUM/ELxJL\n=XruV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e9299bded07441535f69358773f88fa5e3d57bef\nparent f99f71259786384098a939a34868f46d47122695\nauthor Colin Francis <131073567+colifran@users.noreply.github.com> 1781817985 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781817985 -0700\n\nfix(quickjs): ptc tools in tools namespace are rendered without prepended `tools.` in system prompt and task as ptc duplicated task global (#4075)\n\n### Summary\n\nOur system prompt for the code interpreter has a tools namespace section\nthat shows call signatures for PTC tools. The existing logic rendered\nthose tools without tools. prepended. This caused the agent to confuse\nthe task global with the tools-namespaced (PTC) task variant, which uses\n`subagent_type` instead of `subagentType`. Additionally, since we\nalready expose task as a global we should disallow it from being\nprovided as a ptc tool.\n\nThis PR prepends tools. to rendered PTC tool signatures to differentiate\nPTC tools from globals and throws a value error if task is passed in\nptc.\n\n### Tests\n\n- Unit tests to validate expected behavior\n- Ran an e2e test in LangSmith to validate behavior","verified_at":"2026-06-18T21:26:26Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/014a9033af70b5b8b08ad2eb36f98590f5f1cca8","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/014a9033af70b5b8b08ad2eb36f98590f5f1cca8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/014a9033af70b5b8b08ad2eb36f98590f5f1cca8/comments","author":{"login":"colifran","id":131073567,"node_id":"U_kgDOB9AGHw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131073567?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/colifran","html_url":"https://github.com/colifran","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colifran/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colifran/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colifran/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colifran/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colifran/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colifran/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colifran/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colifran/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colifran/recei