 the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.6.11](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents==0.6.10...deepagents==0.6.11)\n(2026-06-18)\n\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* **sdk:** route `BaseSandbox async` helpers through aexecute\n([#3996](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3996))\n([52dcf1a](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/52dcf1a42cb00dd614b336038e4398472f78859d))\n\n---\n\n_Everything above this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"341039a2f6bd9e42011976f6193714182fc0c8e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/341039a2f6bd9e42011976f6193714182fc0c8e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/f99f71259786384098a939a34868f46d47122695","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNF0ICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtDQQAHB0uijXAh4dodtb3LYXQO+Q\nhjW/ZU+kidiGSb1cPUpy2mniMClLuFH4lso6A/Y1ZiT7J4EYzZhmCNxwu6LsxNPx\ngq2weyGrQ/LUt2o6TJYlCiABOCxJzGXXRpUswTYtTp51h4/fPCfhlvvrFpcv+0XK\nHMvfmfrX21qZ2+bKmbTiOjIWCiEEzffc0V174fQoqVypQUBo3MA6hK9ZdeiYKEBx\nt2UuEYFWfiMPM4iw/Q7qyX2BBTlyM+A+TuydrRaWxcLF3cwYGIEuVhPiZCcakBWm\ndslHOIKdW1l4UhJHVfQyhec9uadEluOYC8Q1yzLOv2v+rMqP4iSlRato5+CiEwp2\ncj98kvszXf9r8gD3rAi51KZG4fVSz1P2nRyA3ZmekwM4fFsi7v7pu8OVzJJ9/EAK\ncx/3elelI/k0COHGmt6WJXmUVkY25xktjRwHwOaBBU2XcZYc8NoRL5kA5ZmoEEwG\nvwjKfXXfZ2RKPDOENCxiTEhMHRYAl42C78+1we1V+zLd+2RTuHyW3RS+gubPjob8\n1oBLlZKFT8PkW079sKiN/bsqWNn18Q2tveba8mx0+nBzVXFr2l+jTWRdlBnYPqsl\nviHXLZqsLBecqQPkaHSXBB/r3i2mPsNXKGkbjh1hSjaSFyrgTZWTO/pQr0r9vj6b\n2u1jUCVGnVap+SmpyabW\n=eFZI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 341039a2f6bd9e42011976f6193714182fc0c8e1\nparent f3be15bd397f0080a8eeb32a538d34f96361a0bb\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1781816584 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781816584 -0400\n\nrelease(deepagents): 0.6.11 (#4052)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Everything below this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.6.11](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents==0.6.10...deepagents==0.6.11)\n(2026-06-18)\n\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* **sdk:** route `BaseSandbox async` helpers through aexecute\n([#3996](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3996))\n([52dcf1a](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/52dcf1a42cb00dd614b336038e4398472f78859d))\n\n---\n\n_Everything above this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-18T21:03:05Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f99f71259786384098a939a34868f46d47122695","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f99f71259786384098a939a34868f46d47122695","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f99f71259786384098a939a34868f46d47122695/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f3be15bd397f0080a8eeb32a538d34f96361a0bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f3be15bd397f0080a8eeb32a538d34f96361a0bb","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f3be15bd397f0080a8eeb32a538d34f96361a0bb"}]},{"sha":"f3be15bd397f0080a8eeb32a538d34f96361a0bb","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGYzYmUxNWJkMzk3ZjAwODBhOGVlYjMyYTUzOGQzNGY5NjM2MWEwYmI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Sydney Runkle","email":"54324534+sydney-runkle@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-18T20:50:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-18T20:50:17Z"},"message":"refactor(sdk): use `RemoveMessage` sentinel in FS and patch tool calls middleware (#4072)\n\n`FilesystemMiddleware` and `PatchToolCallsMiddleware` previously emitted\n`Overwrite(...)` to atomically replace the `messages` channel. With the\nlocal `_messages_delta_reducer` and `DeltaChannel`, the same semantics\nare expressible as a `RemoveMessage(REMOVE_ALL_MESSAGES)` sentinel\nfollowed by the desired message list — which is the standard\n`add_messages`-compatible idiom and avoids depending on `Overwrite`.\n\nThree call sites change:\n\n- `PatchToolCallsMiddleware.before_agent` now returns\n`[RemoveMessage(id=REMOVE_ALL_MESSAGES), *patched_messages]`.\n- `FilesystemMiddleware._apply_eviction_and_truncate` emits the same\nsentinel-prefixed list when tagging a newly evicted `HumanMessage`,\npreserving the \"atomic replace so DeltaChannel replay doesn't duplicate\nthe `id=None` write\" property.\n- `FilesystemMiddleware._intercept_large_tool_result` (and its async\nsibling) now detect a leading `REMOVE_ALL_MESSAGES` sentinel on incoming\ntool `Command` updates instead of an `Overwrite` wrapper, and re-emit\nthe sentinel after eviction processing.\n\n`Overwrite` is no longer imported by either middleware. Unit tests\ncovering both middlewares are updated to assert the new\nsentinel-prefixed list shape.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nick Hollon <nick.hollon@langchain.dev>","tree":{"sha":"5cafdfdff6b678bae4729b62d99a1d0702c3673b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/5cafdfdff6b678bae4729b62d99a1d0702c3673b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/f3be15bd397f0080a8eeb32a538d34f96361a0bb","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNFoJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3kEQAI1BDlD5VM3WzpiQPtWuOVRd\nwTfQbkn2GtP7hl66XcTX7X0V6P50Updkdbe/keKvyEqvjwjvDYqJ9te2nwX3J1an\n5UPtdGLZwFmIGvJxXGqptpcsGUh8OCe15fWDSl2Tjan38rfrMJ5c+YgmhVOFcSG7\n/S2OZJjp2ml+jBZ/wa96S6egva1wJ+FJKkCK7iD8fkhl5GwMJAFNfMbbjPEo83yZ\nNajIlDkosuNBanbuFmWv78nlHro2qIyW62nFoz3tXU2Wthz+mYkWeHL4o5twNKoZ\nwHucPxj9SMiYVQpQMOQySFEZq9jlAuSHmfI1BrfMEH7Fvn8kSzLNp7OPXXmb8T8+\nVzpTZ778ef6QQC9e9rJshosUyULrKIgsSaR222HRWMVWBPotGqflDfB98t8tuIEw\nHt7UpZMfGBQc8nXl/OBm08Wlx0ptBKo/oYYSOYqqiS4Hrod6DQcxA28D31sYf+HC\n/E5h7jsYZlc43L14lyQ2uGyrmIyN0F7OPbrcDsd9CRcC28ECopxdsX4k/Q4JXm6V\n00lMwOEwTGnTzpNA9iowCAcgU2tAeulCKJlkWkZGor2Z4UUcHxG5IRTFEusaXc6I\n+IOSh1En8mQbRGXcdxGgsfqphY6u3sWJJHrvoTUhU3X5bUJtwqYkwdwq594y2qJF\nw5ymjUxNrD2nh1nrOD8J\n=29zR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5cafdfdff6b678bae4729b62d99a1d0702c3673b\nparent 7f33becf3fced05ce828b6581b6c1a8b70692a66\nauthor Sydney Runkle <54324534+sydney-runkle@users.noreply.github.com> 1781815817 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781815817 -0400\n\nrefactor(sdk): use `RemoveMessage` sentinel in FS and patch tool calls middleware (#4072)\n\n`FilesystemMiddleware` and `PatchToolCallsMiddleware` previously emitted\n`Overwrite(...)` to atomically replace the `messages` channel. With the\nlocal `_messages_delta_reducer` and `DeltaChannel`, the same semantics\nare expressible as a `RemoveMessage(REMOVE_ALL_MESSAGES)` sentinel\nfollowed by the desired message list — which is the standard\n`add_messages`-compatible idiom and avoids depending on `Overwrite`.\n\nThree call sites change:\n\n- `PatchToolCallsMiddleware.before_agent` now returns\n`[RemoveMessage(id=REMOVE_ALL_MESSAGES), *patched_messages]`.\n- `FilesystemMiddleware._apply_eviction_and_truncate` emits the same\nsentinel-prefixed list when tagging a newly evicted `HumanMessage`,\npreserving the \"atomic replace so DeltaChannel replay doesn't duplicate\nthe `id=None` write\" property.\n- `FilesystemMiddleware._intercept_large_tool_result` (and its async\nsibling) now detect a leading `REMOVE_ALL_MESSAGES` sentinel on incoming\ntool `Command` updates instead of an `Overwrite` wrapper, and re-emit\nthe sentinel after eviction processing.\n\n`Overwrite` is no longer imported by either middleware. Unit tests\ncovering both middlewares are updated to assert the new\nsentinel-prefixed list shape.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nick Hollon <nick.hollon@langchain.dev>","verified_at":"2026-06-18T20:50:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f3be15bd397f0080a8eeb32a538d34f96361a0bb","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f3be15bd397f0080a8eeb32a538d34f96361a0bb","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f3be15bd397f0080a8eeb32a538d34f96361a0bb/comments","author":{"login":"sydney-runkle","id":54324534,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MzI0NTM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54324534?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sydney-runkle","html_url":"https://github.com/sydney-runkle","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sydney-runkle/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sydney-runkle/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sydney-runkle/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sydney-runkle/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sydney-runkle/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sydney-runkle/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sydney-runkle/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sydney-runkle/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sydney-runkle/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7f33becf3fced05ce828b6581b6c1a8b70692a66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7f33becf3fced05ce828b6581b6c1a8b70692a66","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7f33becf3fced05ce828b6581b6c1a8b70692a66"}]},{"sha":"7f33becf3fced05ce828b6581b6c1a8b70692a66","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDdmMzNiZWNmM2ZjZWQwNWNlODI4YjY1ODFiNmMxYThiNzA2OTJhNjY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-18T19:20:31Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-18T19:20:31Z"},"message":"test(code): speed up Textual widget tests (#4078)\n\nSeveral UI-heavy unit tests now exercise the logic they care about\ndirectly instead of routing every assertion through full Textual\nkeypress flows. The test harness also isolates update checks and app\nstate more consistently so local developer config and background startup\nbehavior do not affect unrelated tests.\n\n## Changes\n- Added shared test isolation for startup update checks and app-managed\nstate, while leaving `test_config_manifest` and `test_main` free to\npatch `is_update_check_enabled` themselves.\n- Added `_closing_run_worker_mock` for server restart tests so mocked\n`run_worker` calls close swallowed coroutine work and avoid leaking\nunawaited coroutine warnings.\n- Converted pure `ModelSelectorScreen` filtering and fuzzy matching\ntests to use deterministic in-memory selector state, while keeping\nseparate Textual smoke coverage for real keyboard/UI behavior.\n- Reduced repeated Textual keypress loops in MCP viewer scrolling tests\nby directly positioning the scroll viewport before asserting jump\nbehavior.\n- Changed the thread selector focus-order test to call\n`ThreadSelectorScreen.action_focus_next_filter()` directly instead of\ndispatching repeated synthetic Tab events.","tree":{"sha":"774501cf3c182fef326621455c5eb738e5c734d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/774501cf3c182fef326621455c5eb738e5c734d2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/7f33becf3fced05ce828b6581b6c1a8b70692a66","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNET/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAM/YQAI7ylZsZRU/j0g2KkHqQxVOI\n9W8478UEdUeAL+jIL7NcMWiNjeZ/q2sZRnbkbiFGOb83FFekUyi8m9TK1Y11tsFe\nqLhNQIdtTKr2seq78+S091z5XxA6vr2YnktX5E551KYKcFFU79OGa1+Ozh5tcSax\n4PAf35/d7yQTRplAPIhq9mT/y1aSAUPA3MdPYLKf9RaopUZaPluUQdbnB7F35t0o\nyacJh7tsc4XRuBajfIpPGC5Y5T1FIe5iIqreRRpUfPbbtD51Yo2Hx3P7sbkSTdny\nuum5DujbxzV1m4gJZ2TMszEgxX0J1lU6De/ucVf24ZvtT0m1x2K1v4a16VGxp1DH\n5i8V1H+6h4qqj43h9IMSt+IU1+lqQ9lVr+ETgwSv4AfIBGyJSi8GudI3dU6P6D8B\nbB0+2Cj2p5HrHBB9fXo9oZSk2+a+yrXVH4PMQv0y4atGzBHiOWnC4pUg6n0i4iTp\nlfb08MC2CLgm7ch1VxGFPKQ043NAKI6Dlm4Zro7YDw0cFG+BW/sEKjpHLXTZDh3P\nYsdtwuE3WxqHkgU5TYpewvzrP+Up0FZc+uMcXR8byonYvk+m5y0HLt0D/hE9pLWe\nPDgvyaiBPZoCuwc/cJl65r+oz7QRpSJkNyVm5+tHhuTRjI3Je6qUFmkEPGoVtwZb\ngiQG3HVIBQusSSrXV6MU\n=+lvK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 774501cf3c182fef326621455c5eb738e5c734d2\nparent f46119e804e7e108073cfae261a739f6e77b1318\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781810431 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781810431 -0400\n\ntest(code): speed up Textual widget tests (#4078)\n\nSeveral UI-heavy unit tests now exercise the logic they care about\ndirectly instead of routing every assertion through full Textual\nkeypress flows. The test harness also isolates update checks and app\nstate more consistently so local developer config and background startup\nbehavior do not affect unrelated tests.\n\n## Changes\n- Added shared test isolation for startup update checks and app-managed\nstate, while leaving `test_config_manifest` and `test_main` free to\npatch `is_update_check_enabled` themselves.\n- Added `_closing_run_worker_mock` for server restart tests so mocked\n`run_worker` calls close swallowed coroutine work and avoid leaking\nunawaited coroutine warnings.\n- Converted pure `ModelSelectorScreen` filtering and fuzzy matching\ntests to use deterministic in-memory selector state, while keeping\nseparate Textual smoke coverage for real keyboard/UI behavior.\n- Reduced repeated Textual keypress loops in MCP viewer scrolling tests\nby directly positioning the scroll viewport before asserting jump\nbehavior.\n- Changed the thread selector focus-order test to call\n`ThreadSelectorScreen.action_focus_next_filter()` directly instead of\ndispatching repeated synthetic Tab events.","verified_at":"2026-06-18T19:20:32Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7f33becf3fced05ce828b6581b6c1a8b70692a66","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7f33becf3fced05ce828b6581b6c1a8b70692a66","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7f33