uFqYa2E959LT9LJz1hWJcI\nw0LS233IfcqRl3fsG0/eBbDRXdyS0EpTBKcAleUmlDKTfRAfHx715pmyiKGpG6iz\nz4qrjE9dXYTSjWRpfc+iAepz/c7/2m105i43A4RDBt5+QYjXYAOi0nHUsY1dS6d5\nqxB6dqTjaj+1K/uIMCb/BkD36/1YotAslNynhbcLH/YjwzVoS+Cltq6FVzEbRj0Z\nodPxc3naONWOe/+EC6Sg\n=5Qle\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7ab835a0a1123342fc2e0305c731333068fad700\nparent 8ee6ba6e64895d3d36a5957627221ed7667bc1d4\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781666655 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781666655 -0400\n\nfeat(code): add latest frontier models to recommended list (#4045)\n\nAdd latest frontier models (GLM-5.2, Kimi-K2.7-Code, Qwen3.7-Plus,\nMiniMax-M3, OpenRouter Fusion, Nemotron-3-Ultra) to the recommended\nmodel list.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/88e46d86-b8e4-0215-cc92-afac20e1cae9)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-17T03:24:16Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/114535637eaee383c64eac5282bc9ac57007c83f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/114535637eaee383c64eac5282bc9ac57007c83f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/114535637eaee383c64eac5282bc9ac57007c83f/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8ee6ba6e64895d3d36a5957627221ed7667bc1d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8ee6ba6e64895d3d36a5957627221ed7667bc1d4","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8ee6ba6e64895d3d36a5957627221ed7667bc1d4"}]},{"sha":"8ee6ba6e64895d3d36a5957627221ed7667bc1d4","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDhlZTZiYTZlNjQ4OTVkM2QzNmE1OTU3NjI3MjIxZWQ3NjY3YmMxZDQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-17T02:24:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-17T02:24:43Z"},"message":"fix(code): exclude prompt prefix from `UserMessage` selection (#4002)\n\nSelecting a user message no longer copies the leading prompt prefix — `>\n`, or the mode glyph `$ ` / `/ ` — into the clipboard. That prefix is\npurely decorative.\n\nOn these `Static`-based message widgets, both double-click and\ntriple-click select the entire message (Textual maps double-click to\n`text_select_all`, and triple-click escalates to the scroll container's\nselect-all); previously both pulled the prefix into the copied text.\n\n`UserMessage` and `QueuedUserMessage` now override `get_selection` to\ndrop the two-column prefix from row 0 of any selection that starts\nthere, leaving body-only and later-row selections untouched. This is the\nactual fix and applies to every gesture — double-click, triple-click,\nand drag-from-start.\n\nThey also override `text_select_all` so the double-click highlight\nbegins after the glyph. This affects the highlight only on double-click;\ntriple-click routes through the container and still renders the glyph as\nhighlighted, though it is never copied.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"301b5b4cc134464762e6b1905af34b0bd8d0bfee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/301b5b4cc134464762e6b1905af34b0bd8d0bfee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/8ee6ba6e64895d3d36a5957627221ed7667bc1d4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMgVrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApwkQAJzWsw27Jw6eLeMknuegUAg6\nZoalQr5dPLok6eoYmlkU2kFoD+E9Ipys8o0jvbnQfFRpHSsGMol1AwEUIkgZizR/\nWbXdRK7eIyrERMzjLUQjnT1kl/iMfragaINBGuLSELnQN3y+5b7aP9Y6xVs4oiR3\nN5GJl7YcMv8vcuXFVFeRsUsiqNtetCsRof3VUszbLULIJdCT2ADFf2ZBqZyj2e/C\nYYFaSjfsj8qH/NMOAtRPWfPKz0QQjxl3ql4A0g2+SiB2WimNiMryD710Pa1EWVAM\nucGnVs9fAMd4lI3XknaIvKpuk4DuCkB+wgfB9Bk1D/QPRaeiVLPxs0WwcON0lSHk\nqgkJCXg5gz8l3QBXeA1UBZGnMhbb7Y1fEXEFRPSINfZSVX5OHwpj+cKdfNPB6yS2\n/GcYohmz0hd0UJOU6ISmVpkFlsVNPFDzdwoZrYJKtPHV+5JDzOVlCSPI628P2aFp\nNtK3v5OzHtyS3kgPGcvzt1qcxC3WQA+YygwXw6pZ7zwQlPnoJas6tfSP+PNKeRwb\ng76Z7325KLOR8+XHRlPlJ/LIsdAWIzec8VxkCr8SVEPMG8kffv+iPesnTN1pwrdp\nZj4f9UcYdn8NphmxVPcOBiD2cOkkdQtlRrBb9JufwrjMyeRfNeihiOX3lhecO75C\nO5YIW6zni9khsNzsDqCj\n=Txhs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 301b5b4cc134464762e6b1905af34b0bd8d0bfee\nparent 14be63d476ed8dece75e20fff05016122c258be8\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781663083 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781663083 -0400\n\nfix(code): exclude prompt prefix from `UserMessage` selection (#4002)\n\nSelecting a user message no longer copies the leading prompt prefix — `>\n`, or the mode glyph `$ ` / `/ ` — into the clipboard. That prefix is\npurely decorative.\n\nOn these `Static`-based message widgets, both double-click and\ntriple-click select the entire message (Textual maps double-click to\n`text_select_all`, and triple-click escalates to the scroll container's\nselect-all); previously both pulled the prefix into the copied text.\n\n`UserMessage` and `QueuedUserMessage` now override `get_selection` to\ndrop the two-column prefix from row 0 of any selection that starts\nthere, leaving body-only and later-row selections untouched. This is the\nactual fix and applies to every gesture — double-click, triple-click,\nand drag-from-start.\n\nThey also override `text_select_all` so the double-click highlight\nbegins after the glyph. This affects the highlight only on double-click;\ntriple-click routes through the container and still renders the glyph as\nhighlighted, though it is never copied.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-17T02:24:43Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8ee6ba6e64895d3d36a5957627221ed7667bc1d4","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8ee6ba6e64895d3d36a5957627221ed7667bc1d4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8ee6ba6e64895d3d36a5957627221ed7667bc1d4/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"14be63d476ed8dece75e20fff05016122c258be8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/14be63d476ed8dece75e20fff05016122c258be8","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/14be63d476ed8dece75e20fff05016122c258be8"}]},{"sha":"14be63d476ed8dece75e20fff05016122c258be8","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDE0YmU2M2Q0NzZlZDhkZWNlNzVlMjBmZmYwNTAxNjEyMmMyNThiZTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-17T02:07:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-17T02:07:14Z"},"message":"feat(code): note minimum OpenAI key permissions in `/auth` (#4040)\n\nThe OpenAI `/auth` prompt now documents the minimum Restricted key\npermissions Deep Agents Code needs.\n\n---\n\nWhen acquiring an OpenAI API key, users can pick `all`, `restricted`, or\n`read only` scopes. Deep Agents Code doesn't use any OpenAI provider\ntools, so a `restricted` key with `write` on Responses (`/v1/responses`)\nis sufficient — plus `request` on Chat completions\n(`/v1/chat/completions`) only when a completions model is used. The\n`/auth` prompt now surfaces this so users don't over-provision an `all`\nkey. This follows the existing per-provider special-casing in the\nkey-acquisition instructions (e.g. Azure OpenAI).\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/5e320e33-7cc7-c2c4-4b91-ec46eda94a74)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"0687f496ffc881bbfe29a2eec6edabcf59b571b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/0687f496ffc881bbfe29a2eec6edabcf59b571b9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/14be63d476ed8dece75e20fff05016122c258be8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMgFSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwBMQACu0WUYa6USrwghM5X3v7/xj\n59UTOH3Xtq9g8pV/0btOYP3fCcN1qC+oit9ZqiBA4NYAIFXeAAasvSk5Mfh5iQWY\nBEHS/k51UXCR4EpYKFLCcxUtMXUh783iXHpdt64r9bAe+93pAo4Y+WYceXzQk8Ky\nBObtZPC7kJiWalW9eH4GL/N2aX5l3n2b2LBLFihipeI4U2cfJspLkLE3q7KsNGkb\nsvR+nC2V1UDpeOikbQ/W8olyZm/HCS26cK18iCo4Fw7/13/r2sqlkHqf2rALSB9o\nA7w9oSrw9KERG0dca0GF3y+gzPOKaw8iVhbUya8v8p2+H6wrs0YWVyEt2Xl68+zF\ngEUHz0VEsusZFlEn4uFBo428QsVCutI4ZjqncUUzu8teCojtd5TWG5GOcb1caqyp\nV3YsnO71LeXhL8LXOnVxsIbWBrodvvS4i1XqfZn9yQ/nZUJFCuOOsMdB6W/jDOTi\n6+YNNGj8cDyCehcyM/0IMCBJSEVh22ckHR6SSzA/VltQ3EXu2xm8e5ssW97aT+ZV\nlYmiVOhzVEZ1qGvjU3/OEdKJRNLI+mZcOZpMyzuQztlgZd7g29n2v4KAyzTjTzqR\nc53irbTd2zPCtEARcWJ6oWqb8wH/tNz9WGwh4QooWyDxQt/xjEuAZBE4GzdhU+r5\nlIy3It6aaR8SuAfvxmaL\n=d3bx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0687f496ffc881bbfe29a2eec6edabcf59b571b9\nparent 1b94cf322949e0cafd6f2bacf343fb0044ec5a8c\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781662034 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781662034 -0400\n\nfeat(code): note minimum OpenAI key permissions in `/auth` (#4040)\n\nThe OpenAI `/auth` prompt now documents the minimum Restricted key\npermissions Deep Agents Code needs.\n\n---\n\nWhen acquiring an OpenAI API key, users can pick `all`, `restricted`, or\n`read only` scopes. Deep Agents Code doesn't use any OpenAI provider\ntools, so a `restricted` key with `write` on Responses (`/v1/responses`)\nis sufficient — plus `request` on Chat completions\n(`/v1/chat/completions`) only when a completions model is used. The\n`/auth` prompt now surfaces this so users don't over-provision an `all`\nkey. This follows the existing per-provider special-casing in the\nkey-acquisition instructions (e.g. Azure OpenAI).\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/5e320e33-7cc7-c2c4-4b91-ec46eda94a74)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-17T02:07:15Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/14be63d476ed8dece75e20fff05016122c258be8","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/14be63d476ed8dece75e20fff05016122c258be8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/14be63d476ed8dece75e20fff05016122c258be8/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1b94cf322949e0cafd6f2bacf343fb0044ec5a8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1b94cf322949e0cafd6f2bacf343fb0044ec5a8c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1b94cf322949e0cafd6f2bacf343fb0044ec5a8c"}]},{"sha":"1b94cf322949e0cafd6f2bacf343fb0044ec5a8c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDFiOTRjZjMyMjk0OWUwY2FmZDZmMmJhY2YzNDNmYjAwNDRlYzVhOGM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-17T01:54:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-17T01:54:19Z"},"message":"feat(code): dual-write agent traces to extra LangSmith projects (#3998)\n\n[Docs](https://github.com/langchain-ai/docs/pull/4481/changes)\n\ndcode can now dual-write agent traces to additional LangSmith projects\nvia `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_LANGSMITH_REPLICA_PROJECTS`.\n\n---\n\ndcode currently routes each agent run to a single LangSmith project.\nThis adds an opt-in `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_LANGSMITH_REPLICA_PROJECTS`\n(comma-separated) that mirrors the run to a primary project (e.g.\n`deepagents-code`) *and* each listed project using LangSmith write\nreplicas. The runtime `tracing_context(replicas=...)` route is used\n(project-only replicas reuse the default client), so\n`LANGSMITH_ENDPOINT` is untouched and no API keys are embedded in env.\nOff by default — a single env-var read when unset.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"1bda29f6bbfced2070edb57fe5db9132e314e428","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/1bda29f6bbfced2070edb57fe5db9132e314e428"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/1b94cf322949e0cafd6f2bacf343fb0044ec5a8c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMf5LCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA110QACDjJaSahDt57YWdvQmlQV0M\nSokbsaFoiJA++X78+RdxrL9pOlbjdGXzS2v6FJQ7Nq6Chz6Gkf4wXSFVJXPq0Gzp\nsu8L+YqbKW5lnJ5NEFWP5Pu6Vu1MJQmYfuplLe1jxCIBygD402YmPD9W+t4+t/9r\nHSRzTJQPniqtCoPf1YF6rXlQK/ZI8foeuOO4mUVHYCE5bQZZXBgvizAvsM9j4+xX\nz37yCcc6UgT42P8L/RBvU6soQ8XUhsdmOPT9GFF47MhM7SZJYG8o4po+e2iYWBnd\nvvQ7iMZLvHfUBSJzpybkiK8C+XE8qpmgbQV9dBdVk7y/Y+PmW6zYqBJMMqv8wW1O\nv4FKV6eefQmx4lN4uXsRAA56g/WQl/BlX88cHCQlHXWzOA4IKmcN/m7hIqVB1DCg\n1bGpWMxUOd2d1/qmxZpNabs4rV86rfCVOgQDl4kYTaXI4rY1D/0C9nH0UcEV911f\nMKmrPTbx9DIeTIP8yt+0Zl98ot/SY+UG+s7kJFbFT4C92TDhRF/j0UQKiiUA8j/7\njYFTj6SvP+BjV2pdNgDqDXOFKG9WXv+pHbfkLk3l355fdsZksgteZSFIiSULpQGd\nJbdvxKS68P2ZQpx4yBHrxVjfa1Ae6aMguBaz6ShjbiH/uqizqY/Nzbz1jacAzY6K\nUM5JEPrJ7awo8XWVK4Gk\n=+02y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1bda29f6bbfced2070edb57fe5db9132e314e428\nparent 7f380b4cd8776d75c289c40b9ce78686bcc33f0f\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781661259 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781661259 -0400\n\nfeat(code): dual-write agent traces to extra LangSmith projects (#3998)\n\n[Docs](https://github.com/langchain-ai/docs/pull/4481/changes)\n\ndcode can now dual-write agent traces to additional LangSmith projects\nvia `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_LANGSMITH_REPLICA_PROJECTS`.\n\n---\n\ndcode currently routes each agent run to a single LangSmith project.\nThis adds an opt-in `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_LANGSMITH_REPLICA_PROJECTS`\n(comma-separated) that mirrors the run to a primary project (e.g.\n`deepagents-code`) *and* each listed project using LangSmith write\nreplicas. The runtime `tracing_context(replicas=...)` route is used\n(project-only replicas reuse the default client), so\n`LANGSMITH_ENDPOINT` is untouched and no API keys are embedded in env.\nOff by default — a single env-var read when unset.\n\nMade by [Open SWE](https://openswe.vercel.app)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-17T01:54:19Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1b94cf322949e0cafd6f2bacf343fb0044ec5a8c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1b94cf322949e0cafd6f2bacf343fb0044ec5a8c","comments_