ngWorZPSRoOMxXVr06w6E4oGssZq7a5Y\n1PutJOmT8I5/VjckP1Vl\n=IAb9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3b9c024276cc0e0784a31831b84bddedd55347c6\nparent 74aa1e00765f1c654009e77b7da37a17bcb21619\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781642084 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781642084 -0400\n\ndocs(repo): clarify forced release guidance (#4038)\n\nRelease guidance now explains how to force a release PR when a package\nhas no releasable commits since the last GA. The docs avoid the unsafe\nempty-commit path and make the package path-scoping requirement explicit\nso release-please targets the intended component.","verified_at":"2026-06-16T20:34:45Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7f380b4cd8776d75c289c40b9ce78686bcc33f0f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7f380b4cd8776d75c289c40b9ce78686bcc33f0f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7f380b4cd8776d75c289c40b9ce78686bcc33f0f/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"74aa1e00765f1c654009e77b7da37a17bcb21619","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/74aa1e00765f1c654009e77b7da37a17bcb21619","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/74aa1e00765f1c654009e77b7da37a17bcb21619"}]},{"sha":"74aa1e00765f1c654009e77b7da37a17bcb21619","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDc0YWExZTAwNzY1ZjFjNjU0MDA5ZTc3YjdkYTM3YTE3YmNiMjE2MTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"github-actions[bot]","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-16T20:32:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-16T20:32:16Z"},"message":"release(deepagents-code): 0.1.18 (#4039)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Everything below this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.18](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.17...deepagents-code==0.1.18)\n(2026-06-16)\n\n### Features\n\n* Add provider-specific auth guidance\n([#4004](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4004))\n([6a39247](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6a392471ba30089b1a63135494873d55209bb081))\n\n---\n\n_Everything above this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"dd74738a359d234c8050d5033a14a4a83d637bbf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/dd74738a359d234c8050d5033a14a4a83d637bbf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/74aa1e00765f1c654009e77b7da37a17bcb21619","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMbLQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAw0QQAATd9R2b72oU3whn5z5hFbOC\nWLVsN7dcb/d3S8a6GD/cpbrUMqG8X2zhp8+Y6u58CIAAsbgBM+ybqyj8y2ODIkmv\nStOKkbU4EeXSi1qJqlL0hBF3wObGlMZjFmSy1FU8QOCP1lW3ymlJUroQIjzXxw2S\nJWxdnhQpv113dd0/atgCIUernARBXG9TLACPg0TZro316UjbP8egvq3OIiQYuuz/\nBPVvnHfbHoqWk5mZ0sqRJpF/zGsCi9qbsfQafskE2mLxjaGZ+KdKZw3fSInREhVT\nBmYER0J/igNfy3w6bjDV5l/serqxw2zKAM6+Vq7C/cq1CA/ZXKx/N5qjd2wPPOjV\nZu2Hs3BjFEbywAUFsxiwc9FjXM+lWe+LVd9ePb6wQdIaucnaPLlcu36xAGaxoCTQ\nVPg9NWjABpJHQSsUI857IXYReUk7TEZPGnDhfmC901kC9Qmn6ZdEfKGYELpkHdKu\nYRAti5ik00de7FYv7V/n8xgTwpz6EnNq5OgpaLoOTNspbahyytUB2cdaW1psGvb0\n6rVnoA3j+sahuEv7hsgTgubJYle0hx/xPCyxjRGMcxAYBt1x2fXRKn/Z9bm4759+\nSnn7o8wgUPSMsNwj+MRgtcCCaX+L20bjeHb0BhPE4+fXOvzpeVR7S8mf7Stc1uCc\nh+BPuOjlW7D+O8AzTeZ9\n=ngOR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree dd74738a359d234c8050d5033a14a4a83d637bbf\nparent 6a392471ba30089b1a63135494873d55209bb081\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1781641936 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781641936 -0400\n\nrelease(deepagents-code): 0.1.18 (#4039)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Everything below this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.18](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.17...deepagents-code==0.1.18)\n(2026-06-16)\n\n### Features\n\n* Add provider-specific auth guidance\n([#4004](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/4004))\n([6a39247](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6a392471ba30089b1a63135494873d55209bb081))\n\n---\n\n_Everything above this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-16T20:32:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/74aa1e00765f1c654009e77b7da37a17bcb21619","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/74aa1e00765f1c654009e77b7da37a17bcb21619","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/74aa1e00765f1c654009e77b7da37a17bcb21619/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6a392471ba30089b1a63135494873d55209bb081","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6a392471ba30089b1a63135494873d55209bb081","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6a392471ba30089b1a63135494873d55209bb081"}]},{"sha":"6a392471ba30089b1a63135494873d55209bb081","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDZhMzkyNDcxYmEzMDA4OWIxYTYzMTM1NDk0ODczZDU1MjA5YmIwODE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-16T20:21:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-16T20:21:07Z"},"message":"feat(code): add provider-specific auth guidance (#4004)\n\nAuth setup now leads users through getting the right provider API key\nbefore asking them to paste it, while keeping endpoint and\nenvironment-variable details behind an Advanced disclosure. Provider\nconfiguration can also supply human-readable labels and key-management\nURLs so custom providers read cleanly in `/auth`.\n\n## Changes\n- Added provider-specific display names and API-key links for the auth\nflow, including custom `display_name` and `api_key_url` metadata through\n`ProviderConfig`.\n- Reworked `AuthPromptScreen` to show key acquisition guidance first,\ncall out active environment-sourced credentials, and distinguish scoped\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_` variables from shared provider variables.\n- Moved base URL overrides and env-var precedence details into an\nAdvanced section toggled by F2 or click, with Unicode/ASCII disclosure\nglyphs.\n- Updated auth manager provider labels to use `_provider_display_name`\ninstead of raw provider config keys.\n- Added pointer cursor behavior for clickable links and disclosure rows\nacross auth, Codex login, MCP login, and thread selector modals.\n- Renamed environment credential badges from `[env: ...]` to `[env set:\n...]` for clearer status labels.","tree":{"sha":"35bed835fc41b90b203ec5ba2a166aaeb271b1c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/35bed835fc41b90b203ec5ba2a166aaeb271b1c8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/6a392471ba30089b1a63135494873d55209bb081","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMbAzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvPYQAEoeMmA2HXhvC2cdcAKNW7ko\n2w2m9qFcpksKJeN1DuCf2Ot+/RJHbJTByFzm++MhDIrflIlXxs9Ln4A5BuTzMY0/\nN0DpTyO4HosthbpIjGvT7Vip0aZ+Z6mVk9GboYTG7efd8+ie5CUXDtstlo8EI1Yx\n2Qq1f+2Zcybfr5583IXvT+ZtAt4R4IjrT7+sSd/BLyGrbKdQqfpvGbw04GG62EvI\n7mIqMKKvil1bVSDVsTGROnr8ONSpzBzOA1pLdg53WhMawFHsL0IXVPvGFyjls74s\nlxmV90IUUxVVeoDduqk/casMuaQTqvs7akTnm3ypkW9kdbyJAOmtiZTmJgQCSJPA\nz5J5cFIqENTGteMSRYNurTWPtbE7wUW+sKVuZRAONx3AHZKgKYg3MU8i+YEm/2py\nJr8/XOFa2rE8ftCLT4yJcSVuOqi4nrdNi8yaBgjHKtR7QCZuJ4i1TudiqNYU1BNq\nOhLbGIKTQg/xuTTO+Z3zcorx+z+mjG0ddg4tF4IdAwsNTXV9vtLkq+yn3nQNLKca\nHRXK47gjonZkQPl/ogv9IQUAxiML950PcSOyWnmV7oNkGA9/jwvegmcf3MksAQYo\nz50HzcFhsxOx5oV7AkZ6p+TTSShzt/E9kimOueZbgv7JEYzG4VuNYZcxR+/PhOQ+\n6fbeuEuUiYUUhyZdXWBm\n=lW7A\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 35bed835fc41b90b203ec5ba2a166aaeb271b1c8\nparent 7760214fb468ff65afd88218fc42a023f7fe3365\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781641267 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781641267 -0400\n\nfeat(code): add provider-specific auth guidance (#4004)\n\nAuth setup now leads users through getting the right provider API key\nbefore asking them to paste it, while keeping endpoint and\nenvironment-variable details behind an Advanced disclosure. Provider\nconfiguration can also supply human-readable labels and key-management\nURLs so custom providers read cleanly in `/auth`.\n\n## Changes\n- Added provider-specific display names and API-key links for the auth\nflow, including custom `display_name` and `api_key_url` metadata through\n`ProviderConfig`.\n- Reworked `AuthPromptScreen` to show key acquisition guidance first,\ncall out active environment-sourced credentials, and distinguish scoped\n`DEEPAGENTS_CODE_` variables from shared provider variables.\n- Moved base URL overrides and env-var precedence details into an\nAdvanced section toggled by F2 or click, with Unicode/ASCII disclosure\nglyphs.\n- Updated auth manager provider labels to use `_provider_display_name`\ninstead of raw provider config keys.\n- Added pointer cursor behavior for clickable links and disclosure rows\nacross auth, Codex login, MCP login, and thread selector modals.\n- Renamed environment credential badges from `[env: ...]` to `[env set:\n...]` for clearer status labels.","verified_at":"2026-06-16T20:21:08Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6a392471ba30089b1a63135494873d55209bb081","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/6a392471ba30089b1a63135494873d55209bb081","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/6a392471ba30089b1a63135494873d55209bb081/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7760214fb468ff65afd88218fc42a023f7fe3365","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7760214fb468ff65afd88218fc42a023f7fe3365","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7760214fb468ff65afd88218fc42a023f7fe3365"}]},{"sha":"7760214fb468ff65afd88218fc42a023f7fe3365","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDc3NjAyMTRmYjQ2OGZmNjVhZmQ4ODIxOGZjNDJhMDIzZjdmZTMzNjU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Hunter Lovell","email":"40191806+hntrl@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-16T19:34:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-16T19:34:55Z"},"message":"chore(code): bump langchain-quickjs to 0.2.0 (#4037)\n\nBumps the `langchain-quickjs` dependency constraint in `deepagents-code`\nfrom `>=0.1.4,<0.2.0` to `>=0.2.0,<0.3.0`. `langchain-quickjs` is the\nJavaScript REPL interpreter behind the dcode `--interpreter` flag.\n\nThe `langchain-quickjs` partner package was already released at `0.2.0`\non `main`, but the published `deepagents-code` constraint (`<0.2.0`)\nexcluded it. This bump aligns dcode with the released interpreter so\nthat, once a new `deepagents-code` is published, `/install quickjs` (and\n`dcode --install quickjs`) pulls in `langchain-quickjs` 0.2.x.","tree":{"sha":"e3ba1a2f1c4fa806ea990cfdd5de2b0b8c68ae20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/e3ba1a2f1c4fa806ea990cfdd5de2b0b8c68ae20"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/7760214fb468ff65afd88218fc42a023f7fe3365","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMaVfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5w0QAIQQXx/rSr8/mhHps1PgpU3L\nqiaRXGxeMa9UOeXXtBpka+/5SWRF3bluoEO+wAvDzYBCvDYG3MvpryKG2cIGnyPm\nNjjhI81djaDq6oAXCIXjsRldlfGpP2jC/wSJzPZdxsxHjZjDQ67kCYEGoRVblkdj\nTddg2AodLiaK31m60ynOspdEnEHeCh0aHh5MNOfv6PB6PTzn9ej+IaAaF3hDGrWw\nzUho6XMzJpM71ttVsIeA3rcQKuBXhtUWjpge3AUlP8/MelcL/fPVB5ScAvziRIJ2\nYP+AvcKJ9HlMVexXOcfcLcUC5HjDa+fD026TEn1JubrrsU/uk/rV1iloVSNRRpjO\n5rbNGkZj+Hg+fNJIbu9uWHthled1HpL7oao7TaWK+GGVdVlzws6DMdJ1xwuYh+jQ\nnKTIU4naGF1mp9wywdIg+SAVenBRkwHmybMjl0PyQlDTrO5tO1e/n4oIAo5MhYBg\nT4exB82xdXFUZhyePIe+9NQn9BbFLgcWKyEchqzZuSvP3dwbCIE1JLdpMahk4gNX\ntiqIRpC/40EmZvtPNQHk0GIHjUsz+q+XB7s78KoqRPmMSkvb1XyHAgmgx8iadzbP\nPn8a8s7sMUz3C/GlPXTCGV+V179aTdmg5PYaqeoky3G3Fn9PzqXLNhOKDgn7N6Al\n4KdT2qmVbVV+ksDGUpwk\n=a2WN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e3ba1a2f1c4fa806ea990cfdd5de2b0b8c68ae20\nparent 4c347603162e181c721e5e2a5ca8bbff6828e23c\nauthor Hunter Lovell <40191806+hntrl@users.noreply.github.com> 1781638495 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781638495 -0700\n\nchore(code): bump langchain-quickjs to 0.2.0 (#4037)\n\nBumps the `langchain-quickjs` dependency constraint in `deepagents-code`\nfrom `>=0.1.4,<0.2.0` to `>=0.2.0,<0.3.0`. `langchain-quickjs` is the\nJavaScript REPL interpreter behind the dcode `--interpreter` flag.\n\nThe `langchain-quickjs` partner package was already released at `0.2.0`\non `main`, but the published `deepagents-code` constraint (`<0.2.0`)\nexcluded it. This bump aligns dcode with the released interpreter so\nthat, once a new `deepagents-code` is published, `/install quickjs` (and\n`dcode --install quickjs`) pulls in `langchain-quickjs` 0.2.x.","verified_at":"2026-06-16T19:34:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7760214fb468ff65afd88218fc42a023f7fe3365","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7760214fb468ff65afd88218fc42a023f7fe3365","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/7760214fb468ff65afd88218fc42a023f7fe3365/comments","author":{"login":"hntrl","id":40191806,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMTkxODA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40191806?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl","html_url":"https://github.com/hntrl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hntrl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4c347603162e181c721e5e2a5ca8bbff6828e23c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4c347603162e181c721e5e2a5ca8bbff6828e23c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4c347603162e181c721e5e2a5ca8bbff6828e23c"}]},{"sha":"4c347603162e181c721e5e2a5ca8bbff6828e23c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDRjMzQ3NjAzMTYyZTE4MWM3MjFlNWUyYTVjYThiYmZmNjgyOGUyM2M","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-16T16:24:22Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-16T16:24:22Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump the uv group across 4 directories with 3 updates (#4035)\n\nBumps the uv group with 1 update in the /examples/llm-wiki directory:\n[cryptography](https://github.com/pyca/cryptography).\nBumps the uv group with 1 update in the /examples/repl_swarm directory:\n[cryptography](https://github.com/pyca/cryptography).\nBumps the uv group with 1 update in the /examples/rlm_agent directory:\n[cryptography](https://github.com/pyca/cryptography).\nBumps the uv group with 3 updates in the /libs/talon directory:\n[cryptography](https://github.com/pyca/cryptography),\n[python-multipart](https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart) and\n[starlette](https://github.com/Kludex/starlette).\n\nUpdates `cryptography` from 48.0.0 to 48.0.1\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/blob/main/CHANGELOG.rst\">cryptography's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>48.0.1 - 2026-06-09</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Updated Windows, macOS, and Linux wheels to be compiled with OpenSSL\n4.0.1.\n<p>.. _v48-0-0:<br />\n</code></pre></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/de987ce48ccfeb1abca41efa23b2bf73ec704f74\"><code>de987ce</code></a>\n48.0.1 version bump and changelog (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14996\">#14996</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/compare/48.0.0...48.0.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `cryptography` from 46.0.7 to 48.0.1\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/blob/main/CHANGELOG.rst\">cryptography's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>48.0.1 - 2026-06-09</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Updated Windows, macOS, and Linux wheels to be compiled with OpenSSL\n4.0.1.\n<p>.. _v48-0-0:<br />\n</code></pre></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/de987ce48ccfeb1abca41efa23b2bf73ec704f74\"><code>de987ce</code></a>\n48.0.1 version bump and changelog (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14996\">#14996</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/compare/48.0.0...48.0.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `cryptography` from 46.0.7 to 48.0.1\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/blob/main/CHANGELOG.rst\">cryptography's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>48.0.1 - 2026-06-09</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Updated Windows, macOS, and Linux wheels to be compiled with OpenSSL\n4.0.1.\n<p>.. _v48-0-0:<br />\n</code></pre></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/de987ce48ccfeb1abca41efa23b2bf73ec704f74\"><code>de987ce</code></a>\n48.0.1 version bump and changelog (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14996\">#14996</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/compare/48.0.0...48.0.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `cryptography` from 48.0.0 to 48.0.1\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/blob/main/CHANGELOG.rst\">cryptography's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>48.0.1 - 2026-06-09</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Updated Windows, macOS, and Linux wheels to be compiled with OpenSSL\n4.0.1.\n<p>.. _v48-0-0:<br />\n</code></pre></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/de987ce48ccfeb1abca41efa23b2bf73ec704f74\"><code>de987ce</code></a>\n48.0.1 version bump and changelog (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14996\">#14996</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/compare/48.0.0...48.0.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `python-multipart` from 0.0.30 to 0.0.31\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/releases\">python-multipart's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Version 0.0.31</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Speed up multipart header parsing and callback dispatch by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/pull/295\">Kludex/python-multipart#295</a></li>\n<li>Bound header field name size before validating by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/pull/296\">Kludex/python-multipart#296</a></li>\n<li>Validate Content-Length is non-negative in parse_form by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/pull/297\">Kludex/python-multipart#297</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/compare/0.0.30...0.0.31\">https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/compare/0.0.30...0.0.31</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">python-multipart's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.0.31 (2026-06-04)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Speed up multipart header parsing and callback dispatch <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/pull/295\">#295</a>.</li>\n<li>Bound header field name size before validating <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/pull/296\">#296</a>.</li>\n<li>Validate <code>Content-Length</code> is non-negative in\n<code>parse_form</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/pull/297\">#297</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/commit/4cffc68a165f7a6f6b7756ce006fabf07a05b7a4\"><code>4cffc68</code></a>\nVersion 0.0.31 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/issues/298\">#298</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/commit/c814948acf509cef7881fa75c969969b19239bbf\"><code>c814948</code></a>\nReject negative <code>Content-Length</code> in <code>parse_form</code>\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/issues/297\">#297</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/commit/6b837d47bc68826ed5cbbcb50c6c6a6093444494\"><code>6b837d4</code></a>\nBound header field name size before validating (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/issues/296\">#296</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/commit/e0c4f9df2e737d1663fbbdd6563f80613a2089f9\"><code>e0c4f9d</code></a>\nBump the github-actions group with 3 updates (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/issues/294\">#294</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/commit/b8a01bb683e8e8675fdb5d831b206a478c8215aa\"><code>b8a01bb</code></a>\nBump the python-packages group with 3 updates (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/issues/293\">#293</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/commit/6732164f30c58e28589a1e22213d2f6b8c6bad9f\"><code>6732164</code></a>\nSpeed up multipart header parsing and callback dispatch (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/issues/295\">#295</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/compare/0.0.30...0.0.31\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `starlette` from 1.2.1 to 1.3.1\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/releases\">starlette's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Version 1.3.1</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Use <code>StarletteDeprecationWarning</code> instead of\n<code>DeprecationWarning</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3119\">Kludex/starlette#3119</a></li>\n<li>Enforce <code>max_fields</code> and <code>max_part_size</code> in\n<code>FormParser</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3329\">Kludex/starlette#3329</a></li>\n<li>Enforce <code>FormParser</code> limits in parser callbacks by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3331\">Kludex/starlette#3331</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.3.0...1.3.1\">https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.3.0...1.3.1</a></p>\n<h2>Version 1.3.0</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Clamp oversized suffix ranges in <code>FileResponse</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jiyujie2006\"><code>@​jiyujie2006</code></a> in\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3307\">Kludex/starlette#3307</a></li>\n<li>Catch <code>OSError</code> alongside <code>MultiPartException</code>\nwhen closing temp files by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/N3XT3R1337\"><code>@​N3XT3R1337</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3191\">Kludex/starlette#3191</a></li>\n<li>Add <code>httpx2</code> to the <code>full</code> extra by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3323\">Kludex/starlette#3323</a></li>\n<li>Adjust testclient typing and warnings by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/waketzheng\"><code>@​waketzheng</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3322\">Kludex/starlette#3322</a></li>\n<li>Fix IndexError in URL.replace() on a URL with no authority by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/LeSingh1\"><code>@​LeSingh1</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3317\">Kludex/starlette#3317</a></li>\n<li>Annotate URLPath protocol parameter with Literal by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Chang-LeHung\"><code>@​Chang-LeHung</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3285\">Kludex/starlette#3285</a></li>\n<li>avoid collapsing exception groups from user code by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/graingert\"><code>@​graingert</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/2830\">Kludex/starlette#2830</a></li>\n<li>Use <code>removeprefix</code> to strip weak ETag indicator in\n<code>is_not_modified</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/gnosyslambda\"><code>@​gnosyslambda</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3193\">Kludex/starlette#3193</a></li>\n<li>Build <code>request.url</code> from structured components by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3326\">Kludex/starlette#3326</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>New Contributors</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jiyujie2006\"><code>@​jiyujie2006</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3307\">Kludex/starlette#3307</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/N3XT3R1337\"><code>@​N3XT3R1337</code></a> made\ntheir first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3191\">Kludex/starlette#3191</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/leestana01\"><code>@​leestana01</code></a> made\ntheir first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3319\">Kludex/starlette#3319</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/LeSingh1\"><code>@​LeSingh1</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3317\">Kludex/starlette#3317</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/EmmanuelNiyonshuti\"><code>@​EmmanuelNiyonshuti</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3204\">Kludex/starlette#3204</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Chang-LeHung\"><code>@​Chang-LeHung</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3285\">Kludex/starlette#3285</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/gnosyslambda\"><code>@​gnosyslambda</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3193\">Kludex/starlette#3193</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.2.1...1.3.0\">https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.2.1...1.3.0</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/blob/main/docs/release-notes.md\">starlette's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>1.3.1 (June 12, 2026)</h2>\n<h4>Fixed</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Enforce <code>max_fields</code> and <code>max_part_size</code> in\n<code>FormParser</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3329\">#3329</a>.</li>\n<li>Enforce <code>FormParser</code> limits in parser callbacks <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3331\">#3331</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>1.3.0 (June 11, 2026)</h2>\n<h4>Added</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Add <code>httpx2</code> to the <code>full</code> extra <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3323\">#3323</a>.</li>\n<li>Annotate the <code>URLPath</code> <code>protocol</code> parameter\nwith <code>Literal</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3285\">#3285</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Fixed</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Build <code>request.url</code> from structured components <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3326\">#3326</a>.</li>\n<li>Clamp oversized suffix ranges in <code>FileResponse</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3307\">#3307</a>.</li>\n<li>Catch <code>OSError</code> alongside <code>MultiPartException</code>\nwhen closing temp files <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3191\">#3191</a>.</li>\n<li>Avoid collapsing exception groups raised from user code <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/2830\">#2830</a>.</li>\n<li>Use <code>removeprefix</code> to strip the weak <code>ETag</code>\nindicator in <code>is_not_modified</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3193\">#3193</a>.</li>\n<li>Fix <code>IndexError</code> in <code>URL.replace()</code> on a URL\nwith no authority <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3317\">#3317</a>.</li>\n<li>Adjust <code>testclient</code> typing and warnings <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3322\">#3322</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/8ebffd0678570ddd5d5bb11c6f3c3c7fd4682ab9\"><code>8ebffd0</code></a>\nVersion 1.3.1 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3330\">#3330</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/25b8e179d8d7ed86769c02f648772dd5fb43dc3c\"><code>25b8e17</code></a>\nEnforce <code>FormParser</code> limits in parser callbacks (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3331\">#3331</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/dba1c4babc4f99ad2622bb913d87045775dda735\"><code>dba1c4b</code></a>\nEnforce <code>max_fields</code> and <code>max_part_size</code> in\n<code>FormParser</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3329\">#3329</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/45e51dcf99f3a270b0bcec1aec5410b4345863a9\"><code>45e51dc</code></a>\nUse <code>StarletteDeprecationWarning</code> instead of\n<code>DeprecationWarning</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3119\">#3119</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/5f8610c386e13de1d80d36efa961e1486a1d2d01\"><code>5f8610c</code></a>\nVersion 1.3.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3327\">#3327</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/167b5850e809f38b27fbfed62d58bf6442855975\"><code>167b585</code></a>\nBuild <code>request.url</code> from structured components (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3326\">#3326</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/37309255b4c1b9c381a2d24a1eaf83100984a16a\"><code>3730925</code></a>\nUse <code>removeprefix</code> to strip weak ETag indicator in\n<code>is_not_modified</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3193\">#3193</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/e6f7ad1ab85efb27ab7910d8007b3f4531f7b083\"><code>e6f7ad1</code></a>\navoid collapsing exception groups from user code (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/2830\">#2830</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/115228fcdca0e0ef5bf4a95a40ddce5a9fced428\"><code>115228f</code></a>\nAnnotate URLPath protocol parameter with Literal (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3285\">#3285</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/113f193a34353c9153857028c1074351d22fad07\"><code>113f193</code></a>\ndocs: replace inline ASGI server list with link to canonical implemen…\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3204\">#3204</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.2.1...1.3.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> major version` will close this\ngroup update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific\ndependency's major version (unless you unignore this specific\ndependency's major version or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> minor version` will close this\ngroup update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific\ndependency's minor version (unless you unignore this specific\ndependency's minor version or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name>` will close this group update PR\nand stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific dependency\n(unless you unignore this specific dependency or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name>` will remove all of the ignore\nconditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name> <ignore condition>` will\nremove the ignore condition of the specified dependency and ignore\nconditions\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","tree":{"sha":"5352df6915bd43b680f30271c39661088be9d534","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/5352df6915bd43b680f30271c39661088be9d534"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/4c347603162e181c721e5e2a5ca8bbff6828e23c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMXi2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9ZoQAJNd0e+R6YQjzKwt1B4Q7GKR\n29o8uNBeA8QhqTud+oE9tOLyWy55qj1cvOV/z9jqWceOA7wuKaUR76C4HovW4pNH\nlSp2THrartFxno6peyLqvpPc9KCqntai5GClcyS95dugcbxAo7GazwjVkRNCjc4M\nVwlg/1jFiXwI2pyyAl3NwdwqeAYkILI6MoAs9Qs/jrmEoj/3bwCg7TAlt4JX4MCU\nb3U2l5W2lefi6UgrDP0DgH871FvRE2+WS4luJjE9xVTLnMvmA2/dMmBcz6koIJv6\nUlLsuDsbl+LSF8vOkKKqz08FHLTRyURAmLxg9yxiUcXfTcb9FeYyTFltcReB8EDA\nngCQGUFTe/aNJR1Zo30XagcaQ2ETiAPuSmQXlFy+LSuocDnmblwTNEWW2MLHrl1N\ncDp2HJJDMSAs9xMYyFWByv3rxgHqglJvt55hNxaJQx1Yh+jZbuyd2PDiDEAy7MRC\noMPwoc2M7USAfUMDoFcETMu4eiqrqgWy0AZn7PNQum/f7pwsFD4MqRyoRz0mrHL7\nC/K9G3RLcPqTiIkOhPBoTrKnM/PfxEU4h1nr/WOMU/g4gKBvsHdx8x3Pr7e94r1J\n9AVyMJxEy/B4Jwe6BU64GfavKk+hy0chj9GfBMPSwZ4m+Q0QdtyhqCLjsyTVX5OB\n/aBKh2qyMiVh8T5Qr2jZ\n=sVNa\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5352df6915bd43b680f30271c39661088be9d534\nparent fecede5cb7c883c79f96ad8cb042c809395be59d\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1781627062 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781627062 -0400\n\nchore(deps): bump the uv group across 4 directories with 3 updates (#4035)\n\nBumps the uv group with 1 update in the /examples/llm-wiki directory:\n[cryptography](https://github.com/pyca/cryptography).\nBumps the uv group with 1 update in the /examples/repl_swarm directory:\n[cryptography](https://github.com/pyca/cryptography).\nBumps the uv group with 1 update in the /examples/rlm_agent directory:\n[cryptography](https://github.com/pyca/cryptography).\nBumps the uv group with 3 updates in the /libs/talon directory:\n[cryptography](https://github.com/pyca/cryptography),\n[python-multipart](https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart) and\n[starlette](https://github.com/Kludex/starlette).\n\nUpdates `cryptography` from 48.0.0 to 48.0.1\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/blob/main/CHANGELOG.rst\">cryptography's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>48.0.1 - 2026-06-09</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Updated Windows, macOS, and Linux wheels to be compiled with OpenSSL\n4.0.1.\n<p>.. _v48-0-0:<br />\n</code></pre></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/de987ce48ccfeb1abca41efa23b2bf73ec704f74\"><code>de987ce</code></a>\n48.0.1 version bump and changelog (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14996\">#14996</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/compare/48.0.0...48.0.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `cryptography` from 46.0.7 to 48.0.1\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/blob/main/CHANGELOG.rst\">cryptography's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>48.0.1 - 2026-06-09</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Updated Windows, macOS, and Linux wheels to be compiled with OpenSSL\n4.0.1.\n<p>.. _v48-0-0:<br />\n</code></pre></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/de987ce48ccfeb1abca41efa23b2bf73ec704f74\"><code>de987ce</code></a>\n48.0.1 version bump and changelog (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14996\">#14996</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/compare/48.0.0...48.0.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `cryptography` from 46.0.7 to 48.0.1\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/blob/main/CHANGELOG.rst\">cryptography's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>48.0.1 - 2026-06-09</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Updated Windows, macOS, and Linux wheels to be compiled with OpenSSL\n4.0.1.\n<p>.. _v48-0-0:<br />\n</code></pre></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/de987ce48ccfeb1abca41efa23b2bf73ec704f74\"><code>de987ce</code></a>\n48.0.1 version bump and changelog (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14996\">#14996</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/compare/48.0.0...48.0.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `cryptography` from 48.0.0 to 48.0.1\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/blob/main/CHANGELOG.rst\">cryptography's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>48.0.1 - 2026-06-09</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Updated Windows, macOS, and Linux wheels to be compiled with OpenSSL\n4.0.1.\n<p>.. _v48-0-0:<br />\n</code></pre></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/de987ce48ccfeb1abca41efa23b2bf73ec704f74\"><code>de987ce</code></a>\n48.0.1 version bump and changelog (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14996\">#14996</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/compare/48.0.0...48.0.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `python-multipart` from 0.0.30 to 0.0.31\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/releases\">python-multipart's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Version 0.0.31</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Speed up multipart header parsing and callback dispatch by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/pull/295\">Kludex/python-multipart#295</a></li>\n<li>Bound header field name size before validating by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/pull/296\">Kludex/python-multipart#296</a></li>\n<li>Validate Content-Length is non-negative in parse_form by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/pull/297\">Kludex/python-multipart#297</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/compare/0.0.30...0.0.31\">https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/compare/0.0.30...0.0.31</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">python-multipart's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.0.31 (2026-06-04)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Speed up multipart header parsing and callback dispatch <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/pull/295\">#295</a>.</li>\n<li>Bound header field name size before validating <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/pull/296\">#296</a>.</li>\n<li>Validate <code>Content-Length</code> is non-negative in\n<code>parse_form</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/pull/297\">#297</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/commit/4cffc68a165f7a6f6b7756ce006fabf07a05b7a4\"><code>4cffc68</code></a>\nVersion 0.0.31 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/issues/298\">#298</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/commit/c814948acf509cef7881fa75c969969b19239bbf\"><code>c814948</code></a>\nReject negative <code>Content-Length</code> in <code>parse_form</code>\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/issues/297\">#297</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/commit/6b837d47bc68826ed5cbbcb50c6c6a6093444494\"><code>6b837d4</code></a>\nBound header field name size before validating (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/issues/296\">#296</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/commit/e0c4f9df2e737d1663fbbdd6563f80613a2089f9\"><code>e0c4f9d</code></a>\nBump the github-actions group with 3 updates (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/issues/294\">#294</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/commit/b8a01bb683e8e8675fdb5d831b206a478c8215aa\"><code>b8a01bb</code></a>\nBump the python-packages group with 3 updates (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/issues/293\">#293</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/commit/6732164f30c58e28589a1e22213d2f6b8c6bad9f\"><code>6732164</code></a>\nSpeed up multipart header parsing and callback dispatch (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/issues/295\">#295</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/compare/0.0.30...0.0.31\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `starlette` from 1.2.1 to 1.3.1\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/releases\">starlette's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Version 1.3.1</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Use <code>StarletteDeprecationWarning</code> instead of\n<code>DeprecationWarning</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3119\">Kludex/starlette#3119</a></li>\n<li>Enforce <code>max_fields</code> and <code>max_part_size</code> in\n<code>FormParser</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3329\">Kludex/starlette#3329</a></li>\n<li>Enforce <code>FormParser</code> limits in parser callbacks by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3331\">Kludex/starlette#3331</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.3.0...1.3.1\">https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.3.0...1.3.1</a></p>\n<h2>Version 1.3.0</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Clamp oversized suffix ranges in <code>FileResponse</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jiyujie2006\"><code>@​jiyujie2006</code></a> in\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3307\">Kludex/starlette#3307</a></li>\n<li>Catch <code>OSError</code> alongside <code>MultiPartException</code>\nwhen closing temp files by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/N3XT3R1337\"><code>@​N3XT3R1337</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3191\">Kludex/starlette#3191</a></li>\n<li>Add <code>httpx2</code> to the <code>full</code> extra by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3323\">Kludex/starlette#3323</a></li>\n<li>Adjust testclient typing and warnings by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/waketzheng\"><code>@​waketzheng</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3322\">Kludex/starlette#3322</a></li>\n<li>Fix IndexError in URL.replace() on a URL with no authority by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/LeSingh1\"><code>@​LeSingh1</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3317\">Kludex/starlette#3317</a></li>\n<li>Annotate URLPath protocol parameter with Literal by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Chang-LeHung\"><code>@​Chang-LeHung</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3285\">Kludex/starlette#3285</a></li>\n<li>avoid collapsing exception groups from user code by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/graingert\"><code>@​graingert</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/2830\">Kludex/starlette#2830</a></li>\n<li>Use <code>removeprefix</code> to strip weak ETag indicator in\n<code>is_not_modified</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/gnosyslambda\"><code>@​gnosyslambda</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3193\">Kludex/starlette#3193</a></li>\n<li>Build <code>request.url</code> from structured components by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3326\">Kludex/starlette#3326</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>New Contributors</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jiyujie2006\"><code>@​jiyujie2006</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3307\">Kludex/starlette#3307</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/N3XT3R1337\"><code>@​N3XT3R1337</code></a> made\ntheir first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3191\">Kludex/starlette#3191</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/leestana01\"><code>@​leestana01</code></a> made\ntheir first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3319\">Kludex/starlette#3319</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/LeSingh1\"><code>@​LeSingh1</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3317\">Kludex/starlette#3317</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/EmmanuelNiyonshuti\"><code>@​EmmanuelNiyonshuti</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3204\">Kludex/starlette#3204</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Chang-LeHung\"><code>@​Chang-LeHung</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3285\">Kludex/starlette#3285</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/gnosyslambda\"><code>@​gnosyslambda</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3193\">Kludex/starlette#3193</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.2.1...1.3.0\">https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.2.1...1.3.0</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/blob/main/docs/release-notes.md\">starlette's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>1.3.1 (June 12, 2026)</h2>\n<h4>Fixed</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Enforce <code>max_fields</code> and <code>max_part_size</code> in\n<code>FormParser</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3329\">#3329</a>.</li>\n<li>Enforce <code>FormParser</code> limits in parser callbacks <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3331\">#3331</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>1.3.0 (June 11, 2026)</h2>\n<h4>Added</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Add <code>httpx2</code> to the <code>full</code> extra <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3323\">#3323</a>.</li>\n<li>Annotate the <code>URLPath</code> <code>protocol</code> parameter\nwith <code>Literal</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3285\">#3285</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Fixed</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Build <code>request.url</code> from structured components <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3326\">#3326</a>.</li>\n<li>Clamp oversized suffix ranges in <code>FileResponse</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3307\">#3307</a>.</li>\n<li>Catch <code>OSError</code> alongside <code>MultiPartException</code>\nwhen closing temp files <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3191\">#3191</a>.</li>\n<li>Avoid collapsing exception groups raised from user code <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/2830\">#2830</a>.</li>\n<li>Use <code>removeprefix</code> to strip the weak <code>ETag</code>\nindicator in <code>is_not_modified</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3193\">#3193</a>.</li>\n<li>Fix <code>IndexError</code> in <code>URL.replace()</code> on a URL\nwith no authority <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3317\">#3317</a>.</li>\n<li>Adjust <code>testclient</code> typing and warnings <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3322\">#3322</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/8ebffd0678570ddd5d5bb11c6f3c3c7fd4682ab9\"><code>8ebffd0</code></a>\nVersion 1.3.1 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3330\">#3330</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/25b8e179d8d7ed86769c02f648772dd5fb43dc3c\"><code>25b8e17</code></a>\nEnforce <code>FormParser</code> limits in parser callbacks (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3331\">#3331</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/dba1c4babc4f99ad2622bb913d87045775dda735\"><code>dba1c4b</code></a>\nEnforce <code>max_fields</code> and <code>max_part_size</code> in\n<code>FormParser</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3329\">#3329</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/45e51dcf99f3a270b0bcec1aec5410b4345863a9\"><code>45e51dc</code></a>\nUse <code>StarletteDeprecationWarning</code> instead of\n<code>DeprecationWarning</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3119\">#3119</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/5f8610c386e13de1d80d36efa961e1486a1d2d01\"><code>5f8610c</code></a>\nVersion 1.3.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3327\">#3327</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/167b5850e809f38b27fbfed62d58bf6442855975\"><code>167b585</code></a>\nBuild <code>request.url</code> from structured components (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3326\">#3326</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/37309255b4c1b9c381a2d24a1eaf83100984a16a\"><code>3730925</code></a>\nUse <code>removeprefix</code> to strip weak ETag indicator in\n<code>is_not_modified</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3193\">#3193</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/e6f7ad1ab85efb27ab7910d8007b3f4531f7b083\"><code>e6f7ad1</code></a>\navoid collapsing exception groups from user code (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/2830\">#2830</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/115228fcdca0e0ef5bf4a95a40ddce5a9fced428\"><code>115228f</code></a>\nAnnotate URLPath protocol parameter with Literal (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3285\">#3285</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/113f193a34353c9153857028c1074351d22fad07\"><code>113f193</code></a>\ndocs: replace inline ASGI server list with link to canonical implemen…\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3204\">#3204</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.2.1...1.3.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> major version` will close this\ngroup update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific\ndependency's major version (unless you unignore this specific\ndependency's major version or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> minor version` will close this\ngroup update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific\ndependency's minor version (unless you unignore this specific\ndependency's minor version or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name>` will close this group update PR\nand stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific dependency\n(unless you unignore this specific dependency or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name>` will remove all of the ignore\nconditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name> <ignore condition>` will\nremove the ignore condition of the specified dependency and ignore\nconditions\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","verified_at":"2026-06-16T16:24:22Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4c347603162e181c721e5e2a5ca8bbff6828e23c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4c347603162e181c721e5e2a5ca8bbff6828e23c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4c347603162e181c721e5e2a5ca8bbff6828e23c/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"fecede5cb7c883c79f96ad8cb042c809395be59d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/fecede5cb7c883c79f96ad8cb042c809395be59d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/fecede5cb7c883c79f96ad8cb042c809395be59d"}]},{"sha":"fecede5cb7c883c79f96ad8cb042c809395be59d","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGZlY2VkZTVjYjdjODgzYzc5Zjk2YWQ4Y2IwNDJjODA5Mzk1YmU1OWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-16T16:24:05Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-16T16:24:05Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump the uv group across 5 directories with 3 updates (#4015)\n\nBumps the uv group with 2 updates in the /examples/async-subagent-server\ndirectory: [cryptography](https://github.com/pyca/cryptography) and\n[starlette](https://github.com/Kludex/starlette).\nBumps the uv group with 1 update in the /examples/llm-wiki directory:\n[cryptography](https://github.com/pyca/cryptography).\nBumps the uv group with 1 update in the /examples/repl_swarm directory:\n[cryptography](https://github.com/pyca/cryptography).\nBumps the uv group with 1 update in the /examples/rlm_agent directory:\n[cryptography](https://github.com/pyca/cryptography).\nBumps the uv group with 3 updates in the /libs/talon directory:\n[cryptography](https://github.com/pyca/cryptography),\n[starlette](https://github.com/Kludex/starlette) and\n[python-multipart](https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart).\n\nUpdates `cryptography` from 46.0.7 to 48.0.1\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/blob/main/CHANGELOG.rst\">cryptography's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>48.0.1 - 2026-06-09</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Updated Windows, macOS, and Linux wheels to be compiled with OpenSSL\n4.0.1.\n<p>.. _v48-0-0:</p>\n<p>48.0.0 - 2026-05-04<br />\n</code></pre></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Support for Python 3.8 has\nbeen removed.\n<code>cryptography</code> now requires Python 3.9 or later.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Loading an X.509 CRL whose\ninner\n<code>TBSCertList.signature</code> algorithm does not match the outer\n<code>signatureAlgorithm</code> now raises <code>ValueError</code>.\nPreviously, such CRLs\nwere parsed successfully and only rejected during signature\nvalidation.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Added support for\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mlkem</code> and\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mldsa</code> when using OpenSSL\n3.5.0 or\nlater, in addition to the existing AWS-LC and BoringSSL support. This\nmeans\npost-quantum algorithms are now available to users of our wheels.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Note:</strong> Going forward, we do not guarantee that all\nfunctionality\nin <code>cryptography</code> will be available when building against\nOpenSSL. See :doc:<code>/statements/state-of-openssl</code> for more\ninformation.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>.. _v47-0-0:</p>\n<p>47.0.0 - 2026-04-24</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Support for Python 3.8 is deprecated and will be removed in the next\n  ``cryptography`` release.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for binary elliptic curves\n  (``SECT*`` classes) has been removed. These curves are rarely used and\n  have additional security considerations that make them undesirable.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for OpenSSL 1.1.x has been\nremoved.\nOpenSSL 3.0.0 or later is now required. LibreSSL, BoringSSL, and AWS-LC\n  continue to be supported.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Dropped support for LibreSSL &lt; 4.1.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Loading keys with unsupported algorithms\nor\n  keys with unsupported explicit curve encodings now raises\n  :class:`~cryptography.exceptions.UnsupportedAlgorithm` instead of\n  ``ValueError``. This change affects\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_public_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_public_key`,\n  and :meth:`~cryptography.x509.Certificate.public_key` when called on\n  certificates with unsupported public key algorithms.\n&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt; \n</code></pre>\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/de987ce48ccfeb1abca41efa23b2bf73ec704f74\"><code>de987ce</code></a>\n48.0.1 version bump and changelog (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14996\">#14996</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/8e03e30e3aae01632a697e903e3593c924f0139d\"><code>8e03e30</code></a>\nbump for 48.0.0 release (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14796\">#14796</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/295e0d254ef31ab864730aa41312ec355416ee71\"><code>295e0d2</code></a>\nAdd AGENTS.md with CLAUDE.md symlink (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14794\">#14794</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/104a2de19e268a433e6da92be9cb872dcf0003c8\"><code>104a2de</code></a>\nBump BoringSSL, OpenSSL, AWS-LC in CI (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14793\">#14793</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/67ec1e51988195e17993d2edef5258b27509b926\"><code>67ec1e5</code></a>\ncall check_length early on AesSiv::encrypt (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14792\">#14792</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/b2da57a0d9e4bfd2b95364299091a18f74127b26\"><code>b2da57a</code></a>\nchangelog for mldsa/mlkem for openssl (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14791\">#14791</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/3cf44adee25c368d4a136e072fa9f80465d91eb0\"><code>3cf44ad</code></a>\nML-KEM OpenSSL support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14781\">#14781</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/2e31639666766f846fbab2c605879db0fa64fe83\"><code>2e31639</code></a>\nML-DSA OpenSSL support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14773\">#14773</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/5affe5a286a986fdf512c4a5cb280d28a96c10e3\"><code>5affe5a</code></a>\nfix rust nightly clippy (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14790\">#14790</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/2e73ca448eaf64b6f0d4ffbb794cf96170cef5ec\"><code>2e73ca4</code></a>\nbump rust-openssl dep and update EcPoint::mul_generator to\nmul_generator2 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/1\">#1</a>...</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/compare/46.0.7...48.0.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `starlette` from 1.0.1 to 1.3.1\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/releases\">starlette's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Version 1.3.1</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Use <code>StarletteDeprecationWarning</code> instead of\n<code>DeprecationWarning</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3119\">Kludex/starlette#3119</a></li>\n<li>Enforce <code>max_fields</code> and <code>max_part_size</code> in\n<code>FormParser</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3329\">Kludex/starlette#3329</a></li>\n<li>Enforce <code>FormParser</code> limits in parser callbacks by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3331\">Kludex/starlette#3331</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.3.0...1.3.1\">https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.3.0...1.3.1</a></p>\n<h2>Version 1.3.0</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Clamp oversized suffix ranges in <code>FileResponse</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jiyujie2006\"><code>@​jiyujie2006</code></a> in\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3307\">Kludex/starlette#3307</a></li>\n<li>Catch <code>OSError</code> alongside <code>MultiPartException</code>\nwhen closing temp files by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/N3XT3R1337\"><code>@​N3XT3R1337</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3191\">Kludex/starlette#3191</a></li>\n<li>Add <code>httpx2</code> to the <code>full</code> extra by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3323\">Kludex/starlette#3323</a></li>\n<li>Adjust testclient typing and warnings by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/waketzheng\"><code>@​waketzheng</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3322\">Kludex/starlette#3322</a></li>\n<li>Fix IndexError in URL.replace() on a URL with no authority by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/LeSingh1\"><code>@​LeSingh1</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3317\">Kludex/starlette#3317</a></li>\n<li>Annotate URLPath protocol parameter with Literal by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Chang-LeHung\"><code>@​Chang-LeHung</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3285\">Kludex/starlette#3285</a></li>\n<li>avoid collapsing exception groups from user code by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/graingert\"><code>@​graingert</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/2830\">Kludex/starlette#2830</a></li>\n<li>Use <code>removeprefix</code> to strip weak ETag indicator in\n<code>is_not_modified</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/gnosyslambda\"><code>@​gnosyslambda</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3193\">Kludex/starlette#3193</a></li>\n<li>Build <code>request.url</code> from structured components by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3326\">Kludex/starlette#3326</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>New Contributors</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jiyujie2006\"><code>@​jiyujie2006</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3307\">Kludex/starlette#3307</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/N3XT3R1337\"><code>@​N3XT3R1337</code></a> made\ntheir first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3191\">Kludex/starlette#3191</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/leestana01\"><code>@​leestana01</code></a> made\ntheir first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3319\">Kludex/starlette#3319</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/LeSingh1\"><code>@​LeSingh1</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3317\">Kludex/starlette#3317</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/EmmanuelNiyonshuti\"><code>@​EmmanuelNiyonshuti</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3204\">Kludex/starlette#3204</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Chang-LeHung\"><code>@​Chang-LeHung</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3285\">Kludex/starlette#3285</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/gnosyslambda\"><code>@​gnosyslambda</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3193\">Kludex/starlette#3193</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.2.1...1.3.0\">https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.2.1...1.3.0</a></p>\n<h2>Version 1.2.1</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Use <code>httpx2</code> for type checking in the\n<code>testclient</code> module by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/leifwar\"><code>@​leifwar</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3304\">Kludex/starlette#3304</a></li>\n<li>Add assert error for requires() when request param is not Request\ntype by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/KeeganOP\"><code>@​KeeganOP</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3298\">Kludex/starlette#3298</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>New Contributors</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/leifwar\"><code>@​leifwar</code></a> made\ntheir first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3304\">Kludex/starlette#3304</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/diskeu\"><code>@​diskeu</code></a> made\ntheir first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3243\">Kludex/starlette#3243</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/KeeganOP\"><code>@​KeeganOP</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3298\">Kludex/starlette#3298</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.2.0...1.2.1\">https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.2.0...1.2.1</a></p>\n<h2>Version 1.2.0</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Support httpx2 in the test client by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3291\">Kludex/starlette#3291</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.1.0...1.2.0\">https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.1.0...1.2.0</a></p>\n<h2>Version 1.1.0</h2>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/blob/main/docs/release-notes.md\">starlette's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>1.3.1 (June 12, 2026)</h2>\n<h4>Fixed</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Enforce <code>max_fields</code> and <code>max_part_size</code> in\n<code>FormParser</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3329\">#3329</a>.</li>\n<li>Enforce <code>FormParser</code> limits in parser callbacks <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3331\">#3331</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>1.3.0 (June 11, 2026)</h2>\n<h4>Added</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Add <code>httpx2</code> to the <code>full</code> extra <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3323\">#3323</a>.</li>\n<li>Annotate the <code>URLPath</code> <code>protocol</code> parameter\nwith <code>Literal</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3285\">#3285</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Fixed</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Build <code>request.url</code> from structured components <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3326\">#3326</a>.</li>\n<li>Clamp oversized suffix ranges in <code>FileResponse</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3307\">#3307</a>.</li>\n<li>Catch <code>OSError</code> alongside <code>MultiPartException</code>\nwhen closing temp files <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3191\">#3191</a>.</li>\n<li>Avoid collapsing exception groups raised from user code <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/2830\">#2830</a>.</li>\n<li>Use <code>removeprefix</code> to strip the weak <code>ETag</code>\nindicator in <code>is_not_modified</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3193\">#3193</a>.</li>\n<li>Fix <code>IndexError</code> in <code>URL.replace()</code> on a URL\nwith no authority <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3317\">#3317</a>.</li>\n<li>Adjust <code>testclient</code> typing and warnings <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3322\">#3322</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>1.2.1 (May 31, 2026)</h2>\n<h4>Fixed</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Use <code>httpx2</code> for type checking in the\n<code>testclient</code> module <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3304\">#3304</a>.</li>\n<li>Add assert error for <code>requires()</code> when the request\nparameter is not a <code>Request</code> type <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3298\">#3298</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>1.2.0 (May 28, 2026)</h2>\n<h4>Added</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Support httpx2 in the test client <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3291\">#3291</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>1.1.0 (May 23, 2026)</h2>\n<h4>Added</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Use <code>&quot;application/octet-stream&quot;</code> as the\n<code>FileResponse</code> media type fallback <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3283\">#3283</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Fixed</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Only dispatch standard HTTP verbs in <code>HTTPEndpoint</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3286\">#3286</a>.</li>\n<li>Reject absolute paths in <code>StaticFiles.lookup_path</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3287\">#3287</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/8ebffd0678570ddd5d5bb11c6f3c3c7fd4682ab9\"><code>8ebffd0</code></a>\nVersion 1.3.1 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3330\">#3330</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/25b8e179d8d7ed86769c02f648772dd5fb43dc3c\"><code>25b8e17</code></a>\nEnforce <code>FormParser</code> limits in parser callbacks (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3331\">#3331</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/dba1c4babc4f99ad2622bb913d87045775dda735\"><code>dba1c4b</code></a>\nEnforce <code>max_fields</code> and <code>max_part_size</code> in\n<code>FormParser</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3329\">#3329</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/45e51dcf99f3a270b0bcec1aec5410b4345863a9\"><code>45e51dc</code></a>\nUse <code>StarletteDeprecationWarning</code> instead of\n<code>DeprecationWarning</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3119\">#3119</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/5f8610c386e13de1d80d36efa961e1486a1d2d01\"><code>5f8610c</code></a>\nVersion 1.3.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3327\">#3327</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/167b5850e809f38b27fbfed62d58bf6442855975\"><code>167b585</code></a>\nBuild <code>request.url</code> from structured components (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3326\">#3326</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/37309255b4c1b9c381a2d24a1eaf83100984a16a\"><code>3730925</code></a>\nUse <code>removeprefix</code> to strip weak ETag indicator in\n<code>is_not_modified</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3193\">#3193</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/e6f7ad1ab85efb27ab7910d8007b3f4531f7b083\"><code>e6f7ad1</code></a>\navoid collapsing exception groups from user code (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/2830\">#2830</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/115228fcdca0e0ef5bf4a95a40ddce5a9fced428\"><code>115228f</code></a>\nAnnotate URLPath protocol parameter with Literal (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3285\">#3285</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/113f193a34353c9153857028c1074351d22fad07\"><code>113f193</code></a>\ndocs: replace inline ASGI server list with link to canonical implemen…\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3204\">#3204</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.0.1...1.3.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `cryptography` from 48.0.0 to 48.0.1\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/blob/main/CHANGELOG.rst\">cryptography's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>48.0.1 - 2026-06-09</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Updated Windows, macOS, and Linux wheels to be compiled with OpenSSL\n4.0.1.\n<p>.. _v48-0-0:</p>\n<p>48.0.0 - 2026-05-04<br />\n</code></pre></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Support for Python 3.8 has\nbeen removed.\n<code>cryptography</code> now requires Python 3.9 or later.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Loading an X.509 CRL whose\ninner\n<code>TBSCertList.signature</code> algorithm does not match the outer\n<code>signatureAlgorithm</code> now raises <code>ValueError</code>.\nPreviously, such CRLs\nwere parsed successfully and only rejected during signature\nvalidation.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Added support for\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mlkem</code> and\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mldsa</code> when using OpenSSL\n3.5.0 or\nlater, in addition to the existing AWS-LC and BoringSSL support. This\nmeans\npost-quantum algorithms are now available to users of our wheels.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Note:</strong> Going forward, we do not guarantee that all\nfunctionality\nin <code>cryptography</code> will be available when building against\nOpenSSL. See :doc:<code>/statements/state-of-openssl</code> for more\ninformation.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>.. _v47-0-0:</p>\n<p>47.0.0 - 2026-04-24</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Support for Python 3.8 is deprecated and will be removed in the next\n  ``cryptography`` release.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for binary elliptic curves\n  (``SECT*`` classes) has been removed. These curves are rarely used and\n  have additional security considerations that make them undesirable.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for OpenSSL 1.1.x has been\nremoved.\nOpenSSL 3.0.0 or later is now required. LibreSSL, BoringSSL, and AWS-LC\n  continue to be supported.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Dropped support for LibreSSL &lt; 4.1.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Loading keys with unsupported algorithms\nor\n  keys with unsupported explicit curve encodings now raises\n  :class:`~cryptography.exceptions.UnsupportedAlgorithm` instead of\n  ``ValueError``. This change affects\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_public_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_public_key`,\n  and :meth:`~cryptography.x509.Certificate.public_key` when called on\n  certificates with unsupported public key algorithms.\n&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt; \n</code></pre>\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/de987ce48ccfeb1abca41efa23b2bf73ec704f74\"><code>de987ce</code></a>\n48.0.1 version bump and changelog (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14996\">#14996</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/8e03e30e3aae01632a697e903e3593c924f0139d\"><code>8e03e30</code></a>\nbump for 48.0.0 release (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14796\">#14796</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/295e0d254ef31ab864730aa41312ec355416ee71\"><code>295e0d2</code></a>\nAdd AGENTS.md with CLAUDE.md symlink (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14794\">#14794</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/104a2de19e268a433e6da92be9cb872dcf0003c8\"><code>104a2de</code></a>\nBump BoringSSL, OpenSSL, AWS-LC in CI (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14793\">#14793</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/67ec1e51988195e17993d2edef5258b27509b926\"><code>67ec1e5</code></a>\ncall check_length early on AesSiv::encrypt (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14792\">#14792</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/b2da57a0d9e4bfd2b95364299091a18f74127b26\"><code>b2da57a</code></a>\nchangelog for mldsa/mlkem for openssl (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14791\">#14791</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/3cf44adee25c368d4a136e072fa9f80465d91eb0\"><code>3cf44ad</code></a>\nML-KEM OpenSSL support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14781\">#14781</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/2e31639666766f846fbab2c605879db0fa64fe83\"><code>2e31639</code></a>\nML-DSA OpenSSL support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14773\">#14773</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/5affe5a286a986fdf512c4a5cb280d28a96c10e3\"><code>5affe5a</code></a>\nfix rust nightly clippy (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14790\">#14790</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/2e73ca448eaf64b6f0d4ffbb794cf96170cef5ec\"><code>2e73ca4</code></a>\nbump rust-openssl dep and update EcPoint::mul_generator to\nmul_generator2 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/1\">#1</a>...</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/compare/46.0.7...48.0.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `cryptography` from 46.0.7 to 48.0.1\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/blob/main/CHANGELOG.rst\">cryptography's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>48.0.1 - 2026-06-09</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Updated Windows, macOS, and Linux wheels to be compiled with OpenSSL\n4.0.1.\n<p>.. _v48-0-0:</p>\n<p>48.0.0 - 2026-05-04<br />\n</code></pre></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Support for Python 3.8 has\nbeen removed.\n<code>cryptography</code> now requires Python 3.9 or later.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Loading an X.509 CRL whose\ninner\n<code>TBSCertList.signature</code> algorithm does not match the outer\n<code>signatureAlgorithm</code> now raises <code>ValueError</code>.\nPreviously, such CRLs\nwere parsed successfully and only rejected during signature\nvalidation.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Added support for\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mlkem</code> and\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mldsa</code> when using OpenSSL\n3.5.0 or\nlater, in addition to the existing AWS-LC and BoringSSL support. This\nmeans\npost-quantum algorithms are now available to users of our wheels.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Note:</strong> Going forward, we do not guarantee that all\nfunctionality\nin <code>cryptography</code> will be available when building against\nOpenSSL. See :doc:<code>/statements/state-of-openssl</code> for more\ninformation.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>.. _v47-0-0:</p>\n<p>47.0.0 - 2026-04-24</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Support for Python 3.8 is deprecated and will be removed in the next\n  ``cryptography`` release.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for binary elliptic curves\n  (``SECT*`` classes) has been removed. These curves are rarely used and\n  have additional security considerations that make them undesirable.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for OpenSSL 1.1.x has been\nremoved.\nOpenSSL 3.0.0 or later is now required. LibreSSL, BoringSSL, and AWS-LC\n  continue to be supported.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Dropped support for LibreSSL &lt; 4.1.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Loading keys with unsupported algorithms\nor\n  keys with unsupported explicit curve encodings now raises\n  :class:`~cryptography.exceptions.UnsupportedAlgorithm` instead of\n  ``ValueError``. This change affects\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_public_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_public_key`,\n  and :meth:`~cryptography.x509.Certificate.public_key` when called on\n  certificates with unsupported public key algorithms.\n&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt; \n</code></pre>\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/de987ce48ccfeb1abca41efa23b2bf73ec704f74\"><code>de987ce</code></a>\n48.0.1 version bump and changelog (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14996\">#14996</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/8e03e30e3aae01632a697e903e3593c924f0139d\"><code>8e03e30</code></a>\nbump for 48.0.0 release (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14796\">#14796</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/295e0d254ef31ab864730aa41312ec355416ee71\"><code>295e0d2</code></a>\nAdd AGENTS.md with CLAUDE.md symlink (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14794\">#14794</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/104a2de19e268a433e6da92be9cb872dcf0003c8\"><code>104a2de</code></a>\nBump BoringSSL, OpenSSL, AWS-LC in CI (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14793\">#14793</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/67ec1e51988195e17993d2edef5258b27509b926\"><code>67ec1e5</code></a>\ncall check_length early on AesSiv::encrypt (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14792\">#14792</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/b2da57a0d9e4bfd2b95364299091a18f74127b26\"><code>b2da57a</code></a>\nchangelog for mldsa/mlkem for openssl (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14791\">#14791</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/3cf44adee25c368d4a136e072fa9f80465d91eb0\"><code>3cf44ad</code></a>\nML-KEM OpenSSL support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14781\">#14781</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/2e31639666766f846fbab2c605879db0fa64fe83\"><code>2e31639</code></a>\nML-DSA OpenSSL support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14773\">#14773</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/5affe5a286a986fdf512c4a5cb280d28a96c10e3\"><code>5affe5a</code></a>\nfix rust nightly clippy (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14790\">#14790</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/2e73ca448eaf64b6f0d4ffbb794cf96170cef5ec\"><code>2e73ca4</code></a>\nbump rust-openssl dep and update EcPoint::mul_generator to\nmul_generator2 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/1\">#1</a>...</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/compare/46.0.7...48.0.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `cryptography` from 46.0.7 to 48.0.1\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/blob/main/CHANGELOG.rst\">cryptography's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>48.0.1 - 2026-06-09</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Updated Windows, macOS, and Linux wheels to be compiled with OpenSSL\n4.0.1.\n<p>.. _v48-0-0:</p>\n<p>48.0.0 - 2026-05-04<br />\n</code></pre></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Support for Python 3.8 has\nbeen removed.\n<code>cryptography</code> now requires Python 3.9 or later.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Loading an X.509 CRL whose\ninner\n<code>TBSCertList.signature</code> algorithm does not match the outer\n<code>signatureAlgorithm</code> now raises <code>ValueError</code>.\nPreviously, such CRLs\nwere parsed successfully and only rejected during signature\nvalidation.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Added support for\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mlkem</code> and\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mldsa</code> when using OpenSSL\n3.5.0 or\nlater, in addition to the existing AWS-LC and BoringSSL support. This\nmeans\npost-quantum algorithms are now available to users of our wheels.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Note:</strong> Going forward, we do not guarantee that all\nfunctionality\nin <code>cryptography</code> will be available when building against\nOpenSSL. See :doc:<code>/statements/state-of-openssl</code> for more\ninformation.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>.. _v47-0-0:</p>\n<p>47.0.0 - 2026-04-24</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Support for Python 3.8 is deprecated and will be removed in the next\n  ``cryptography`` release.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for binary elliptic curves\n  (``SECT*`` classes) has been removed. These curves are rarely used and\n  have additional security considerations that make them undesirable.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for OpenSSL 1.1.x has been\nremoved.\nOpenSSL 3.0.0 or later is now required. LibreSSL, BoringSSL, and AWS-LC\n  continue to be supported.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Dropped support for LibreSSL &lt; 4.1.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Loading keys with unsupported algorithms\nor\n  keys with unsupported explicit curve encodings now raises\n  :class:`~cryptography.exceptions.UnsupportedAlgorithm` instead of\n  ``ValueError``. This change affects\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_public_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_public_key`,\n  and :meth:`~cryptography.x509.Certificate.public_key` when called on\n  certificates with unsupported public key algorithms.\n&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt; \n</code></pre>\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/de987ce48ccfeb1abca41efa23b2bf73ec704f74\"><code>de987ce</code></a>\n48.0.1 version bump and changelog (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14996\">#14996</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/8e03e30e3aae01632a697e903e3593c924f0139d\"><code>8e03e30</code></a>\nbump for 48.0.0 release (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14796\">#14796</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/295e0d254ef31ab864730aa41312ec355416ee71\"><code>295e0d2</code></a>\nAdd AGENTS.md with CLAUDE.md symlink (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14794\">#14794</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/104a2de19e268a433e6da92be9cb872dcf0003c8\"><code>104a2de</code></a>\nBump BoringSSL, OpenSSL, AWS-LC in CI (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14793\">#14793</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/67ec1e51988195e17993d2edef5258b27509b926\"><code>67ec1e5</code></a>\ncall check_length early on AesSiv::encrypt (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14792\">#14792</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/b2da57a0d9e4bfd2b95364299091a18f74127b26\"><code>b2da57a</code></a>\nchangelog for mldsa/mlkem for openssl (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14791\">#14791</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/3cf44adee25c368d4a136e072fa9f80465d91eb0\"><code>3cf44ad</code></a>\nML-KEM OpenSSL support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14781\">#14781</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/2e31639666766f846fbab2c605879db0fa64fe83\"><code>2e31639</code></a>\nML-DSA OpenSSL support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14773\">#14773</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/5affe5a286a986fdf512c4a5cb280d28a96c10e3\"><code>5affe5a</code></a>\nfix rust nightly clippy (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14790\">#14790</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/2e73ca448eaf64b6f0d4ffbb794cf96170cef5ec\"><code>2e73ca4</code></a>\nbump rust-openssl dep and update EcPoint::mul_generator to\nmul_generator2 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/1\">#1</a>...</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/compare/46.0.7...48.0.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `cryptography` from 48.0.0 to 48.0.1\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/blob/main/CHANGELOG.rst\">cryptography's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>48.0.1 - 2026-06-09</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Updated Windows, macOS, and Linux wheels to be compiled with OpenSSL\n4.0.1.\n<p>.. _v48-0-0:</p>\n<p>48.0.0 - 2026-05-04<br />\n</code></pre></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Support for Python 3.8 has\nbeen removed.\n<code>cryptography</code> now requires Python 3.9 or later.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Loading an X.509 CRL whose\ninner\n<code>TBSCertList.signature</code> algorithm does not match the outer\n<code>signatureAlgorithm</code> now raises <code>ValueError</code>.\nPreviously, such CRLs\nwere parsed successfully and only rejected during signature\nvalidation.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Added support for\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mlkem</code> and\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mldsa</code> when using OpenSSL\n3.5.0 or\nlater, in addition to the existing AWS-LC and BoringSSL support. This\nmeans\npost-quantum algorithms are now available to users of our wheels.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Note:</strong> Going forward, we do not guarantee that all\nfunctionality\nin <code>cryptography</code> will be available when building against\nOpenSSL. See :doc:<code>/statements/state-of-openssl</code> for more\ninformation.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>.. _v47-0-0:</p>\n<p>47.0.0 - 2026-04-24</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Support for Python 3.8 is deprecated and will be removed in the next\n  ``cryptography`` release.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for binary elliptic curves\n  (``SECT*`` classes) has been removed. These curves are rarely used and\n  have additional security considerations that make them undesirable.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for OpenSSL 1.1.x has been\nremoved.\nOpenSSL 3.0.0 or later is now required. LibreSSL, BoringSSL, and AWS-LC\n  continue to be supported.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Dropped support for LibreSSL &lt; 4.1.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Loading keys with unsupported algorithms\nor\n  keys with unsupported explicit curve encodings now raises\n  :class:`~cryptography.exceptions.UnsupportedAlgorithm` instead of\n  ``ValueError``. This change affects\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_public_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_public_key`,\n  and :meth:`~cryptography.x509.Certificate.public_key` when called on\n  certificates with unsupported public key algorithms.\n&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt; \n</code></pre>\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/de987ce48ccfeb1abca41efa23b2bf73ec704f74\"><code>de987ce</code></a>\n48.0.1 version bump and changelog (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14996\">#14996</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/8e03e30e3aae01632a697e903e3593c924f0139d\"><code>8e03e30</code></a>\nbump for 48.0.0 release (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14796\">#14796</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/295e0d254ef31ab864730aa41312ec355416ee71\"><code>295e0d2</code></a>\nAdd AGENTS.md with CLAUDE.md symlink (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14794\">#14794</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/104a2de19e268a433e6da92be9cb872dcf0003c8\"><code>104a2de</code></a>\nBump BoringSSL, OpenSSL, AWS-LC in CI (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14793\">#14793</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/67ec1e51988195e17993d2edef5258b27509b926\"><code>67ec1e5</code></a>\ncall check_length early on AesSiv::encrypt (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14792\">#14792</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/b2da57a0d9e4bfd2b95364299091a18f74127b26\"><code>b2da57a</code></a>\nchangelog for mldsa/mlkem for openssl (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14791\">#14791</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/3cf44adee25c368d4a136e072fa9f80465d91eb0\"><code>3cf44ad</code></a>\nML-KEM OpenSSL support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14781\">#14781</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/2e31639666766f846fbab2c605879db0fa64fe83\"><code>2e31639</code></a>\nML-DSA OpenSSL support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14773\">#14773</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/5affe5a286a986fdf512c4a5cb280d28a96c10e3\"><code>5affe5a</code></a>\nfix rust nightly clippy (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14790\">#14790</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/2e73ca448eaf64b6f0d4ffbb794cf96170cef5ec\"><code>2e73ca4</code></a>\nbump rust-openssl dep and update EcPoint::mul_generator to\nmul_generator2 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/1\">#1</a>...</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/compare/46.0.7...48.0.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `starlette` from 1.2.1 to 1.3.1\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/releases\">starlette's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Version 1.3.1</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Use <code>StarletteDeprecationWarning</code> instead of\n<code>DeprecationWarning</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3119\">Kludex/starlette#3119</a></li>\n<li>Enforce <code>max_fields</code> and <code>max_part_size</code> in\n<code>FormParser</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3329\">Kludex/starlette#3329</a></li>\n<li>Enforce <code>FormParser</code> limits in parser callbacks by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3331\">Kludex/starlette#3331</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.3.0...1.3.1\">https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.3.0...1.3.1</a></p>\n<h2>Version 1.3.0</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Clamp oversized suffix ranges in <code>FileResponse</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jiyujie2006\"><code>@​jiyujie2006</code></a> in\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3307\">Kludex/starlette#3307</a></li>\n<li>Catch <code>OSError</code> alongside <code>MultiPartException</code>\nwhen closing temp files by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/N3XT3R1337\"><code>@​N3XT3R1337</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3191\">Kludex/starlette#3191</a></li>\n<li>Add <code>httpx2</code> to the <code>full</code> extra by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3323\">Kludex/starlette#3323</a></li>\n<li>Adjust testclient typing and warnings by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/waketzheng\"><code>@​waketzheng</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3322\">Kludex/starlette#3322</a></li>\n<li>Fix IndexError in URL.replace() on a URL with no authority by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/LeSingh1\"><code>@​LeSingh1</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3317\">Kludex/starlette#3317</a></li>\n<li>Annotate URLPath protocol parameter with Literal by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Chang-LeHung\"><code>@​Chang-LeHung</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3285\">Kludex/starlette#3285</a></li>\n<li>avoid collapsing exception groups from user code by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/graingert\"><code>@​graingert</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/2830\">Kludex/starlette#2830</a></li>\n<li>Use <code>removeprefix</code> to strip weak ETag indicator in\n<code>is_not_modified</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/gnosyslambda\"><code>@​gnosyslambda</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3193\">Kludex/starlette#3193</a></li>\n<li>Build <code>request.url</code> from structured components by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3326\">Kludex/starlette#3326</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>New Contributors</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jiyujie2006\"><code>@​jiyujie2006</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3307\">Kludex/starlette#3307</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/N3XT3R1337\"><code>@​N3XT3R1337</code></a> made\ntheir first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3191\">Kludex/starlette#3191</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/leestana01\"><code>@​leestana01</code></a> made\ntheir first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3319\">Kludex/starlette#3319</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/LeSingh1\"><code>@​LeSingh1</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3317\">Kludex/starlette#3317</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/EmmanuelNiyonshuti\"><code>@​EmmanuelNiyonshuti</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3204\">Kludex/starlette#3204</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Chang-LeHung\"><code>@​Chang-LeHung</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3285\">Kludex/starlette#3285</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/gnosyslambda\"><code>@​gnosyslambda</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3193\">Kludex/starlette#3193</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.2.1...1.3.0\">https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.2.1...1.3.0</a></p>\n<h2>Version 1.2.1</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Use <code>httpx2</code> for type checking in the\n<code>testclient</code> module by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/leifwar\"><code>@​leifwar</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3304\">Kludex/starlette#3304</a></li>\n<li>Add assert error for requires() when request param is not Request\ntype by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/KeeganOP\"><code>@​KeeganOP</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3298\">Kludex/starlette#3298</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>New Contributors</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/leifwar\"><code>@​leifwar</code></a> made\ntheir first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3304\">Kludex/starlette#3304</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/diskeu\"><code>@​diskeu</code></a> made\ntheir first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3243\">Kludex/starlette#3243</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/KeeganOP\"><code>@​KeeganOP</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3298\">Kludex/starlette#3298</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.2.0...1.2.1\">https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.2.0...1.2.1</a></p>\n<h2>Version 1.2.0</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Support httpx2 in the test client by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3291\">Kludex/starlette#3291</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.1.0...1.2.0\">https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.1.0...1.2.0</a></p>\n<h2>Version 1.1.0</h2>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/blob/main/docs/release-notes.md\">starlette's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>1.3.1 (June 12, 2026)</h2>\n<h4>Fixed</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Enforce <code>max_fields</code> and <code>max_part_size</code> in\n<code>FormParser</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3329\">#3329</a>.</li>\n<li>Enforce <code>FormParser</code> limits in parser callbacks <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3331\">#3331</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>1.3.0 (June 11, 2026)</h2>\n<h4>Added</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Add <code>httpx2</code> to the <code>full</code> extra <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3323\">#3323</a>.</li>\n<li>Annotate the <code>URLPath</code> <code>protocol</code> parameter\nwith <code>Literal</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3285\">#3285</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Fixed</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Build <code>request.url</code> from structured components <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3326\">#3326</a>.</li>\n<li>Clamp oversized suffix ranges in <code>FileResponse</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3307\">#3307</a>.</li>\n<li>Catch <code>OSError</code> alongside <code>MultiPartException</code>\nwhen closing temp files <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3191\">#3191</a>.</li>\n<li>Avoid collapsing exception groups raised from user code <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/2830\">#2830</a>.</li>\n<li>Use <code>removeprefix</code> to strip the weak <code>ETag</code>\nindicator in <code>is_not_modified</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3193\">#3193</a>.</li>\n<li>Fix <code>IndexError</code> in <code>URL.replace()</code> on a URL\nwith no authority <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3317\">#3317</a>.</li>\n<li>Adjust <code>testclient</code> typing and warnings <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3322\">#3322</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>1.2.1 (May 31, 2026)</h2>\n<h4>Fixed</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Use <code>httpx2</code> for type checking in the\n<code>testclient</code> module <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3304\">#3304</a>.</li>\n<li>Add assert error for <code>requires()</code> when the request\nparameter is not a <code>Request</code> type <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3298\">#3298</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>1.2.0 (May 28, 2026)</h2>\n<h4>Added</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Support httpx2 in the test client <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3291\">#3291</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>1.1.0 (May 23, 2026)</h2>\n<h4>Added</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Use <code>&quot;application/octet-stream&quot;</code> as the\n<code>FileResponse</code> media type fallback <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3283\">#3283</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Fixed</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Only dispatch standard HTTP verbs in <code>HTTPEndpoint</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3286\">#3286</a>.</li>\n<li>Reject absolute paths in <code>StaticFiles.lookup_path</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3287\">#3287</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/8ebffd0678570ddd5d5bb11c6f3c3c7fd4682ab9\"><code>8ebffd0</code></a>\nVersion 1.3.1 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3330\">#3330</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/25b8e179d8d7ed86769c02f648772dd5fb43dc3c\"><code>25b8e17</code></a>\nEnforce <code>FormParser</code> limits in parser callbacks (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3331\">#3331</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/dba1c4babc4f99ad2622bb913d87045775dda735\"><code>dba1c4b</code></a>\nEnforce <code>max_fields</code> and <code>max_part_size</code> in\n<code>FormParser</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3329\">#3329</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/45e51dcf99f3a270b0bcec1aec5410b4345863a9\"><code>45e51dc</code></a>\nUse <code>StarletteDeprecationWarning</code> instead of\n<code>DeprecationWarning</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3119\">#3119</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/5f8610c386e13de1d80d36efa961e1486a1d2d01\"><code>5f8610c</code></a>\nVersion 1.3.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3327\">#3327</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/167b5850e809f38b27fbfed62d58bf6442855975\"><code>167b585</code></a>\nBuild <code>request.url</code> from structured components (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3326\">#3326</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/37309255b4c1b9c381a2d24a1eaf83100984a16a\"><code>3730925</code></a>\nUse <code>removeprefix</code> to strip weak ETag indicator in\n<code>is_not_modified</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3193\">#3193</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/e6f7ad1ab85efb27ab7910d8007b3f4531f7b083\"><code>e6f7ad1</code></a>\navoid collapsing exception groups from user code (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/2830\">#2830</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/115228fcdca0e0ef5bf4a95a40ddce5a9fced428\"><code>115228f</code></a>\nAnnotate URLPath protocol parameter with Literal (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3285\">#3285</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/113f193a34353c9153857028c1074351d22fad07\"><code>113f193</code></a>\ndocs: replace inline ASGI server list with link to canonical implemen…\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3204\">#3204</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.0.1...1.3.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `python-multipart` from 0.0.30 to 0.0.31\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/releases\">python-multipart's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Version 0.0.31</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Speed up multipart header parsing and callback dispatch by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/pull/295\">Kludex/python-multipart#295</a></li>\n<li>Bound header field name size before validating by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/pull/296\">Kludex/python-multipart#296</a></li>\n<li>Validate Content-Length is non-negative in parse_form by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/pull/297\">Kludex/python-multipart#297</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/compare/0.0.30...0.0.31\">https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/compare/0.0.30...0.0.31</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">python-multipart's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.0.31 (2026-06-04)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Speed up multipart header parsing and callback dispatch <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/pull/295\">#295</a>.</li>\n<li>Bound header field name size before validating <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/pull/296\">#296</a>.</li>\n<li>Validate <code>Content-Length</code> is non-negative in\n<code>parse_form</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/pull/297\">#297</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/commit/4cffc68a165f7a6f6b7756ce006fabf07a05b7a4\"><code>4cffc68</code></a>\nVersion 0.0.31 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/issues/298\">#298</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/commit/c814948acf509cef7881fa75c969969b19239bbf\"><code>c814948</code></a>\nReject negative <code>Content-Length</code> in <code>parse_form</code>\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/issues/297\">#297</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/commit/6b837d47bc68826ed5cbbcb50c6c6a6093444494\"><code>6b837d4</code></a>\nBound header field name size before validating (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/issues/296\">#296</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/commit/e0c4f9df2e737d1663fbbdd6563f80613a2089f9\"><code>e0c4f9d</code></a>\nBump the github-actions group with 3 updates (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/issues/294\">#294</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/commit/b8a01bb683e8e8675fdb5d831b206a478c8215aa\"><code>b8a01bb</code></a>\nBump the python-packages group with 3 updates (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/issues/293\">#293</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/commit/6732164f30c58e28589a1e22213d2f6b8c6bad9f\"><code>6732164</code></a>\nSpeed up multipart header parsing and callback dispatch (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/issues/295\">#295</a>)</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/compare/0.0.30...0.0.31\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> major version` will close this\ngroup update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific\ndependency's major version (unless you unignore this specific\ndependency's major version or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> minor version` will close this\ngroup update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific\ndependency's minor version (unless you unignore this specific\ndependency's minor version or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name>` will close this group update PR\nand stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific dependency\n(unless you unignore this specific dependency or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name>` will remove all of the ignore\nconditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name> <ignore condition>` will\nremove the ignore condition of the specified dependency and ignore\nconditions\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","tree":{"sha":"5352df6915bd43b680f30271c39661088be9d534","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/5352df6915bd43b680f30271c39661088be9d534"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/fecede5cb7c883c79f96ad8cb042c809395be59d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMXilCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxs0QAJu8W9rel+06CguSBpaLNMdE\nmJM+16vRUmOhQirFKj7RpahstGGGpShq0ZWOjV1JZ4Pjc/IrivQjhezQAouQXdRm\n9ym1N0v/7gamyfkws16j71YTv1eFEfVkeFl9SXRPHkwEYXBJY1p9H4GONVvfcrtV\no77l6msME2+lDjb79GSIXI7ozQoGHLAE0HfmaYFdoswq6ZWmxhU7Cgv1WnGUVm6+\nZea/tH2oZFIAOHkw/izTca2jBeGJcmO8ymKVFHm7Ruj0dOBBDMT8QXLMDIlTC2p2\nMUl4TFhsaHqSPL1UuA3JHiy3NDMAFl1tMpf7CHGlZomf2P29ct9UoBJSqPadMbZJ\nixPcHckLfvW6zKQ4i2AcI02rH28OedBtipv1G8WrySfkHSVsfL+RLIiWuXJWmtxI\nlac2peqa6u+ZoI1OLi65xEqU+mqatccJWmNWdcB0AInhvusswwInPUFxrU429caR\nrOUsfkUpR4z8hSvw3aSchxA4+OvHYIL5qSNB4tgwbxzTU/qsnAEJNI7/sd8NQHgD\nplehZ275+IR7erqW65Z+S1oAaW2uj+yCJINNr74kLaP7zFUwNOopek0hwR1rhiju\nKY7UEvES/y62SUuQqrv2Sxyaa5GlUwyvqR/BuE0WFKxXB5U+Y/oMuqRYqtuOosB6\nqA7nNjeTHeOz1h889Aik\n=o5zA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5352df6915bd43b680f30271c39661088be9d534\nparent 554df4a67368bb209ad4525a2f6a7195b816d2aa\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1781627045 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781627045 -0400\n\nchore(deps): bump the uv group across 5 directories with 3 updates (#4015)\n\nBumps the uv group with 2 updates in the /examples/async-subagent-server\ndirectory: [cryptography](https://github.com/pyca/cryptography) and\n[starlette](https://github.com/Kludex/starlette).\nBumps the uv group with 1 update in the /examples/llm-wiki directory:\n[cryptography](https://github.com/pyca/cryptography).\nBumps the uv group with 1 update in the /examples/repl_swarm directory:\n[cryptography](https://github.com/pyca/cryptography).\nBumps the uv group with 1 update in the /examples/rlm_agent directory:\n[cryptography](https://github.com/pyca/cryptography).\nBumps the uv group with 3 updates in the /libs/talon directory:\n[cryptography](https://github.com/pyca/cryptography),\n[starlette](https://github.com/Kludex/starlette) and\n[python-multipart](https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart).\n\nUpdates `cryptography` from 46.0.7 to 48.0.1\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/blob/main/CHANGELOG.rst\">cryptography's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>48.0.1 - 2026-06-09</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Updated Windows, macOS, and Linux wheels to be compiled with OpenSSL\n4.0.1.\n<p>.. _v48-0-0:</p>\n<p>48.0.0 - 2026-05-04<br />\n</code></pre></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Support for Python 3.8 has\nbeen removed.\n<code>cryptography</code> now requires Python 3.9 or later.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Loading an X.509 CRL whose\ninner\n<code>TBSCertList.signature</code> algorithm does not match the outer\n<code>signatureAlgorithm</code> now raises <code>ValueError</code>.\nPreviously, such CRLs\nwere parsed successfully and only rejected during signature\nvalidation.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Added support for\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mlkem</code> and\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mldsa</code> when using OpenSSL\n3.5.0 or\nlater, in addition to the existing AWS-LC and BoringSSL support. This\nmeans\npost-quantum algorithms are now available to users of our wheels.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Note:</strong> Going forward, we do not guarantee that all\nfunctionality\nin <code>cryptography</code> will be available when building against\nOpenSSL. See :doc:<code>/statements/state-of-openssl</code> for more\ninformation.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>.. _v47-0-0:</p>\n<p>47.0.0 - 2026-04-24</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Support for Python 3.8 is deprecated and will be removed in the next\n  ``cryptography`` release.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for binary elliptic curves\n  (``SECT*`` classes) has been removed. These curves are rarely used and\n  have additional security considerations that make them undesirable.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for OpenSSL 1.1.x has been\nremoved.\nOpenSSL 3.0.0 or later is now required. LibreSSL, BoringSSL, and AWS-LC\n  continue to be supported.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Dropped support for LibreSSL &lt; 4.1.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Loading keys with unsupported algorithms\nor\n  keys with unsupported explicit curve encodings now raises\n  :class:`~cryptography.exceptions.UnsupportedAlgorithm` instead of\n  ``ValueError``. This change affects\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_public_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_public_key`,\n  and :meth:`~cryptography.x509.Certificate.public_key` when called on\n  certificates with unsupported public key algorithms.\n&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt; \n</code></pre>\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/de987ce48ccfeb1abca41efa23b2bf73ec704f74\"><code>de987ce</code></a>\n48.0.1 version bump and changelog (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14996\">#14996</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/8e03e30e3aae01632a697e903e3593c924f0139d\"><code>8e03e30</code></a>\nbump for 48.0.0 release (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14796\">#14796</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/295e0d254ef31ab864730aa41312ec355416ee71\"><code>295e0d2</code></a>\nAdd AGENTS.md with CLAUDE.md symlink (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14794\">#14794</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/104a2de19e268a433e6da92be9cb872dcf0003c8\"><code>104a2de</code></a>\nBump BoringSSL, OpenSSL, AWS-LC in CI (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14793\">#14793</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/67ec1e51988195e17993d2edef5258b27509b926\"><code>67ec1e5</code></a>\ncall check_length early on AesSiv::encrypt (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14792\">#14792</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/b2da57a0d9e4bfd2b95364299091a18f74127b26\"><code>b2da57a</code></a>\nchangelog for mldsa/mlkem for openssl (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14791\">#14791</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/3cf44adee25c368d4a136e072fa9f80465d91eb0\"><code>3cf44ad</code></a>\nML-KEM OpenSSL support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14781\">#14781</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/2e31639666766f846fbab2c605879db0fa64fe83\"><code>2e31639</code></a>\nML-DSA OpenSSL support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14773\">#14773</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/5affe5a286a986fdf512c4a5cb280d28a96c10e3\"><code>5affe5a</code></a>\nfix rust nightly clippy (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14790\">#14790</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/2e73ca448eaf64b6f0d4ffbb794cf96170cef5ec\"><code>2e73ca4</code></a>\nbump rust-openssl dep and update EcPoint::mul_generator to\nmul_generator2 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/1\">#1</a>...</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/compare/46.0.7...48.0.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `starlette` from 1.0.1 to 1.3.1\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/releases\">starlette's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Version 1.3.1</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Use <code>StarletteDeprecationWarning</code> instead of\n<code>DeprecationWarning</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3119\">Kludex/starlette#3119</a></li>\n<li>Enforce <code>max_fields</code> and <code>max_part_size</code> in\n<code>FormParser</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3329\">Kludex/starlette#3329</a></li>\n<li>Enforce <code>FormParser</code> limits in parser callbacks by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3331\">Kludex/starlette#3331</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.3.0...1.3.1\">https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.3.0...1.3.1</a></p>\n<h2>Version 1.3.0</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Clamp oversized suffix ranges in <code>FileResponse</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jiyujie2006\"><code>@​jiyujie2006</code></a> in\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3307\">Kludex/starlette#3307</a></li>\n<li>Catch <code>OSError</code> alongside <code>MultiPartException</code>\nwhen closing temp files by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/N3XT3R1337\"><code>@​N3XT3R1337</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3191\">Kludex/starlette#3191</a></li>\n<li>Add <code>httpx2</code> to the <code>full</code> extra by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3323\">Kludex/starlette#3323</a></li>\n<li>Adjust testclient typing and warnings by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/waketzheng\"><code>@​waketzheng</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3322\">Kludex/starlette#3322</a></li>\n<li>Fix IndexError in URL.replace() on a URL with no authority by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/LeSingh1\"><code>@​LeSingh1</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3317\">Kludex/starlette#3317</a></li>\n<li>Annotate URLPath protocol parameter with Literal by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Chang-LeHung\"><code>@​Chang-LeHung</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3285\">Kludex/starlette#3285</a></li>\n<li>avoid collapsing exception groups from user code by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/graingert\"><code>@​graingert</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/2830\">Kludex/starlette#2830</a></li>\n<li>Use <code>removeprefix</code> to strip weak ETag indicator in\n<code>is_not_modified</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/gnosyslambda\"><code>@​gnosyslambda</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3193\">Kludex/starlette#3193</a></li>\n<li>Build <code>request.url</code> from structured components by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3326\">Kludex/starlette#3326</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>New Contributors</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/jiyujie2006\"><code>@​jiyujie2006</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3307\">Kludex/starlette#3307</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/N3XT3R1337\"><code>@​N3XT3R1337</code></a> made\ntheir first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3191\">Kludex/starlette#3191</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/leestana01\"><code>@​leestana01</code></a> made\ntheir first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3319\">Kludex/starlette#3319</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/LeSingh1\"><code>@​LeSingh1</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3317\">Kludex/starlette#3317</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/EmmanuelNiyonshuti\"><code>@​EmmanuelNiyonshuti</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3204\">Kludex/starlette#3204</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Chang-LeHung\"><code>@​Chang-LeHung</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3285\">Kludex/starlette#3285</a></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/gnosyslambda\"><code>@​gnosyslambda</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3193\">Kludex/starlette#3193</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.2.1...1.3.0\">https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.2.1...1.3.0</a></p>\n<h2>Version 1.2.1</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Use <code>httpx2</code> for type checking in the\n<code>testclient</code> module by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/leifwar\"><code>@​leifwar</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3304\">Kludex/starlette#3304</a></li>\n<li>Add assert error for requires() when request param is not Request\ntype by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/KeeganOP\"><code>@​KeeganOP</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3298\">Kludex/starlette#3298</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>New Contributors</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/leifwar\"><code>@​leifwar</code></a> made\ntheir first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3304\">Kludex/starlette#3304</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/diskeu\"><code>@​diskeu</code></a> made\ntheir first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3243\">Kludex/starlette#3243</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/KeeganOP\"><code>@​KeeganOP</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3298\">Kludex/starlette#3298</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.2.0...1.2.1\">https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.2.0...1.2.1</a></p>\n<h2>Version 1.2.0</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Support httpx2 in the test client by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/pull/3291\">Kludex/starlette#3291</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.1.0...1.2.0\">https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.1.0...1.2.0</a></p>\n<h2>Version 1.1.0</h2>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/blob/main/docs/release-notes.md\">starlette's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>1.3.1 (June 12, 2026)</h2>\n<h4>Fixed</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Enforce <code>max_fields</code> and <code>max_part_size</code> in\n<code>FormParser</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3329\">#3329</a>.</li>\n<li>Enforce <code>FormParser</code> limits in parser callbacks <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3331\">#3331</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>1.3.0 (June 11, 2026)</h2>\n<h4>Added</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Add <code>httpx2</code> to the <code>full</code> extra <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3323\">#3323</a>.</li>\n<li>Annotate the <code>URLPath</code> <code>protocol</code> parameter\nwith <code>Literal</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3285\">#3285</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Fixed</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Build <code>request.url</code> from structured components <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3326\">#3326</a>.</li>\n<li>Clamp oversized suffix ranges in <code>FileResponse</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3307\">#3307</a>.</li>\n<li>Catch <code>OSError</code> alongside <code>MultiPartException</code>\nwhen closing temp files <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3191\">#3191</a>.</li>\n<li>Avoid collapsing exception groups raised from user code <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/2830\">#2830</a>.</li>\n<li>Use <code>removeprefix</code> to strip the weak <code>ETag</code>\nindicator in <code>is_not_modified</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3193\">#3193</a>.</li>\n<li>Fix <code>IndexError</code> in <code>URL.replace()</code> on a URL\nwith no authority <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3317\">#3317</a>.</li>\n<li>Adjust <code>testclient</code> typing and warnings <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3322\">#3322</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>1.2.1 (May 31, 2026)</h2>\n<h4>Fixed</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Use <code>httpx2</code> for type checking in the\n<code>testclient</code> module <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3304\">#3304</a>.</li>\n<li>Add assert error for <code>requires()</code> when the request\nparameter is not a <code>Request</code> type <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3298\">#3298</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>1.2.0 (May 28, 2026)</h2>\n<h4>Added</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Support httpx2 in the test client <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3291\">#3291</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>1.1.0 (May 23, 2026)</h2>\n<h4>Added</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Use <code>&quot;application/octet-stream&quot;</code> as the\n<code>FileResponse</code> media type fallback <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3283\">#3283</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Fixed</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Only dispatch standard HTTP verbs in <code>HTTPEndpoint</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3286\">#3286</a>.</li>\n<li>Reject absolute paths in <code>StaticFiles.lookup_path</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/encode/starlette/pull/3287\">#3287</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/8ebffd0678570ddd5d5bb11c6f3c3c7fd4682ab9\"><code>8ebffd0</code></a>\nVersion 1.3.1 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3330\">#3330</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/25b8e179d8d7ed86769c02f648772dd5fb43dc3c\"><code>25b8e17</code></a>\nEnforce <code>FormParser</code> limits in parser callbacks (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3331\">#3331</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/dba1c4babc4f99ad2622bb913d87045775dda735\"><code>dba1c4b</code></a>\nEnforce <code>max_fields</code> and <code>max_part_size</code> in\n<code>FormParser</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3329\">#3329</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/45e51dcf99f3a270b0bcec1aec5410b4345863a9\"><code>45e51dc</code></a>\nUse <code>StarletteDeprecationWarning</code> instead of\n<code>DeprecationWarning</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3119\">#3119</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/5f8610c386e13de1d80d36efa961e1486a1d2d01\"><code>5f8610c</code></a>\nVersion 1.3.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3327\">#3327</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/167b5850e809f38b27fbfed62d58bf6442855975\"><code>167b585</code></a>\nBuild <code>request.url</code> from structured components (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3326\">#3326</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/37309255b4c1b9c381a2d24a1eaf83100984a16a\"><code>3730925</code></a>\nUse <code>removeprefix</code> to strip weak ETag indicator in\n<code>is_not_modified</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3193\">#3193</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/e6f7ad1ab85efb27ab7910d8007b3f4531f7b083\"><code>e6f7ad1</code></a>\navoid collapsing exception groups from user code (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/2830\">#2830</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/115228fcdca0e0ef5bf4a95a40ddce5a9fced428\"><code>115228f</code></a>\nAnnotate URLPath protocol parameter with Literal (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3285\">#3285</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/commit/113f193a34353c9153857028c1074351d22fad07\"><code>113f193</code></a>\ndocs: replace inline ASGI server list with link to canonical implemen…\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/3204\">#3204</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/compare/1.0.1...1.3.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `cryptography` from 48.0.0 to 48.0.1\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/blob/main/CHANGELOG.rst\">cryptography's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>48.0.1 - 2026-06-09</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Updated Windows, macOS, and Linux wheels to be compiled with OpenSSL\n4.0.1.\n<p>.. _v48-0-0:</p>\n<p>48.0.0 - 2026-05-04<br />\n</code></pre></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Support for Python 3.8 has\nbeen removed.\n<code>cryptography</code> now requires Python 3.9 or later.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Loading an X.509 CRL whose\ninner\n<code>TBSCertList.signature</code> algorithm does not match the outer\n<code>signatureAlgorithm</code> now raises <code>ValueError</code>.\nPreviously, such CRLs\nwere parsed successfully and only rejected during signature\nvalidation.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Added support for\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mlkem</code> and\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mldsa</code> when using OpenSSL\n3.5.0 or\nlater, in addition to the existing AWS-LC and BoringSSL support. This\nmeans\npost-quantum algorithms are now available to users of our wheels.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Note:</strong> Going forward, we do not guarantee that all\nfunctionality\nin <code>cryptography</code> will be available when building against\nOpenSSL. See :doc:<code>/statements/state-of-openssl</code> for more\ninformation.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>.. _v47-0-0:</p>\n<p>47.0.0 - 2026-04-24</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Support for Python 3.8 is deprecated and will be removed in the next\n  ``cryptography`` release.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for binary elliptic curves\n  (``SECT*`` classes) has been removed. These curves are rarely used and\n  have additional security considerations that make them undesirable.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for OpenSSL 1.1.x has been\nremoved.\nOpenSSL 3.0.0 or later is now required. LibreSSL, BoringSSL, and AWS-LC\n  continue to be supported.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Dropped support for LibreSSL &lt; 4.1.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Loading keys with unsupported algorithms\nor\n  keys with unsupported explicit curve encodings now raises\n  :class:`~cryptography.exceptions.UnsupportedAlgorithm` instead of\n  ``ValueError``. This change affects\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_public_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_public_key`,\n  and :meth:`~cryptography.x509.Certificate.public_key` when called on\n  certificates with unsupported public key algorithms.\n&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt; \n</code></pre>\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/de987ce48ccfeb1abca41efa23b2bf73ec704f74\"><code>de987ce</code></a>\n48.0.1 version bump and changelog (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14996\">#14996</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/8e03e30e3aae01632a697e903e3593c924f0139d\"><code>8e03e30</code></a>\nbump for 48.0.0 release (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14796\">#14796</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/295e0d254ef31ab864730aa41312ec355416ee71\"><code>295e0d2</code></a>\nAdd AGENTS.md with CLAUDE.md symlink (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14794\">#14794</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/104a2de19e268a433e6da92be9cb872dcf0003c8\"><code>104a2de</code></a>\nBump BoringSSL, OpenSSL, AWS-LC in CI (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14793\">#14793</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/67ec1e51988195e17993d2edef5258b27509b926\"><code>67ec1e5</code></a>\ncall check_length early on AesSiv::encrypt (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14792\">#14792</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/b2da57a0d9e4bfd2b95364299091a18f74127b26\"><code>b2da57a</code></a>\nchangelog for mldsa/mlkem for openssl (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14791\">#14791</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/3cf44adee25c368d4a136e072fa9f80465d91eb0\"><code>3cf44ad</code></a>\nML-KEM OpenSSL support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14781\">#14781</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/2e31639666766f846fbab2c605879db0fa64fe83\"><code>2e31639</code></a>\nML-DSA OpenSSL support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14773\">#14773</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/5affe5a286a986fdf512c4a5cb280d28a96c10e3\"><code>5affe5a</code></a>\nfix rust nightly clippy (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14790\">#14790</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/2e73ca448eaf64b6f0d4ffbb794cf96170cef5ec\"><code>2e73ca4</code></a>\nbump rust-openssl dep and update EcPoint::mul_generator to\nmul_generator2 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/1\">#1</a>...</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/compare/46.0.7...48.0.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `cryptography` from 46.0.7 to 48.0.1\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/blob/main/CHANGELOG.rst\">cryptography's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>48.0.1 - 2026-06-09</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Updated Windows, macOS, and Linux wheels to be compiled with OpenSSL\n4.0.1.\n<p>.. _v48-0-0:</p>\n<p>48.0.0 - 2026-05-04<br />\n</code></pre></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Support for Python 3.8 has\nbeen removed.\n<code>cryptography</code> now requires Python 3.9 or later.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Loading an X.509 CRL whose\ninner\n<code>TBSCertList.signature</code> algorithm does not match the outer\n<code>signatureAlgorithm</code> now raises <code>ValueError</code>.\nPreviously, such CRLs\nwere parsed successfully and only rejected during signature\nvalidation.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Added support for\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mlkem</code> and\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mldsa</code> when using OpenSSL\n3.5.0 or\nlater, in addition to the existing AWS-LC and BoringSSL support. This\nmeans\npost-quantum algorithms are now available to users of our wheels.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Note:</strong> Going forward, we do not guarantee that all\nfunctionality\nin <code>cryptography</code> will be available when building against\nOpenSSL. See :doc:<code>/statements/state-of-openssl</code> for more\ninformation.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>.. _v47-0-0:</p>\n<p>47.0.0 - 2026-04-24</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Support for Python 3.8 is deprecated and will be removed in the next\n  ``cryptography`` release.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for binary elliptic curves\n  (``SECT*`` classes) has been removed. These curves are rarely used and\n  have additional security considerations that make them undesirable.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for OpenSSL 1.1.x has been\nremoved.\nOpenSSL 3.0.0 or later is now required. LibreSSL, BoringSSL, and AWS-LC\n  continue to be supported.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Dropped support for LibreSSL &lt; 4.1.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Loading keys with unsupported algorithms\nor\n  keys with unsupported explicit curve encodings now raises\n  :class:`~cryptography.exceptions.UnsupportedAlgorithm` instead of\n  ``ValueError``. This change affects\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_public_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_public_key`,\n  and :meth:`~cryptography.x509.Certificate.public_key` when called on\n  certificates with unsupported public key algorithms.\n&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt; \n</code></pre>\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/de987ce48ccfeb1abca41efa23b2bf73ec704f74\"><code>de987ce</code></a>\n48.0.1 version bump and changelog (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14996\">#14996</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/8e03e30e3aae01632a697e903e3593c924f0139d\"><code>8e03e30</code></a>\nbump for 48.0.0 release (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14796\">#14796</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/295e0d254ef31ab864730aa41312ec355416ee71\"><code>295e0d2</code></a>\nAdd AGENTS.md with CLAUDE.md symlink (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14794\">#14794</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/104a2de19e268a433e6da92be9cb872dcf0003c8\"><code>104a2de</code></a>\nBump BoringSSL, OpenSSL, AWS-LC in CI (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14793\">#14793</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/67ec1e51988195e17993d2edef5258b27509b926\"><code>67ec1e5</code></a>\ncall check_length early on AesSiv::encrypt (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14792\">#14792</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/b2da57a0d9e4bfd2b95364299091a18f74127b26\"><code>b2da57a</code></a>\nchangelog for mldsa/mlkem for openssl (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14791\">#14791</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/3cf44adee25c368d4a136e072fa9f80465d91eb0\"><code>3cf44ad</code></a>\nML-KEM OpenSSL support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14781\">#14781</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/2e31639666766f846fbab2c605879db0fa64fe83\"><code>2e31639</code></a>\nML-DSA OpenSSL support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14773\">#14773</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/5affe5a286a986fdf512c4a5cb280d28a96c10e3\"><code>5affe5a</code></a>\nfix rust nightly clippy (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14790\">#14790</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/2e73ca448eaf64b6f0d4ffbb794cf96170cef5ec\"><code>2e73ca4</code></a>\nbump rust-openssl dep and update EcPoint::mul_generator to\nmul_generator2 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/1\">#1</a>...</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/compare/46.0.7...48.0.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `cryptography` from 46.0.7 to 48.0.1\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/blob/main/CHANGELOG.rst\">cryptography's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>48.0.1 - 2026-06-09</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Updated Windows, macOS, and Linux wheels to be compiled with OpenSSL\n4.0.1.\n<p>.. _v48-0-0:</p>\n<p>48.0.0 - 2026-05-04<br />\n</code></pre></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Support for Python 3.8 has\nbeen removed.\n<code>cryptography</code> now requires Python 3.9 or later.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Loading an X.509 CRL whose\ninner\n<code>TBSCertList.signature</code> algorithm does not match the outer\n<code>signatureAlgorithm</code> now raises <code>ValueError</code>.\nPreviously, such CRLs\nwere parsed successfully and only rejected during signature\nvalidation.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Added support for\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mlkem</code> and\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mldsa</code> when using OpenSSL\n3.5.0 or\nlater, in addition to the existing AWS-LC and BoringSSL support. This\nmeans\npost-quantum algorithms are now available to users of our wheels.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Note:</strong> Going forward, we do not guarantee that all\nfunctionality\nin <code>cryptography</code> will be available when building against\nOpenSSL. See :doc:<code>/statements/state-of-openssl</code> for more\ninformation.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>.. _v47-0-0:</p>\n<p>47.0.0 - 2026-04-24</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Support for Python 3.8 is deprecated and will be removed in the next\n  ``cryptography`` release.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for binary elliptic curves\n  (``SECT*`` classes) has been removed. These curves are rarely used and\n  have additional security considerations that make them undesirable.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for OpenSSL 1.1.x has been\nremoved.\nOpenSSL 3.0.0 or later is now required. LibreSSL, BoringSSL, and AWS-LC\n  continue to be supported.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Dropped support for LibreSSL &lt; 4.1.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Loading keys with unsupported algorithms\nor\n  keys with unsupported explicit curve encodings now raises\n  :class:`~cryptography.exceptions.UnsupportedAlgorithm` instead of\n  ``ValueError``. This change affects\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_public_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_public_key`,\n  and :meth:`~cryptography.x509.Certificate.public_key` when called on\n  certificates with unsupported public key algorithms.\n&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt; \n</code></pre>\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/de987ce48ccfeb1abca41efa23b2bf73ec704f74\"><code>de987ce</code></a>\n48.0.1 version bump and changelog (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14996\">#14996</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://g