","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4033f0121f7405ad8b528a0c552c9ec82cc0bf32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4033f0121f7405ad8b528a0c552c9ec82cc0bf32","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4033f0121f7405ad8b528a0c552c9ec82cc0bf32"}]},{"sha":"4033f0121f7405ad8b528a0c552c9ec82cc0bf32","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDQwMzNmMDEyMWY3NDA1YWQ4YjUyOGEwYzU1MmM5ZWM4MmNjMGJmMzI","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-16T16:22:51Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-16T16:22:51Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump cryptography from 46.0.7 to 48.0.1 in /libs/code (#4018)\n\nBumps [cryptography](https://github.com/pyca/cryptography) from 46.0.7\nto 48.0.1.\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/blob/main/CHANGELOG.rst\">cryptography's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>48.0.1 - 2026-06-09</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Updated Windows, macOS, and Linux wheels to be compiled with OpenSSL\n4.0.1.\n<p>.. _v48-0-0:</p>\n<p>48.0.0 - 2026-05-04<br />\n</code></pre></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Support for Python 3.8 has\nbeen removed.\n<code>cryptography</code> now requires Python 3.9 or later.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Loading an X.509 CRL whose\ninner\n<code>TBSCertList.signature</code> algorithm does not match the outer\n<code>signatureAlgorithm</code> now raises <code>ValueError</code>.\nPreviously, such CRLs\nwere parsed successfully and only rejected during signature\nvalidation.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Added support for\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mlkem</code> and\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mldsa</code> when using OpenSSL\n3.5.0 or\nlater, in addition to the existing AWS-LC and BoringSSL support. This\nmeans\npost-quantum algorithms are now available to users of our wheels.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Note:</strong> Going forward, we do not guarantee that all\nfunctionality\nin <code>cryptography</code> will be available when building against\nOpenSSL. See :doc:<code>/statements/state-of-openssl</code> for more\ninformation.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>.. _v47-0-0:</p>\n<p>47.0.0 - 2026-04-24</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Support for Python 3.8 is deprecated and will be removed in the next\n  ``cryptography`` release.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for binary elliptic curves\n  (``SECT*`` classes) has been removed. These curves are rarely used and\n  have additional security considerations that make them undesirable.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for OpenSSL 1.1.x has been\nremoved.\nOpenSSL 3.0.0 or later is now required. LibreSSL, BoringSSL, and AWS-LC\n  continue to be supported.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Dropped support for LibreSSL &lt; 4.1.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Loading keys with unsupported algorithms\nor\n  keys with unsupported explicit curve encodings now raises\n  :class:`~cryptography.exceptions.UnsupportedAlgorithm` instead of\n  ``ValueError``. This change affects\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_public_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_public_key`,\n  and :meth:`~cryptography.x509.Certificate.public_key` when called on\n  certificates with unsupported public key algorithms.\n&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt; \n</code></pre>\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/de987ce48ccfeb1abca41efa23b2bf73ec704f74\"><code>de987ce</code></a>\n48.0.1 version bump and changelog (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14996\">#14996</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/8e03e30e3aae01632a697e903e3593c924f0139d\"><code>8e03e30</code></a>\nbump for 48.0.0 release (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14796\">#14796</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/295e0d254ef31ab864730aa41312ec355416ee71\"><code>295e0d2</code></a>\nAdd AGENTS.md with CLAUDE.md symlink (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14794\">#14794</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/104a2de19e268a433e6da92be9cb872dcf0003c8\"><code>104a2de</code></a>\nBump BoringSSL, OpenSSL, AWS-LC in CI (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14793\">#14793</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/67ec1e51988195e17993d2edef5258b27509b926\"><code>67ec1e5</code></a>\ncall check_length early on AesSiv::encrypt (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14792\">#14792</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/b2da57a0d9e4bfd2b95364299091a18f74127b26\"><code>b2da57a</code></a>\nchangelog for mldsa/mlkem for openssl (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14791\">#14791</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/3cf44adee25c368d4a136e072fa9f80465d91eb0\"><code>3cf44ad</code></a>\nML-KEM OpenSSL support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14781\">#14781</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/2e31639666766f846fbab2c605879db0fa64fe83\"><code>2e31639</code></a>\nML-DSA OpenSSL support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14773\">#14773</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/5affe5a286a986fdf512c4a5cb280d28a96c10e3\"><code>5affe5a</code></a>\nfix rust nightly clippy (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14790\">#14790</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/2e73ca448eaf64b6f0d4ffbb794cf96170cef5ec\"><code>2e73ca4</code></a>\nbump rust-openssl dep and update EcPoint::mul_generator to\nmul_generator2 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/1\">#1</a>...</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/compare/46.0.7...48.0.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"ffd8130c7f76b4d494c0f3fe6abda0983a1abedc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/ffd8130c7f76b4d494c0f3fe6abda0983a1abedc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/4033f0121f7405ad8b528a0c552c9ec82cc0bf32","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMXhbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASRQQAJpvfuMO4R3L+wCIDkUKbhu7\n2sMilt/TQTFJ1csfbGODvrB7jPtaHsrrCgRjjYepfsVamSnbPgcWvWevQu9bS7pN\n/1PETcDeYcrAklf6K8r3ZzFYlWq4LpjGucjsb20zcpYQWkUbFS+RfMJJ8bNuf2M9\nJd0A7VYw5Ceq9Jbjl7nNOa3Bq4qEUHjZyLfEPuVMAYrWZH0p7LH7wjr1bOeoC8y7\n/SAsZ8+JZTJxe95FlhF4OUnQvmUUfSD7W15lNTaQ8H4df7XT8ZeCMhJGck3Ry843\n7zoeeMyQsSvYItagjb9LIbCOFDIOFmtpHycFX0fUtmHEnBjW6S0osq7IG9Gi9Yx/\nnZzcuknK1NJijzdoN2kLhwrrTdP9pn7E5DmUiRe0wrjGrcK29PbLM0RcG22oyqjc\n7swxXQlongA98LJADDmaUCeyPUtV40tqXF/Q5Poj8VlFHdMLJfND69Bz/ERa4XEP\niXQcX+U1i/2Lwq/Ij1zW54CFaf7e5aSUu9iNDSjatdUNbdfqZt5S7tJq6TDfUm/w\nrkcbwDIop+rhCCGzgx4mFn1XAdR2nop7RRT7BT32jC9eW11EJLBM/M5oiutiIFr6\nmM6aQRsvwTz2Idnt4EREvhs6g+RjU5O5l2kmz9ArQq4yPh4WJtdXweFmCoVbAZqL\nPoNVTEBR90t5Z9t4W2gW\n=i6NE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ffd8130c7f76b4d494c0f3fe6abda0983a1abedc\nparent ae35717b624237e053d194c2cb62f1fa87168b4b\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1781626971 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781626971 -0400\n\nchore(deps): bump cryptography from 46.0.7 to 48.0.1 in /libs/code (#4018)\n\nBumps [cryptography](https://github.com/pyca/cryptography) from 46.0.7\nto 48.0.1.\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/blob/main/CHANGELOG.rst\">cryptography's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>48.0.1 - 2026-06-09</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Updated Windows, macOS, and Linux wheels to be compiled with OpenSSL\n4.0.1.\n<p>.. _v48-0-0:</p>\n<p>48.0.0 - 2026-05-04<br />\n</code></pre></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Support for Python 3.8 has\nbeen removed.\n<code>cryptography</code> now requires Python 3.9 or later.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Loading an X.509 CRL whose\ninner\n<code>TBSCertList.signature</code> algorithm does not match the outer\n<code>signatureAlgorithm</code> now raises <code>ValueError</code>.\nPreviously, such CRLs\nwere parsed successfully and only rejected during signature\nvalidation.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Added support for\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mlkem</code> and\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mldsa</code> when using OpenSSL\n3.5.0 or\nlater, in addition to the existing AWS-LC and BoringSSL support. This\nmeans\npost-quantum algorithms are now available to users of our wheels.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Note:</strong> Going forward, we do not guarantee that all\nfunctionality\nin <code>cryptography</code> will be available when building against\nOpenSSL. See :doc:<code>/statements/state-of-openssl</code> for more\ninformation.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>.. _v47-0-0:</p>\n<p>47.0.0 - 2026-04-24</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Support for Python 3.8 is deprecated and will be removed in the next\n  ``cryptography`` release.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for binary elliptic curves\n  (``SECT*`` classes) has been removed. These curves are rarely used and\n  have additional security considerations that make them undesirable.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for OpenSSL 1.1.x has been\nremoved.\nOpenSSL 3.0.0 or later is now required. LibreSSL, BoringSSL, and AWS-LC\n  continue to be supported.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Dropped support for LibreSSL &lt; 4.1.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Loading keys with unsupported algorithms\nor\n  keys with unsupported explicit curve encodings now raises\n  :class:`~cryptography.exceptions.UnsupportedAlgorithm` instead of\n  ``ValueError``. This change affects\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_public_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_public_key`,\n  and :meth:`~cryptography.x509.Certificate.public_key` when called on\n  certificates with unsupported public key algorithms.\n&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt; \n</code></pre>\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/de987ce48ccfeb1abca41efa23b2bf73ec704f74\"><code>de987ce</code></a>\n48.0.1 version bump and changelog (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14996\">#14996</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/8e03e30e3aae01632a697e903e3593c924f0139d\"><code>8e03e30</code></a>\nbump for 48.0.0 release (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14796\">#14796</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/295e0d254ef31ab864730aa41312ec355416ee71\"><code>295e0d2</code></a>\nAdd AGENTS.md with CLAUDE.md symlink (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14794\">#14794</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/104a2de19e268a433e6da92be9cb872dcf0003c8\"><code>104a2de</code></a>\nBump BoringSSL, OpenSSL, AWS-LC in CI (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14793\">#14793</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/67ec1e51988195e17993d2edef5258b27509b926\"><code>67ec1e5</code></a>\ncall check_length early on AesSiv::encrypt (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14792\">#14792</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/b2da57a0d9e4bfd2b95364299091a18f74127b26\"><code>b2da57a</code></a>\nchangelog for mldsa/mlkem for openssl (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14791\">#14791</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/3cf44adee25c368d4a136e072fa9f80465d91eb0\"><code>3cf44ad</code></a>\nML-KEM OpenSSL support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14781\">#14781</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/2e31639666766f846fbab2c605879db0fa64fe83\"><code>2e31639</code></a>\nML-DSA OpenSSL support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14773\">#14773</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/5affe5a286a986fdf512c4a5cb280d28a96c10e3\"><code>5affe5a</code></a>\nfix rust nightly clippy (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14790\">#14790</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/2e73ca448eaf64b6f0d4ffbb794cf96170cef5ec\"><code>2e73ca4</code></a>\nbump rust-openssl dep and update EcPoint::mul_generator to\nmul_generator2 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/1\">#1</a>...</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/compare/46.0.7...48.0.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-16T16:22:51Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4033f0121f7405ad8b528a0c552c9ec82cc0bf32","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4033f0121f7405ad8b528a0c552c9ec82cc0bf32","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4033f0121f7405ad8b528a0c552c9ec82cc0bf32/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ae35717b624237e053d194c2cb62f1fa87168b4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ae35717b624237e053d194c2cb62f1fa87168b4b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ae35717b624237e053d194c2cb62f1fa87168b4b"}]},{"sha":"ae35717b624237e053d194c2cb62f1fa87168b4b","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGFlMzU3MTdiNjI0MjM3ZTA1M2QxOTRjMmNiNjJmMWZhODcxNjhiNGI","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-16T16:22:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-16T16:22:40Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump python-multipart from 0.0.28 to 0.0.31 in /libs/code (#4019)\n\nBumps [python-multipart](https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart)\nfrom 0.0.28 to 0.0.31.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/releases\">python-multipart's\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Version 0.0.31</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Speed up multipart header parsing and callback dispatch by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/pull/295\">Kludex/python-multipart#295</a></li>\n<li>Bound header field name size before validating by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/pull/296\">Kludex/python-multipart#296</a></li>\n<li>Validate Content-Length is non-negative in parse_form by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/pull/297\">Kludex/python-multipart#297</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/compare/0.0.30...0.0.31\">https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/compare/0.0.30...0.0.31</a></p>\n<h2>Version 0.0.30</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Treat only <code>&amp;</code> as the urlencoded field separator by\n<a href=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/pull/290\">Kludex/python-multipart#290</a></li>\n<li>Ignore RFC 2231 extended parameters in\n<code>parse_options_header</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex\"><code>@​Kludex</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/pull/291\">Kludex/python-multipart#291</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/compare/0.0.29...0.0.30\">https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/compare/0.0.29...0.0.30</a></p>\n<h2>Version 0.0.29</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Handle malformed RFC 2231 continuations in\n<code>parse_options_header</code> by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/manunio\"><code>@​manunio</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/pull/270\">Kludex/python-multipart#270</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/compare/0.0.28...0.0.29\">https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/compare/0.0.28...0.0.29</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">python-multipart's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>0.0.31 (2026-06-04)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Speed up multipart header parsing and callback dispatch <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/pull/295\">#295</a>.</li>\n<li>Bound header field name size before validating <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/pull/296\">#296</a>.</li>\n<li>Validate <code>Content-Length</code> is non-negative in\n<code>parse_form</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/pull/297\">#297</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>0.0.30 (2026-05-31)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Parse <code>application/x-www-form-urlencoded</code> bodies per the\nWHATWG URL standard, treating only <code>&amp;</code> as a field\nseparator <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/pull/290\">#290</a>.</li>\n<li>Ignore RFC 2231/5987 extended parameters (<code>name*</code>,\n<code>filename*</code>) in <code>parse_options_header</code>, keeping\nthe plain parameter authoritative per <a\nhref=\"https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7578#section-4.2\">RFC\n7578 §4.2</a> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/pull/291\">#291</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>0.0.29 (2026-05-17)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Handle malformed RFC 2231 continuations in\n<code>parse_options_header</code> <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/pull/270\">#270</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/commit/4cffc68a165f7a6f6b7756ce006fabf07a05b7a4\"><code>4cffc68</code></a>\nVersion 0.0.31 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/issues/298\">#298</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/commit/c814948acf509cef7881fa75c969969b19239bbf\"><code>c814948</code></a>\nReject negative <code>Content-Length</code> in <code>parse_form</code>\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/issues/297\">#297</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/commit/6b837d47bc68826ed5cbbcb50c6c6a6093444494\"><code>6b837d4</code></a>\nBound header field name size before validating (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/issues/296\">#296</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/commit/e0c4f9df2e737d1663fbbdd6563f80613a2089f9\"><code>e0c4f9d</code></a>\nBump the github-actions group with 3 updates (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/issues/294\">#294</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/commit/b8a01bb683e8e8675fdb5d831b206a478c8215aa\"><code>b8a01bb</code></a>\nBump the python-packages group with 3 updates (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/issues/293\">#293</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/commit/6732164f30c58e28589a1e22213d2f6b8c6bad9f\"><code>6732164</code></a>\nSpeed up multipart header parsing and callback dispatch (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/issues/295\">#295</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/commit/9d3ead568a259f222cff6425262ff63e88d930d4\"><code>9d3ead5</code></a>\nVersion 0.0.30 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/issues/292\">#292</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/commit/3506c15ce99cb62faf2d5ceb3c4c1e5800cb843d\"><code>3506c15</code></a>\nIgnore RFC 2231 extended parameters in <code>parse_options_header</code>\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/issues/291\">#291</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/commit/d69df35cd2cad9c72794c2c340db646afae957d8\"><code>d69df35</code></a>\nTreat only <code>&amp;</code> as the urlencoded field separator (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/issues/290\">#290</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/commit/1e6ff9740b09fb439755f30e2b0e2ada1d297325\"><code>1e6ff97</code></a>\nBump idna from 3.11 to 3.15 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/issues/289\">#289</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/Kludex/python-multipart/compare/0.0.28...0.0.31\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=python-multipart&package-manager=uv&previous-version=0.0.28&new-version=0.0.31)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.git