/api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f0f4788098797b199e09c754c453222410d6c4d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f0f4788098797b199e09c754c453222410d6c4d0","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f0f4788098797b199e09c754c453222410d6c4d0"}]},{"sha":"f0f4788098797b199e09c754c453222410d6c4d0","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGYwZjQ3ODgwOTg3OTdiMTk5ZTA5Yzc1NGM0NTMyMjI0MTBkNmM0ZDA","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-16T16:19:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-16T16:19:46Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump cryptography from 46.0.7 to 48.0.1 in /libs/deepagents (#4016)\n\nBumps [cryptography](https://github.com/pyca/cryptography) from 46.0.7\nto 48.0.1.\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/blob/main/CHANGELOG.rst\">cryptography's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>48.0.1 - 2026-06-09</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Updated Windows, macOS, and Linux wheels to be compiled with OpenSSL\n4.0.1.\n<p>.. _v48-0-0:</p>\n<p>48.0.0 - 2026-05-04<br />\n</code></pre></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Support for Python 3.8 has\nbeen removed.\n<code>cryptography</code> now requires Python 3.9 or later.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Loading an X.509 CRL whose\ninner\n<code>TBSCertList.signature</code> algorithm does not match the outer\n<code>signatureAlgorithm</code> now raises <code>ValueError</code>.\nPreviously, such CRLs\nwere parsed successfully and only rejected during signature\nvalidation.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Added support for\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mlkem</code> and\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mldsa</code> when using OpenSSL\n3.5.0 or\nlater, in addition to the existing AWS-LC and BoringSSL support. This\nmeans\npost-quantum algorithms are now available to users of our wheels.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Note:</strong> Going forward, we do not guarantee that all\nfunctionality\nin <code>cryptography</code> will be available when building against\nOpenSSL. See :doc:<code>/statements/state-of-openssl</code> for more\ninformation.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>.. _v47-0-0:</p>\n<p>47.0.0 - 2026-04-24</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Support for Python 3.8 is deprecated and will be removed in the next\n  ``cryptography`` release.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for binary elliptic curves\n  (``SECT*`` classes) has been removed. These curves are rarely used and\n  have additional security considerations that make them undesirable.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for OpenSSL 1.1.x has been\nremoved.\nOpenSSL 3.0.0 or later is now required. LibreSSL, BoringSSL, and AWS-LC\n  continue to be supported.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Dropped support for LibreSSL &lt; 4.1.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Loading keys with unsupported algorithms\nor\n  keys with unsupported explicit curve encodings now raises\n  :class:`~cryptography.exceptions.UnsupportedAlgorithm` instead of\n  ``ValueError``. This change affects\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_public_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_public_key`,\n  and :meth:`~cryptography.x509.Certificate.public_key` when called on\n  certificates with unsupported public key algorithms.\n&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt; \n</code></pre>\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/de987ce48ccfeb1abca41efa23b2bf73ec704f74\"><code>de987ce</code></a>\n48.0.1 version bump and changelog (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14996\">#14996</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/8e03e30e3aae01632a697e903e3593c924f0139d\"><code>8e03e30</code></a>\nbump for 48.0.0 release (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14796\">#14796</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/295e0d254ef31ab864730aa41312ec355416ee71\"><code>295e0d2</code></a>\nAdd AGENTS.md with CLAUDE.md symlink (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14794\">#14794</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/104a2de19e268a433e6da92be9cb872dcf0003c8\"><code>104a2de</code></a>\nBump BoringSSL, OpenSSL, AWS-LC in CI (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14793\">#14793</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/67ec1e51988195e17993d2edef5258b27509b926\"><code>67ec1e5</code></a>\ncall check_length early on AesSiv::encrypt (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14792\">#14792</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/b2da57a0d9e4bfd2b95364299091a18f74127b26\"><code>b2da57a</code></a>\nchangelog for mldsa/mlkem for openssl (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14791\">#14791</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/3cf44adee25c368d4a136e072fa9f80465d91eb0\"><code>3cf44ad</code></a>\nML-KEM OpenSSL support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14781\">#14781</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/2e31639666766f846fbab2c605879db0fa64fe83\"><code>2e31639</code></a>\nML-DSA OpenSSL support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14773\">#14773</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/5affe5a286a986fdf512c4a5cb280d28a96c10e3\"><code>5affe5a</code></a>\nfix rust nightly clippy (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14790\">#14790</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/2e73ca448eaf64b6f0d4ffbb794cf96170cef5ec\"><code>2e73ca4</code></a>\nbump rust-openssl dep and update EcPoint::mul_generator to\nmul_generator2 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/1\">#1</a>...</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/compare/46.0.7...48.0.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"9ce581ac0b7d287a658b8cfc99d525e300bf1568","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/9ce581ac0b7d287a658b8cfc99d525e300bf1568"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/f0f4788098797b199e09c754c453222410d6c4d0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMXeiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJ6YQAEloIBTDXAP1YMLx4sbbL3RU\n2ZQxGCNM3NH8hBltVQnLq0DO1g9yJX5eBdREz0u7AIwFrBnLuOnNb6GaygSHqLfM\nnw0hq7hO2/kgexqcjuBEm4dtQJJqMhq+0JnVr83EJOb7fEWEJq7wiGs5iOauRBfA\nmgHn/D/b7sHnCIRQK97Q72Sn/a3DiNV+osiNiwt3LHdWUmAMkNiLrxMSqKLdBgRE\nw9W6MzY+G7kpw0RBfcgM+lMmOF6BcJzRXOAETVDSlvfWZSG2C6v00IjLNUjY8dnR\nuegYhfXaZLNEsdXycW+RFK1qvf4kl/Dv2a/sKVzndekwj3DNyH2EJH3+Qd7OeVC/\noahToqQg2IyZotO4wvm9sYEM1at3bqcoSy+QposEwxrT9wHMo6Cj2E+vVKBctzn6\nlW8eBrctxNjEukzWfaSfO3VI8pf2YG6YOTCxYm/jNcUVtj9AmY6GPhf7MuY5lw6h\niraU/mUWaVDmlmNQTiIEpDJjscc7CeEsN/NoEWltcgpP+nOA9y9OArUNr7a6AP3Q\nhv1RwLovHFSAAlbZdn2xuc8s1pXjXC05tPG28gOmC4DEWtb9ByhyUCj/Pl7/Zvko\nrdjIUYaO6UkJBfwrD4OIx1gcXhWOSVM1pTFYps92voi+V5D1nS5u/j6CiYsDcc07\nUW/yBLaCDjmBLPUrEs7e\n=pWcg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9ce581ac0b7d287a658b8cfc99d525e300bf1568\nparent fc9f4807c77514e326c66c5fe1f6e1460fee5857\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1781626786 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781626786 -0400\n\nchore(deps): bump cryptography from 46.0.7 to 48.0.1 in /libs/deepagents (#4016)\n\nBumps [cryptography](https://github.com/pyca/cryptography) from 46.0.7\nto 48.0.1.\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/blob/main/CHANGELOG.rst\">cryptography's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>48.0.1 - 2026-06-09</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Updated Windows, macOS, and Linux wheels to be compiled with OpenSSL\n4.0.1.\n<p>.. _v48-0-0:</p>\n<p>48.0.0 - 2026-05-04<br />\n</code></pre></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Support for Python 3.8 has\nbeen removed.\n<code>cryptography</code> now requires Python 3.9 or later.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Loading an X.509 CRL whose\ninner\n<code>TBSCertList.signature</code> algorithm does not match the outer\n<code>signatureAlgorithm</code> now raises <code>ValueError</code>.\nPreviously, such CRLs\nwere parsed successfully and only rejected during signature\nvalidation.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Added support for\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mlkem</code> and\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mldsa</code> when using OpenSSL\n3.5.0 or\nlater, in addition to the existing AWS-LC and BoringSSL support. This\nmeans\npost-quantum algorithms are now available to users of our wheels.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Note:</strong> Going forward, we do not guarantee that all\nfunctionality\nin <code>cryptography</code> will be available when building against\nOpenSSL. See :doc:<code>/statements/state-of-openssl</code> for more\ninformation.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>.. _v47-0-0:</p>\n<p>47.0.0 - 2026-04-24</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Support for Python 3.8 is deprecated and will be removed in the next\n  ``cryptography`` release.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for binary elliptic curves\n  (``SECT*`` classes) has been removed. These curves are rarely used and\n  have additional security considerations that make them undesirable.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for OpenSSL 1.1.x has been\nremoved.\nOpenSSL 3.0.0 or later is now required. LibreSSL, BoringSSL, and AWS-LC\n  continue to be supported.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Dropped support for LibreSSL &lt; 4.1.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Loading keys with unsupported algorithms\nor\n  keys with unsupported explicit curve encodings now raises\n  :class:`~cryptography.exceptions.UnsupportedAlgorithm` instead of\n  ``ValueError``. This change affects\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_public_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_public_key`,\n  and :meth:`~cryptography.x509.Certificate.public_key` when called on\n  certificates with unsupported public key algorithms.\n&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt; \n</code></pre>\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/de987ce48ccfeb1abca41efa23b2bf73ec704f74\"><code>de987ce</code></a>\n48.0.1 version bump and changelog (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14996\">#14996</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/8e03e30e3aae01632a697e903e3593c924f0139d\"><code>8e03e30</code></a>\nbump for 48.0.0 release (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14796\">#14796</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/295e0d254ef31ab864730aa41312ec355416ee71\"><code>295e0d2</code></a>\nAdd AGENTS.md with CLAUDE.md symlink (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14794\">#14794</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/104a2de19e268a433e6da92be9cb872dcf0003c8\"><code>104a2de</code></a>\nBump BoringSSL, OpenSSL, AWS-LC in CI (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14793\">#14793</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/67ec1e51988195e17993d2edef5258b27509b926\"><code>67ec1e5</code></a>\ncall check_length early on AesSiv::encrypt (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14792\">#14792</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/b2da57a0d9e4bfd2b95364299091a18f74127b26\"><code>b2da57a</code></a>\nchangelog for mldsa/mlkem for openssl (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14791\">#14791</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/3cf44adee25c368d4a136e072fa9f80465d91eb0\"><code>3cf44ad</code></a>\nML-KEM OpenSSL support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14781\">#14781</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/2e31639666766f846fbab2c605879db0fa64fe83\"><code>2e31639</code></a>\nML-DSA OpenSSL support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14773\">#14773</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/5affe5a286a986fdf512c4a5cb280d28a96c10e3\"><code>5affe5a</code></a>\nfix rust nightly clippy (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14790\">#14790</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/2e73ca448eaf64b6f0d4ffbb794cf96170cef5ec\"><code>2e73ca4</code></a>\nbump rust-openssl dep and update EcPoint::mul_generator to\nmul_generator2 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/1\">#1</a>...</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/compare/46.0.7...48.0.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-16T16:19:46Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f0f4788098797b199e09c754c453222410d6c4d0","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f0f4788098797b199e09c754c453222410d6c4d0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f0f4788098797b199e09c754c453222410d6c4d0/comments","author":{"login":"dependabot[bot]","id":49699333,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"fc9f4807c77514e326c66c5fe1f6e1460fee5857","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/fc9f4807c77514e326c66c5fe1f6e1460fee5857","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/fc9f4807c77514e326c66c5fe1f6e1460fee5857"}]},{"sha":"fc9f4807c77514e326c66c5fe1f6e1460fee5857","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGZjOWY0ODA3Yzc3NTE0ZTMyNmM2NmM1ZmUxZjZlMTQ2MGZlZTU4NTc","commit":{"author":{"name":"dependabot[bot]","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-16T16:19:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-16T16:19:17Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump cryptography from 46.0.7 to 48.0.1 in /libs/partners/daytona (#4011)\n\nBumps [cryptography](https://github.com/pyca/cryptography) from 46.0.7\nto 48.0.1.\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/blob/main/CHANGELOG.rst\">cryptography's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>48.0.1 - 2026-06-09</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Updated Windows, macOS, and Linux wheels to be compiled with OpenSSL\n4.0.1.\n<p>.. _v48-0-0:</p>\n<p>48.0.0 - 2026-05-04<br />\n</code></pre></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Support for Python 3.8 has\nbeen removed.\n<code>cryptography</code> now requires Python 3.9 or later.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Loading an X.509 CRL whose\ninner\n<code>TBSCertList.signature</code> algorithm does not match the outer\n<code>signatureAlgorithm</code> now raises <code>ValueError</code>.\nPreviously, such CRLs\nwere parsed successfully and only rejected during signature\nvalidation.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Added support for\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mlkem</code> and\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mldsa</code> when using OpenSSL\n3.5.0 or\nlater, in addition to the existing AWS-LC and BoringSSL support. This\nmeans\npost-quantum algorithms are now available to users of our wheels.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Note:</strong> Going forward, we do not guarantee that all\nfunctionality\nin <code>cryptography</code> will be available when building against\nOpenSSL. See :doc:<code>/statements/state-of-openssl</code> for more\ninformation.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>.. _v47-0-0:</p>\n<p>47.0.0 - 2026-04-24</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Support for Python 3.8 is deprecated and will be removed in the next\n  ``cryptography`` release.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for binary elliptic curves\n  (``SECT*`` classes) has been removed. These curves are rarely used and\n  have additional security considerations that make them undesirable.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for OpenSSL 1.1.x has been\nremoved.\nOpenSSL 3.0.0 or later is now required. LibreSSL, BoringSSL, and AWS-LC\n  continue to be supported.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Dropped support for LibreSSL &lt; 4.1.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Loading keys with unsupported algorithms\nor\n  keys with unsupported explicit curve encodings now raises\n  :class:`~cryptography.exceptions.UnsupportedAlgorithm` instead of\n  ``ValueError``. This change affects\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_public_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_public_key`,\n  and :meth:`~cryptography.x509.Certificate.public_key` when called on\n  certificates with unsupported public key algorithms.\n&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt; \n</code></pre>\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/de987ce48ccfeb1abca41efa23b2bf73ec704f74\"><code>de987ce</code></a>\n48.0.1 version bump and changelog (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14996\">#14996</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/8e03e30e3aae01632a697e903e3593c924f0139d\"><code>8e03e30</code></a>\nbump for 48.0.0 release (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14796\">#14796</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/295e0d254ef31ab864730aa41312ec355416ee71\"><code>295e0d2</code></a>\nAdd AGENTS.md with CLAUDE.md symlink (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14794\">#14794</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/104a2de19e268a433e6da92be9cb872dcf0003c8\"><code>104a2de</code></a>\nBump BoringSSL, OpenSSL, AWS-LC in CI (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14793\">#14793</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/67ec1e51988195e17993d2edef5258b27509b926\"><code>67ec1e5</code></a>\ncall check_length early on AesSiv::encrypt (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14792\">#14792</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/b2da57a0d9e4bfd2b95364299091a18f74127b26\"><code>b2da57a</code></a>\nchangelog for mldsa/mlkem for openssl (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14791\">#14791</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/3cf44adee25c368d4a136e072fa9f80465d91eb0\"><code>3cf44ad</code></a>\nML-KEM OpenSSL support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14781\">#14781</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/2e31639666766f846fbab2c605879db0fa64fe83\"><code>2e31639</code></a>\nML-DSA OpenSSL support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14773\">#14773</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/5affe5a286a986fdf512c4a5cb280d28a96c10e3\"><code>5affe5a</code></a>\nfix rust nightly clippy (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14790\">#14790</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/2e73ca448eaf64b6f0d4ffbb794cf96170cef5ec\"><code>2e73ca4</code></a>\nbump rust-openssl dep and update EcPoint::mul_generator to\nmul_generator2 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/1\">#1</a>...</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/compare/46.0.7...48.0.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"61a43b87501eed905175bea4f069b83578d86246","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/61a43b87501eed905175bea4f069b83578d86246"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/fc9f4807c77514e326c66c5fe1f6e1460fee5857","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMXeFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8VUQAEziTqnKHKFm5GKcIwUQr1wk\nyDCtzdbdr0UDc2Tj1hIApmw6Nhz+GCLFT+n13yI0Y5vh3AObIjhlS7xNPmVIEwJb\nXMIp5Cr385pI8G2AZP72nHTi73LP0ZkFCmhd5pwVi6Wn4dGwHSighLXbma02265p\nAl/b98Frd09+RYx09hOXXV29I9km51sOh5upQ3QENu2pRhtZ62dFwXjByx/1Qdzv\nO/YnqfReRA8LfXocaDMNQlnnGX4vF7NEIoIBsUpGdsp3YVGgpYC8Rj4Yk9AUFQ4L\nJW2ffSigGMgbyF1fR2WZ6b/fyyP3vyXV12dqiNSI+/NY8BhIbh8QK8/3e3XOMeQv\nL6Y3r/qYVdDh8nA0G+Fet2mIRlnEeZluAVd+MEhx2zOz+eoQWZfj4o0gunWfTAuP\ntYjLH0DUindvXutO/mJ+jWQm2Xai2jHj/oi4w+AZatsanLrEO+mvtHFppLHYIGY+\nd4b7pa3kv2dribqqF+Tc55pAZTMvfX0biNHq3qRmYLE1DD7jkmBIMpteP3/1CGcq\nyx619KH7EdK4jq2VoUygWkb5us58miZ/VC5cLUjLjz4LR2nWfcogCqUuAzXD6oWM\n2o1xDuAObE7l84LWGHTu02rzBOGUb5k41NpxVyg2zZh9QMaoMcLQCkFJ3OUp3WyD\nwzqnR5F9IiQtamWUTdlN\n=4xOW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 61a43b87501eed905175bea4f069b83578d86246\nparent 39620a1a15d34aa04047a95ea76e47617381cabf\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1781626757 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781626757 -0400\n\nchore(deps): bump cryptography from 46.0.7 to 48.0.1 in /libs/partners/daytona (#4011)\n\nBumps [cryptography](https://github.com/pyca/cryptography) from 46.0.7\nto 48.0.1.\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/blob/main/CHANGELOG.rst\">cryptography's\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>48.0.1 - 2026-06-09</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Updated Windows, macOS, and Linux wheels to be compiled with OpenSSL\n4.0.1.\n<p>.. _v48-0-0:</p>\n<p>48.0.0 - 2026-05-04<br />\n</code></pre></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Support for Python 3.8 has\nbeen removed.\n<code>cryptography</code> now requires Python 3.9 or later.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:</strong> Loading an X.509 CRL whose\ninner\n<code>TBSCertList.signature</code> algorithm does not match the outer\n<code>signatureAlgorithm</code> now raises <code>ValueError</code>.\nPreviously, such CRLs\nwere parsed successfully and only rejected during signature\nvalidation.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Added support for\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mlkem</code> and\n:doc:<code>/hazmat/primitives/asymmetric/mldsa</code> when using OpenSSL\n3.5.0 or\nlater, in addition to the existing AWS-LC and BoringSSL support. This\nmeans\npost-quantum algorithms are now available to users of our wheels.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Note:</strong> Going forward, we do not guarantee that all\nfunctionality\nin <code>cryptography</code> will be available when building against\nOpenSSL. See :doc:<code>/statements/state-of-openssl</code> for more\ninformation.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>.. _v47-0-0:</p>\n<p>47.0.0 - 2026-04-24</p>\n<pre><code>\n* Support for Python 3.8 is deprecated and will be removed in the next\n  ``cryptography`` release.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for binary elliptic curves\n  (``SECT*`` classes) has been removed. These curves are rarely used and\n  have additional security considerations that make them undesirable.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Support for OpenSSL 1.1.x has been\nremoved.\nOpenSSL 3.0.0 or later is now required. LibreSSL, BoringSSL, and AWS-LC\n  continue to be supported.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Dropped support for LibreSSL &lt; 4.1.\n* **BACKWARDS INCOMPATIBLE:** Loading keys with unsupported algorithms\nor\n  keys with unsupported explicit curve encodings now raises\n  :class:`~cryptography.exceptions.UnsupportedAlgorithm` instead of\n  ``ValueError``. This change affects\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_private_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_pem_public_key`,\n\n:func:`~cryptography.hazmat.primitives.serialization.load_der_public_key`,\n  and :meth:`~cryptography.x509.Certificate.public_key` when called on\n  certificates with unsupported public key algorithms.\n&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt; \n</code></pre>\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/de987ce48ccfeb1abca41efa23b2bf73ec704f74\"><code>de987ce</code></a>\n48.0.1 version bump and changelog (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14996\">#14996</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/8e03e30e3aae01632a697e903e3593c924f0139d\"><code>8e03e30</code></a>\nbump for 48.0.0 release (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14796\">#14796</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/295e0d254ef31ab864730aa41312ec355416ee71\"><code>295e0d2</code></a>\nAdd AGENTS.md with CLAUDE.md symlink (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14794\">#14794</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/104a2de19e268a433e6da92be9cb872dcf0003c8\"><code>104a2de</code></a>\nBump BoringSSL, OpenSSL, AWS-LC in CI (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14793\">#14793</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/67ec1e51988195e17993d2edef5258b27509b926\"><code>67ec1e5</code></a>\ncall check_length early on AesSiv::encrypt (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14792\">#14792</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/b2da57a0d9e4bfd2b95364299091a18f74127b26\"><code>b2da57a</code></a>\nchangelog for mldsa/mlkem for openssl (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14791\">#14791</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/3cf44adee25c368d4a136e072fa9f80465d91eb0\"><code>3cf44ad</code></a>\nML-KEM OpenSSL support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14781\">#14781</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/2e31639666766f846fbab2c605879db0fa64fe83\"><code>2e31639</code></a>\nML-DSA OpenSSL support (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14773\">#14773</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/5affe5a286a986fdf512c4a5cb280d28a96c10e3\"><code>5affe5a</code></a>\nfix rust nightly clippy (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/14790\">#14790</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/commit/2e73ca448eaf64b6f0d4ffbb794cf96170cef5ec\"><code>2e73ca4</code></a>\nbump rust-openssl dep and update EcPoint::mul_generator to\nmul_generator2 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/pyca/cryptography/issues/1\">#1</a>...</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/pyca/cryptography/compare/46.0.7...48.0.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-16T16:19:18Z"}