e937faf718db7ad2e98))\n* Add pre-release update support\n([#3960](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3960))\n([341a5cc](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/341a5cc55a30d808dbb366b396923c7801c431d2))\n* Add agent filter dropdown to `/threads` picker\n([#3677](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3677))\n([f8193df](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f8193df41d7c47626d94252039217f4079d117cd))\n* Non-interactive `deepagents auth` subcommands\n([#3910](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3910))\n([11a71bb](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/11a71bbf00c4e6c1f989e70fb3472a65c8d39662))\n* Prompt before updating an out-of-date dcode install\n([#3995](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3995))\n([a5ec6dd](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a5ec6dd0fec66ad321c1cc0f5e2f990c9026e03f))\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* Guard against misconfigured LangSmith tracing\n([#3993](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3993))\n([81acc2e](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/81acc2ecdada55a98e512f96b0caf8cb0f2c6d29))\n* Guard restart-prompt import against in-place self-upgrade\n([#3980](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3980))\n([7af13f6](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/7af13f6ec2440c2e3eb63bad2ff31e809f772804))\n* Skip startup auto-update when already updated in-session\n([#3915](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3915))\n([3ba3471](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3ba347138ac61a474bad58365fdeaa0d00cc1a42))\n\n---\n\n_Everything above this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-16T05:58:04Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a98f0dfa8d534d8a1885b524632400e52db22ac6","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a98f0dfa8d534d8a1885b524632400e52db22ac6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a98f0dfa8d534d8a1885b524632400e52db22ac6/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f8193df41d7c47626d94252039217f4079d117cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f8193df41d7c47626d94252039217f4079d117cd","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f8193df41d7c47626d94252039217f4079d117cd"}]},{"sha":"f8193df41d7c47626d94252039217f4079d117cd","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGY4MTkzZGY0MWQ3YzQ3NjI2ZDk0MjUyMDM5MjE3ZjQwNzlkMTE3Y2Q","commit":{"author":{"name":"Ninaad R. Rao","email":"35262832+NinaadRao@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-16T05:54:09Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-16T05:54:09Z"},"message":"feat(code): add agent filter dropdown to `/threads` picker (#3677)\n\nFixes #3667 \n\n---\n\nThe `/threads` picker now has a **\"Show agent:\"** dropdown in the\nOptions panel, letting users scope the thread list to a single agent\nwithout having to type into the fuzzy search box.\n\n## What changed\n\n**`libs/code/deepagents_code/widgets/thread_selector.py`**\n\n- Added `_AGENT_SELECT_ID` / `_AGENT_VALUE_ALL` constants alongside the\nexisting `_SCOPE_SELECT_ID` family, plus a shared `_UNKNOWN_AGENT_LABEL`\nsentinel so the Agent column, the dropdown options, and the filter\npredicate all render and match threads with no stored `agent_name`\nidentically.\n- Added `self._filter_agent: str | None` state (default `None` = all\nagents).\n- Added `_collect_agent_options()` — builds the dropdown options by\n**unioning** the agent names found in the loaded thread list with the\nconfigured agents (the `/agents` list), then prepends an \"All agents\"\nsentinel. Including the configured agents keeps the filter in sync with\n`/agents` so an agent that has not produced any threads yet is still\nselectable.\n- Added `_load_available_agent_names()` — caches the configured agent\nnames by running the `~/.deepagents/` scan in a worker thread (via\n`asyncio.to_thread`) so the event loop is never blocked on directory\nI/O. Its caller in `_load_threads` wraps the await in a best-effort\nguard so an unexpected scan failure degrades the filter to\nthread-derived names only rather than stranding the picker mid-load.\n- Added `_refresh_agent_select_options()` — repopulates the dropdown\nafter `_load_threads` completes, preserving the current selection when\nthe agent is still a valid option (present in the reloaded threads or\nthe configured `/agents` list) and falling back to \"All agents\"\notherwise.\n- Added `_agent_filtered_threads()` — returns `self._threads` narrowed\nto `self._filter_agent`; used as the base for both the sync\n(`_update_filtered_list`) and async (`_filter_and_build`) filtering\npaths so the agent filter ANDs with the existing text filter.\n- Extended `on_select_changed` with a branch for the agent select:\nupdates `self._filter_agent` and triggers\n`_schedule_filter_and_rebuild()` (in-memory, no DB re-query).\n- Generalized the scope-select-only focus/expansion helpers\n(`_get_select`, `_expanded_select_id`, `_is_select_expanded`,\n`_close_expanded_select`, `_select_expanded_highlight`,\n`_open_focused_select`, `_restore_expanded_select_focus`) to drive both\nOptions-panel dropdowns.\n- Added the agent `Select` widget and its label to `compose()` beneath\nthe existing scope select, and updated `_filter_focus_order` to include\nit between the scope select and the sort switch.\n\nThe filter is **in-memory** (applied after `_load_threads`) rather than\npassed to `list_threads`, so no extra DB query is needed when the user\nchanges the agent selection.\n\n**`libs/code/tests/unit_tests/test_thread_selector.py`**\n\nAdded `TestThreadSelectorAgentFilter` covering the data-shaping helpers\n(`_collect_agent_options` union/sort/dedup with mixed-case names,\n`_agent_filtered_threads` including the `(unknown)` sentinel), the\ndropdown-driven `Select.Changed` path and its `_confirming_delete`\nguard, selection preservation vs. clearing across reloads, the\nconfigured-agent union surfacing in the rendered widget, focus\nrestoration across async loads, and that an unexpected agent-scan\nfailure does not strand the picker. A new autouse fixture isolates the\nsuite from the host's `~/.deepagents/` so the option set is\ndeterministic. Existing tab-order tests were updated for the agent\nselect inserted between the scope select and the sort switch.\n\n## How did you verify your code works?\n\nSeeded the local `sessions.db` with 5 threads across 3 agents\n(`my-agent`, `other-agent`, `coding-bot`) and opened `/threads` in the\nrunning TUI:\n\n```\n   Thread ID Agent       Msg Created Updated Branch    │ Options\n > threadabc my-agent    ... 1d ago  1d ago  main      │\n   threadabc my-agent    ... 2d ago  2d ago  main      │ Show threads from:\n   threaddef other-agent ... 3d ago  3d ago  main      │ Current directory  ▼\n   threaddef other-agent ... 4d ago  4d ago  main      │\n   threadghi coding-bot  ... 5d ago  5d ago  main      │ Show agent:\n                                                        │ All agents        ▼\n```\n\nThe \"Show agent:\" dropdown appeared with \"All agents\" as the default.\nFiltering to `my-agent` narrowed the list to 2 threads; selecting\n`coding-bot` showed 1. Switching back to \"All agents\" restored all 5.\n\nAll 170 unit tests pass (`uv run pytest\ntests/unit_tests/test_thread_selector.py`).\n<img width=\"1347\" height=\"288\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-05-31 at 2 31 09 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/79826ed7-d200-4517-b974-e4dce0ca3c98\"\n/>\n<img width=\"288\" height=\"372\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-05-31 at 2 40 23 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4800ee3c-4229-4c37-9a41-69fa25162624\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1097\" height=\"439\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/93baf260-265e-483b-a413-880098f9ca18\"\n/>\n\n> This contribution was developed with the assistance of generative AI.\n\n## Social handles (optional)\nLinkedIn: https://linkedin.com/in/ninaadrao\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"05d587bee0ab176dfae32adc3260c9ed4e7068ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/05d587bee0ab176dfae32adc3260c9ed4e7068ac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/f8193df41d7c47626d94252039217f4079d117cd","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMOUBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeroQAJo7sZmFVJaVx7YMJ6wDBfHQ\nm1gQO2Zxeaj5dpHETEO9Fxousfl1eLQMy+MsHkJR5xTLQRjoWjvCRDwW34Weupe9\nSNgBZY6bx06n2u5ZuQ3clYJg+iXF2R0Pjvx1LkKv5tKD7fAfBe2MZkK/hzEcXpgH\nbtgt+0rMLDy/RAVkUXW5xjCDX9hBd8BSoryW07cJCsggI8RvkK6Hs/REyHN7ZMXP\nJNF/7qrXvVu7muYlImdi7MdwB0PICZcy0VfR6gaeYMmrYBykk3Pib94k3dBN2YTL\nEicqprhqm/3iSLMgh7Kqeet/D/4Oh+Vg8wFiBfI0RSRVX9w2pRF1bb/4ODRTQ2DC\ntYNmFqt7vOgTQZnNpWMUwzMICS335ej9E3DWU/Dj1ruLdvWcc/90DOmc87xH2yhL\ntARJ+Q6X9p0poZcqESR0tpEYFoPA/oPbqSw3OaVibcmX1gayYRRep6S4wLdm3X3K\nNTyLbeo2FmaEe1ma2YnvfaouYdJKnZbS+fSmWY+4tzTpEZaPF76OtbiX2ftPLOh5\n9O6CLSmNPsgo6MlZwj+U/qP3dKeg0rCzfyjI3RDEG9OGO389ip3La9T6Xw01oSaC\nXUE57BFPLosS0GEnXBs0JKjNoGxhq4O5SvD/YiKn+3ZbUd1OI7Nwly9sSvRTq0+S\ngIjj4DIAAW0LSmDRfjOX\n=GwW2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 05d587bee0ab176dfae32adc3260c9ed4e7068ac\nparent 81acc2ecdada55a98e512f96b0caf8cb0f2c6d29\nauthor Ninaad R. Rao <35262832+NinaadRao@users.noreply.github.com> 1781589249 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781589249 -0400\n\nfeat(code): add agent filter dropdown to `/threads` picker (#3677)\n\nFixes #3667 \n\n---\n\nThe `/threads` picker now has a **\"Show agent:\"** dropdown in the\nOptions panel, letting users scope the thread list to a single agent\nwithout having to type into the fuzzy search box.\n\n## What changed\n\n**`libs/code/deepagents_code/widgets/thread_selector.py`**\n\n- Added `_AGENT_SELECT_ID` / `_AGENT_VALUE_ALL` constants alongside the\nexisting `_SCOPE_SELECT_ID` family, plus a shared `_UNKNOWN_AGENT_LABEL`\nsentinel so the Agent column, the dropdown options, and the filter\npredicate all render and match threads with no stored `agent_name`\nidentically.\n- Added `self._filter_agent: str | None` state (default `None` = all\nagents).\n- Added `_collect_agent_options()` — builds the dropdown options by\n**unioning** the agent names found in the loaded thread list with the\nconfigured agents (the `/agents` list), then prepends an \"All agents\"\nsentinel. Including the configured agents keeps the filter in sync with\n`/agents` so an agent that has not produced any threads yet is still\nselectable.\n- Added `_load_available_agent_names()` — caches the configured agent\nnames by running the `~/.deepagents/` scan in a worker thread (via\n`asyncio.to_thread`) so the event loop is never blocked on directory\nI/O. Its caller in `_load_threads` wraps the await in a best-effort\nguard so an unexpected scan failure degrades the filter to\nthread-derived names only rather than stranding the picker mid-load.\n- Added `_refresh_agent_select_options()` — repopulates the dropdown\nafter `_load_threads` completes, preserving the current selection when\nthe agent is still a valid option (present in the reloaded threads or\nthe configured `/agents` list) and falling back to \"All agents\"\notherwise.\n- Added `_agent_filtered_threads()` — returns `self._threads` narrowed\nto `self._filter_agent`; used as the base for both the sync\n(`_update_filtered_list`) and async (`_filter_and_build`) filtering\npaths so the agent filter ANDs with the existing text filter.\n- Extended `on_select_changed` with a branch for the agent select:\nupdates `self._filter_agent` and triggers\n`_schedule_filter_and_rebuild()` (in-memory, no DB re-query).\n- Generalized the scope-select-only focus/expansion helpers\n(`_get_select`, `_expanded_select_id`, `_is_select_expanded`,\n`_close_expanded_select`, `_select_expanded_highlight`,\n`_open_focused_select`, `_restore_expanded_select_focus`) to drive both\nOptions-panel dropdowns.\n- Added the agent `Select` widget and its label to `compose()` beneath\nthe existing scope select, and updated `_filter_focus_order` to include\nit between the scope select and the sort switch.\n\nThe filter is **in-memory** (applied after `_load_threads`) rather than\npassed to `list_threads`, so no extra DB query is needed when the user\nchanges the agent selection.\n\n**`libs/code/tests/unit_tests/test_thread_selector.py`**\n\nAdded `TestThreadSelectorAgentFilter` covering the data-shaping helpers\n(`_collect_agent_options` union/sort/dedup with mixed-case names,\n`_agent_filtered_threads` including the `(unknown)` sentinel), the\ndropdown-driven `Select.Changed` path and its `_confirming_delete`\nguard, selection preservation vs. clearing across reloads, the\nconfigured-agent union surfacing in the rendered widget, focus\nrestoration across async loads, and that an unexpected agent-scan\nfailure does not strand the picker. A new autouse fixture isolates the\nsuite from the host's `~/.deepagents/` so the option set is\ndeterministic. Existing tab-order tests were updated for the agent\nselect inserted between the scope select and the sort switch.\n\n## How did you verify your code works?\n\nSeeded the local `sessions.db` with 5 threads across 3 agents\n(`my-agent`, `other-agent`, `coding-bot`) and opened `/threads` in the\nrunning TUI:\n\n```\n   Thread ID Agent       Msg Created Updated Branch    │ Options\n > threadabc my-agent    ... 1d ago  1d ago  main      │\n   threadabc my-agent    ... 2d ago  2d ago  main      │ Show threads from:\n   threaddef other-agent ... 3d ago  3d ago  main      │ Current directory  ▼\n   threaddef other-agent ... 4d ago  4d ago  main      │\n   threadghi coding-bot  ... 5d ago  5d ago  main      │ Show agent:\n                                                        │ All agents        ▼\n```\n\nThe \"Show agent:\" dropdown appeared with \"All agents\" as the default.\nFiltering to `my-agent` narrowed the list to 2 threads; selecting\n`coding-bot` showed 1. Switching back to \"All agents\" restored all 5.\n\nAll 170 unit tests pass (`uv run pytest\ntests/unit_tests/test_thread_selector.py`).\n<img width=\"1347\" height=\"288\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-05-31 at 2 31 09 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/79826ed7-d200-4517-b974-e4dce0ca3c98\"\n/>\n<img width=\"288\" height=\"372\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-05-31 at 2 40 23 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4800ee3c-4229-4c37-9a41-69fa25162624\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1097\" height=\"439\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/93baf260-265e-483b-a413-880098f9ca18\"\n/>\n\n> This contribution was developed with the assistance of generative AI.\n\n## Social handles (optional)\nLinkedIn: https://linkedin.com/in/ninaadrao\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-16T05:54:10Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f8193df41d7c47626d94252039217f4079d117cd","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f8193df41d7c47626d94252039217f4079d117cd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f8193df41d7c47626d94252039217f4079d117cd/comments","author":{"login":"NinaadRao","id":35262832,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MjYyODMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35262832?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NinaadRao","html_url":"https://github.com/NinaadRao","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NinaadRao/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NinaadRao/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NinaadRao/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NinaadRao/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NinaadRao/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NinaadRao/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NinaadRao/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NinaadRao/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NinaadRao/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"81acc2ecdada55a98e512f96b0caf8cb0f2c6d29","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/81acc2ecdada55a98e512f96b0caf8cb0f2c6d29","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/81acc2ecdada55a98e512f96b0caf8cb0f2c6d29"}]},{"sha":"81acc2ecdada55a98e512f96b0caf8cb0f2c6d29","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDgxYWNjMmVjZGFkYTU1YTk4ZTUxMmY5NmIwY2FmOGNiMGYyYzZkMjk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-16T02:31:28Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-16T02:31:28Z"},"message":"fix(code): guard against misconfigured LangSmith tracing (#3993)\n\nMisconfigured LangSmith tracing (a tracing flag enabled without\nresolvable credentials) no longer floods the terminal with repeated 401\nauthentication errors, while keyless self-hosted/proxied tracing setups\nremain supported.\n\n---\n\nLangChain enables tracing whenever a tracing flag\n(`LANGCHAIN_TRACING_V2`, `LANGSMITH_TRACING`, etc.) is truthy,\nregardless of whether credentials exist. With the flag set but no key —\na common leftover in a shell profile or stale `.env` — the background\ntracer keeps retrying ingestion and floods `langsmith.client` 401 errors\ninto the TUI, most visibly at the atexit flush.\n\nAt bootstrap we now:\n\n- **Route the `langsmith`/`langchain` SDK loggers off the terminal** —\nto the debug log when `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DEBUG` is set, otherwise a\n`NullHandler` — so their errors cannot leak onto the alternate-screen\nTUI via Python's last-resort stderr handler.\n- **Disable tracing before any traced run starts** when a tracing flag\nis on but no credentials resolve, avoiding wasted background ingestion\nwork and a slow/hanging atexit flush against the default hosted\nLangSmith endpoint.\n- **Resolve credentials from both env vars and LangSmith profiles.**\nCredentials include `LANGSMITH_API_KEY` / `LANGCHAIN_API_KEY`, plus the\nactive LangSmith profile's stored `api_key` or OAuth access/refresh\ntokens, so users who ran `langsmith auth login` are not falsely caught.\n- **Respect self-hosted / proxied setups from env vars or profiles.**\nTracing is left untouched when a custom endpoint is configured through\n`LANGSMITH_ENDPOINT` / `LANGCHAIN_ENDPOINT` or through the active\nLangSmith profile's `api_url`, because those deployments may\nintentionally support keyless ingestion.\n- **Surface a one-shot warning toast** explaining that tracing was\ndisabled and how to re-enable it: set `LANGSMITH_API_KEY`, or run\n`langsmith auth login` when that CLI is on `PATH`. The toast is\nbest-effort; the durable record is the `logger.warning` emitted at the\ndisable site.\n\nLangSmith profile resolution matches the SDK behavior:\n\n- If `LANGSMITH_CONFIG_FILE` is set, that exact config file is loaded.\n- Otherwise, LangSmith auto-detects `~/.langsmith/config.json`.\n- If `LANGSMITH_PROFILE` is set, that profile is used.\n- Otherwise, LangSmith uses `current_profile`, falling back to `default`\nwhen present.\n- Endpoint env vars are not auto-detected; if unset, LangSmith checks\nthe active profile's `api_url`, then falls back to\n`https://api.smith.langchain.com`.\n\nRegression coverage now verifies the profile-only custom endpoint case:\na config with only `api_url`, tracing enabled, no API key, and no\nendpoint env vars keeps tracing enabled and stages no orphaned-tracing\nnotice.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"7ca7ece694fe47a4f67e542efc3c21ddc111f955","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/7ca7ece694fe47a4f67e542efc3c21ddc111f955"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/81acc2ecdada55a98e512f96b0caf8cb0f2c6d29","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqMLWACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAT5kQADK5sz3FTyl8ewmf2rPGxzqT\nP2W4ZrLxPpN5qETk5j8d26xbWGMIZDG0LPwFrUz/QC70SE0/Y9DAsXQeQKNEzq5+\n4s/n1YTxUVXGTcwTQK23Runx0zXtefsqu9ct7b1p7qG12zxZzWSmFQ0freepqAPD\ny2nwsJe+U03Idn5SedKSArmFV/1Cuig8aY4B+6Q8DUofpNVYNWeD/820eiyNosQl\n/MX8iLJ30hrW99iYTM0dpvzvCaHN8usw/crenB/zt0UzhuNaV/dcBz1Kf/WUNjDt\n5CBYed8fMJHRF6D2aMumpq9Bfx6wNG5GAdf2m9xeIjtlVAB4JvJ7TtCC+79ugLhy\n3OyP5iZ4nbxZUT8DPJgvDbqHdigmrDAQuqJx7dF0xvC9U76SRmtOKZYRi5Q7GBC3\nD48oiCpXazE1IAzFlhjcJR5nPA1pGvyYCxqSHuC9023DeFbSc6REQnFJhgkvPIZP\n/7v98TyCD2z7+wH/0NedZJMFDRMcelOuXTOovGubyyugXnHB2fZDpB9i9ueF6S6J\nvUb8wJPrwXI5vfpM2xFal/a62A7i7vdl2fq5tClpdWyFCXd4ZylVFw/ys4DXW2bV\nd8QQuRaJnjlvpVA59DGOf5os0OZo/mFtguYhYYjtmYum6rzirY4uUkldDbeNbru6\nMNiqYUv8bKTyr753R20K\n=P0zr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7ca7ece694fe47a4f67e542efc3c21ddc111f955\nparent a5ec6dd0fec66ad321c1cc0f5e2f990c9026e03f\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1781577088 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781577088 -0400\n\nfix(code): guard against misconfigured LangSmith tracing (#3993)\n\nMisconfigured LangSmith tracing (a tracing flag enabled without\nresolvable credentials) no longer floods the terminal with repeated 401\nauthentication errors, while keyless self-hosted/proxied tracing setups\nremain supported.\n\n---\n\nLangChain enables tracing whenever a tracing flag\n(`LANGCHAIN_TRACING_V2`, `LANGSMITH_TRACING`, etc.) is truthy,\nregardless of whether credentials exist. With the flag set but no key —\na common leftover in a shell profile or stale `.env` — the background\ntracer keeps retrying ingestion and floods `langsmith.client` 401 errors\ninto the TUI, most visibly at the atexit flush.\n\nAt bootstrap we now:\n\n- **Route the `langsmith`/`langchain` SDK loggers off the terminal** —\nto the debug log when `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DEBUG` is set, otherwise a\n`NullHandler` — so their errors cannot leak onto the alternate-screen\nTUI via Python's last-resort stderr handler.\n- **Disable tracing before any traced run starts** when a tracing flag\nis on but no credentials resolve, avoiding wasted background ingestion\nwork and a slow/hanging atexit flush against the default hosted\nLangSmith endpoint.\n- **Resolve credentials from both env vars and LangSmith profiles.**\nCredentials include `LANGSMITH_API_KEY` / `LANGCHAIN_API_KEY`, plus the\nactive LangSmith profile's stored `api_key` or OAuth access/refresh\ntokens, so users who ran `langsmith auth login` are not falsely caught.\n- **Respect self-hosted / proxied setups from env vars or profiles.**\nTracing is left untouched when a custom endpoint is configured through\n`LANGSMITH_ENDPOINT` / `LANGCHAIN_ENDPOINT` or through the active\nLangSmith profile's `api_url`, because those deployments may\nintentionally support keyless ingestion.\n- **Surface a one-shot warning toast** explaining that tracing was\ndisabled and how to re-enable it: set `LANGSMITH_API_KEY`, or run\n`langsmith auth login` when that CLI is on `PATH`. The toast is\nbest-effort; the durable record is the `logger.warning` emitted at the\ndisable site.\n\nLangSmith profile resolution matches the SDK behavior:\n\n- If `LANGSMITH_CONFIG_FILE` is set, that exact config file is loaded.\n- Otherwise, LangSmith auto-detects `~/.langsmith/config.json`.\n- If `LANGSMITH_PROFILE` is set, that profile is used.\n- Otherwise, LangSmith uses `current_profile`, falling back to `default`\nwhen present.\n- Endpoint env vars are not auto-detected; if unset, LangSmith checks\nthe active profile's `api_url`, then falls back to\n`https://api.smith.langchain.com`.\n\nRegression coverage now verifies the profile-only custom endpoint case:\na config with only `api_url`, tracing enabled, no API key, and no\nendpoint env vars keeps tracing enabled and stages no orphaned-tracing\nnotice.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-16T02:31:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/81acc2ecdada55a98e512f96b0caf8cb0f2c6d29","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/81acc2ecdada55a98e512f96b0caf8cb0f2c6d29","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/81acc2ecdada55a98e512f96b0caf8cb0f2c6d29/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a5ec6dd0fec66ad321c1cc0f5e2f990c9026e03f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a5ec6dd0fec66ad321c1cc0f5e2f990c9026e03f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a5ec6dd0fec66ad321c1cc0f5e2f990c9026e03f"}]}]